COLLDATA("tayalisi","en",[[1,"\"No servant commits a sin, then performs wudu' and prays two rak'ahs, then asks Allah for forgiveness, except that He forgives him.\" Then he recited this verse: {And those who, when they commit an immorality or wrong themselves, remember Allah and seek forgiveness for their sins} [Al 'Imran: 135], and the other verse: {And whoever does evil or wrongs himself} [An-Nisa': 110]."],[2,"When I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, Allah benefited me through it as He willed. And when someone other than him narrated to me, I made him swear that he heard it from him, then I believed him. Abu Bakr narrated to me — and Abu Bakr ؓ spoke the truth — that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ... then he mentioned something similar to the hadith of Shu'bah."],[3,"\"Abu Bakr ؓ sent for me after the Battle of al-Yamamah, and 'Umar ibn al-Khattab ؓ was with him. He said: 'This man came to me and informed me that the killing has intensified among the Quran reciters in this place — meaning the Day of al-Yamamah — and I fear that the killing will intensify among the Quran reciters in other places, and so the Quran will be lost. I have decided that you should compile it.' I said to him — meaning to 'Umar —: 'How can we do something the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not do?' 'Umar said to me: 'By Allah, it is good.' 'Umar kept persuading me until Allah opened my chest to what He had opened his chest, and I saw in it what he saw. You are a sensible man, you used to write down the revelation for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and we do not accuse you, so compile it.'\""],[4,"\"I was with Abu Bakr ؓ while he was threatening a man and spoke harshly to him. I said: 'Shall I strike his neck?' Abu Bakr said: 'No one has that right after the Prophet ﷺ.'\""],[5,"I heard Abu Bakr ؓ delivering a sermon. He mentioned the Prophet ﷺ and wept, then said — meaning the Prophet ﷺ —: 'You must be truthful, for truthfulness leads to righteousness, and both are in Paradise. Beware of lying, for lying leads to wickedness, and both are in the Fire. Ask Allah for certainty and well-being, for people have not been given anything after certainty better than well-being' — or he said 'forgiveness' — 'Do not envy one another, do not hate one another, do not cut off relations with one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and be, O servants of Allah, brothers.'"],[6,"Abu Bakr ؓ, when he mentioned the Day of Uhud, wept and then said: 'That entire day belonged to Talhah.' Then he began to narrate, saying: 'I was the first to return on the Day of Uhud. I saw a man fighting alongside the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, protecting him — and I think he said: defending him. I said: \"Be Talhah, since I missed what I missed.\" I said: \"If only he were a man from my people, that would be dearer to me.\" Between me and the east there was a man I did not recognize, and I was closer to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ than he, but he was moving swiftly in a way I could not. Then I saw it was Abu 'Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah. We reached the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; his front tooth had been broken, his face had been wounded, and two rings of the helmet had pierced his cheeks. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Take care of your companion,\" meaning Talhah. But he did not pay attention to his words, and I went to remove that from his face. Abu 'Ubaydah said: \"I adjure you by my right to leave me.\" So I left him. He disliked touching them with his hand, lest he hurt the Prophet ﷺ. He bit down on them with his mouth and extracted one of the rings, and his front tooth fell with the ring. I went to do what he had done, but he said: \"I adjure you by my right to leave me.\" He did the same as the first time, and his other front tooth fell with the ring. Abu 'Ubaydah was among the most handsome of people with broken teeth. We attended to the Prophet ﷺ, then we went to Talhah in one of those pits. There he was, with seventy-some wounds — or fewer or more — between stabs, arrows, and strikes, and his finger had been cut off. So we attended to him.'"],[7,"\"The first person to knock on the door of Paradise is a servant who fulfills the right of Allah and the rights of his masters.\""],[8,"\"Neither a deceitful person nor a traitor will enter Paradise.\""],[9,"O Messenger of Allah, command me with something I can say in the morning and the evening. He said: 'Say: O Allah, Knower of the unseen and the seen, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Lord and Owner of everything, I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul and from the evil of Satan and his trap. Say it in the morning, in the evening, and when you go to bed.'"],[10,"'Umar ibn al-Khattab ؓ asked the Prophet ﷺ for permission to perform 'umrah. He gave him permission and said to him: \"O my brother, include us in your supplication\" or \"do not forget us in your supplication.\""],[11,"'Umar said: 'O Messenger of Allah, tell me about what we do — is it a new matter, or something already decreed?' He said: 'It is something already decreed. So act, O Ibn al-Khattab, for everyone is facilitated. Whoever is among the people of happiness, he will act for happiness. Whoever is among the people of misery, he will act for misery.'"],[12,"\"Whoever enters any of these markets and says: 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner. His is the dominion, and His is the praise. He gives life and causes death, and He is Ever-Living and does not die. In His hand is all good, and He has power over all things,' Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will record for him a thousand thousand good deeds, erase from him a thousand thousand bad deeds, and build for him a palace in Paradise.\""],[13,"\"There is no man who sees someone afflicted and says: 'Praise be to Allah who has spared me from what He has afflicted him with, and has favored me over many of those He created with a great favor,' but that affliction will not strike him, whatever it may be.\""],[14,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ wiping over the leather socks.\""],[15,"\"Indeed, the deceased is punished in his grave because of the wailing over him.\""],[16,"I asked Ibn 'Umar ؓ about nabidh, and he narrated from 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade jars, gourds, and pitch-covered vessels."],[17,"O Messenger of Allah, I am affected by janabah at night, so what should I do? He said: \"Wash your private part, perform wudu', then sleep.\""],[18,"That 'Umar saw a striped silk robe of 'Utarid al-Tamimi being sold, so 'Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, buy this robe and wear it on Friday and for delegations when they come to you. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Only one who has no share in the Hereafter wears this.\" Then afterwards the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought robes of that kind, and he sent 'Umar one of them. 'Umar came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, you sent me a robe today, while you said about the robe of 'Utarid what you said. He said: \"You may sell it or clothe your women with it.\""],[19,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came upon 'Umar ؓ while he was swearing by his father, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called out to him: \"Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, forbids you to swear by your fathers. Whoever swears, let him swear by Allah or be silent.\""],[20,"I asked Ibn 'Umar about a man who divorced his wife while she was menstruating. He said: \"Do you know Ibn 'Umar? He divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so 'Umar mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'He should take her back.'\""],[21,"That he was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when a man came to him wearing two white garments, upright, handsome in stature and appearance, and said: \"May I draw near to you, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Draw near.\" Then he said: \"May I draw near to you, O Messenger of Allah?\" He said: \"Draw near.\" He kept drawing near until his knee was at the knee of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then he said: \"May I ask you?\" He said: \"Ask.\" He said: \"Tell me about Islam.\" He said: \"The testimony that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, the establishment of prayer, the giving of zakat, the pilgrimage to the House, and the fast of Ramadan.\" He said: \"If I do that, then I am a Muslim?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Yes.\" The man said to him: \"You have spoken the truth.\" We began to wonder at his saying to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"You have spoken the truth,\" as if he knew more than him. Then he said: \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me about faith (iman).\" He said: \"Faith is to believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, the resurrection after death, Paradise, and Hell, and to believe in the divine decree, its good and its evil.\" He said: \"If I do that, then I am a believer?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"You have spoken the truth.\" We began to wonder at his saying to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, \"You have spoken the truth.\" Then he said: \"Tell me what is ihsan.\" He said: \"To fear Allah as if you see Him; for if you do not see Him, He sees you.\" He said: \"You have spoken the truth.\" Then he said: \"Tell me about the Hour.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"The one questioned about it is no more knowledgeable than the questioner. They are five things that no one knows except Allah: Indeed, Allah has knowledge of the Hour, and He sends down the rain...\" the verse. The man said: \"You have spoken the truth.\""],[22,"\"There is no man who dies and three people testify good of him but Paradise becomes incumbent for him.\" I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, and two?\" He said: \"And two.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was not asked about one."],[23,"We set out with 'Umar ؓ until we reached Marr al-Zahran. 'Umar went into the arak trees to relieve himself, and I waited for him until he came out. I said: \"O Commander of the Faithful, I have wanted to ask you about something for a year, but your awe prevented me from asking you.\" He said: \"Do not do that. If you know that I have knowledge, then ask me.\" I said: \"I ask you about the matter of the two women.\" He said: \"Yes, Hafsah and 'A'ishah. In the time of ignorance we did not consider women of any account, and we did not include them in any of our affairs. When Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, brought Islam and sent down about them what He sent down, and gave them a right without including them in any of our affairs, then one day while I was sitting concerning some of my affairs, my wife said to me such and such. I said: 'What is it to you and this? When have you ever entered into our affairs?' She said: 'O Ibn al-Khattab, no one can speak to you, but your daughter speaks to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he remains angry all day.' I said: 'And she does that?' She said: 'Yes.' So I got up and entered upon Hafsah, and I said: 'O Hafsah, do you not fear Allah? You speak to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ until he remains angry all day. Woe to you, do not be deceived by the beauty of 'A'ishah and the love of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for her.' Then I also went to Umm Salamah and said the same to her. She said: 'O Ibn al-Khattab, you have entered into everything, even between the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and his wives.' I had a companion from the Ansar who would attend the Messenger of Allah ﷺ when I was absent, and I would attend when he was absent, and he would inform me and I would inform him. We feared most of all that a king of the kings of Ghassan would attack us. When Allah calmed the matter for us, one day while I was sitting concerning some of my affairs, my companion came and said: 'Abu Hafs! Abu Hafs!' twice. I said: 'Woe to you, what is the matter? Has the Ghassanid come? Has the Ghassanid come?' He said: 'No, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ has divorced his wives.' I said: 'May Hafsah's nose be rubbed in the dust, may Hafsah's nose be rubbed in the dust.' I put on my sandals and went to the Prophet ﷺ. There was weeping in every room, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was in an upper room, and at the door was a black slave. I said: 'Ask permission for me to see the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' He asked permission, and he admitted me. There he was, sleeping on a mat, with a leather pillow stuffed with palm fiber under his head, and there were acacia pods and tanned hides hanging. I began to tell him what I had said to Hafsah and Umm Salamah. He had sworn to stay away from his wives for a month. When it was the night of the twenty-ninth, he came down to them."],[24,"\"Do not extol me as the Christians extolled 'Isa b. Maryam. I am only a servant, so say: 'The servant of Allah and His Messenger.'\""],[25,"Ibn ʿAbbās ؓ addressed us from the pulpit of Baṣra and said: O people, ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ stood among us and said: O people, indeed stoning is one of the limits set by God, so do not be deceived away from it. It is in the Book of God and the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ stoned, Abu Bakr stoned, and I stoned."],[26,"I was the first of the people to come to ʿUmar ؓ when he was stabbed. He said: O Abu ʿAbbās, preserve from me three things, for I fear that people will not reach me [in time]. I have not ruled on kalāla, I have not appointed a successor over the people, and every slave I own is free. It was said to him: Appoint a successor. He said: Whichever of those I do, one better than me has done it. If I appoint a successor, one better than me appointed a successor, and if I leave the people to their own affair, the Messenger of God ﷺ left it. I said: Rejoice in Paradise, O Commander of the Faithful. You accompanied the Messenger of God ﷺ and prolonged his company, then you took charge and were just, and you delivered the trust. ʿUmar ؓ said: As for your giving me glad tidings of Paradise, by God besides whom there is no deity, if I had all that is between heaven and earth I would ransom myself with it from what is ahead of me before I learn the outcome. As for what you mentioned about the affair of the Muslims, by God I wish I had been delivered from it with neither liability nor credit. As for what you mentioned about the company of the Messenger of God ﷺ, that is so."],[27,"He performed ṭawāf and wanted not to do ramal. He said: The Prophet ﷺ only did ramal to anger the polytheists. Then he said: It is a matter the Messenger of God ﷺ did and did not forbid, so he did ramal."],[28,"I saw Muḥammad b. ʿAbbād b. Jaʿfar kiss the Stone and prostrate upon it. Then he said: I saw your maternal uncle Ibn ʿAbbās kiss it and prostrate upon it. Ibn ʿAbbās said: I saw ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb kiss it and prostrate upon it. Then ʿUmar said: Had I not seen the Messenger of God ﷺ kiss it, I would not have kissed it."],[29,"Men of good standing testified before me, among them ʿUmar, and the most pleasing of them to me was ʿUmar, that the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade prayer after ʿAṣr until the sun sets, and prayer after Ṣubḥ until the sun rises."],[30,"I entered the mosque while the Messenger of God ﷺ was delivering a sermon. ʿUmar said to me: The Messenger of God ﷺ said before you came: Whoever dies believing in God and the Last Day, it will be said to him: Enter Paradise from whichever of the eight gates of Paradise you wish."],[31,"ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ addressed us at al-Jābiya and said: The Messenger of God ﷺ stood among us as I stand among you and said: Honor my Companions, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then lying will spread until a man swears without being asked to swear, and bears witness without being asked to bear witness. Whoever wants the midst of Paradise should keep to the community, for Satan is with the solitary person and is farther from two. Let no man be alone with a woman, for the third of them is Satan. Whoever is pleased by his good deed and grieved by his evil deed is a believer."],[32,"I came to Madinah in the season of dried curd and ghee, when the Bedouins were bringing al-burqān and selling them. I saw a man with raised gaze looking at the people, and I thought he was a stranger. I approached him, greeted him, and he returned my greeting and said to me: Are you from the people of this place? I said: Yes. I sat with him and said: From whom are you? He said: From Hilāl, and my name is Kahmas – or he said: From Banu Sulūl, and my name is Kahmas. Then he said to me: Shall I not tell you a hadith I witnessed from ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb? I said: Certainly. He said: While we were sitting with him, a woman came and sat before him and said: O Commander of the Faithful, my husband's evil has increased and his good has decreased. ʿUmar ؓ said to her: Who is your husband? She said: Abu Salama. He said: That man is a man of companionship, and he is a truthful man. Then ʿUmar said to a man sitting near him: Is it not so? He said: O Commander of the Faithful, we know him only as you said. Then ʿUmar said to a man: Arise and summon him for me. The woman rose when he sent for her husband and sat behind ʿUmar. It was not long before they came together and sat in front of ʿUmar. ʿUmar said: What do you say about this woman sitting behind me? He said: Who is she, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: This is your wife. He said: And what does she say? He said: She claims that your good has decreased and your evil has increased. He said: What an evil thing she has said, O Commander of the Faithful. She is among the best of her women, the most clothed and most comfortable, but her stallion is stingy. ʿUmar said: What do you say? She said: You are right. ʿUmar rose to her with the whip and struck her with it. Then he said: O enemy of herself, you have eaten his wealth and exhausted his youth, and then you set about informing of what is not in him. She said: O Commander of the Faithful, do not be hasty. By God, I will never sit in this gathering again. Then he ordered three garments for her and said: Take this for what I did to you, and beware of complaining about this old man. It is as if I see her rising with the garments. Then he turned to her husband and said: Do not let what you saw me do to her make you mistreat her. Go away. The man said: I would never do that. Then ʿUmar said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: The best of my community is the generation in which I am, then the second, then the third. Then a people will arise whose oaths precede their testimony, testifying without being asked to testify. They will have clamor in their markets. He said: Kahmas said to me: Do you fear that these might be among those? Then Kahmas said to me: I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him of my Islam. Then I was absent from him for a year. Then I came to him and said: O Messenger of God, it is as if you do not recognize me? He said: Indeed. I said: O Messenger of God, I have not broken fast since I parted from you. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: Who commanded you to torment yourself? Fast one day a month. I said: Give me more. He said: Fast two days, until he said: Fast three days of the month."],[33,"When ʿUmar was stabbed, Ṣuhayb said: O his brother, O his brother. ʿUmar said to him: Stop, O my brother; stop, O Ṣuhayb. Have you not heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: The deceased is punished in his grave by the weeping of his family?"],[34,"I saw ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb kissing the Stone and saying: I kiss you, and I know that you are a stone, but I saw Abu al-Qāsim ﷺ kind to you."],[35,"I prayed two rakʿahs with the Messenger of God ﷺ at Dhu al-Ḥulayfa."],[36,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ and with him was a group of people. A man came to him and said: O Messenger of God, which of the people has the best station with God on the Day of Resurrection after His prophets and His chosen ones? He said: The one who strives in the path of God with his self and his wealth until the call of God comes to him while he is on the back of his horse, holding its reins. He said: Then who? He said: A man in a remote corner who worships his Lord well and leaves the people safe from his evil. He said: O Messenger of God, which of the people has the worst station with God on the Day of Resurrection? He said: The polytheist. He said: Then who? He said: A tyrannical ruler who deviates from the truth and has been given power. The Messenger of God ﷺ singled out the doors of the unseen and said: Ask me, and you will not ask me about anything except that I will inform you of it. ʿUmar said: We are content with God as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with you as Prophet. Enough for us is what has come to us. He said: Then it was relieved from him."],[37,"\"O people, actions are only by intention, and each person will have only what he intended. Whoever's migration was to Allah and His Messenger, his migration is to Allah and His Messenger. And whoever's migration was for a worldly gain to attain or a woman to marry, his migration is to what he migrated for.\""],[38,"We met Umar and said to him: \"Abd Allah b. Amr narrated to us such and such.\" Umar said: \"Abd Allah b. Amr knows best what he says.\" He said it three times. Then the call for the congregational prayer was given, and the people gathered to him. Umar addressed them, saying: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'A group from my ummah will continue to uphold the truth until the command of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, comes.'\""],[39,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me a surah from the Quran, and I memorized it and comprehended it. While I was standing in the mosque praying, Hisham b. Hakim was praying beside me. He began reciting that surah in a different reading than the one the Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me. I wanted to grab him during the prayer, but I restrained myself until he finished. Then I took hold of his garment and said: \"Who taught you this verse?\" He said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught it to me.\" I said: \"You lie. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught it to me in a different reading.\" So I dragged him away. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw me, he said to me: \"O Umar, let him go.\" I released his garment and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, you taught me a surah from the Quran, and he recites it differently from what you taught me.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Recite, O Hisham.\" He recited, and the Prophet said: \"Thus it was revealed.\" Then he said to me: \"Recite, O Umar.\" I recited, and he said: \"Thus it was revealed. The Quran was revealed in seven ahruf, so recite whatever is easy from it.\""],[40,"We looked for the new moon, and no one among the people claimed to have seen it except me. I said to Umar: \"O Commander of the Believers, do you not see it?\" I kept pointing it out to him. When he was unable to see it, he said: \"I will see it while lying on my bed.\" Then he began narrating to us about the Day of Badr, saying: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was telling us yesterday about the places where the people would fall: 'This is where so-and-so will fall, if Allah wills, tomorrow; this is where so-and-so will fall, if Allah wills, tomorrow.' By the One who sent him with the truth, they did not miss those spots, and they were made to fall on them. Then they were thrown into the well. The Prophet ﷺ came and said: 'O so-and-so, son of so-and-so, have you found what your Lord promised you to be true? For I have found what my Lord promised me to be true.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, do you speak to bodies without souls?' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'By the One in whose hand is my soul, you are not more able to hear than them, but they cannot respond to me.'\""],[41,"\"I agreed with my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, in four matters. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, if only you prayed behind the Maqam,' and this verse was revealed: 'And take the Maqam of Ibrahim as a place of prayer.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, if only you ordered your wives to veil, for both the righteous and the wicked enter upon you.' So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: 'And when you ask them for something, ask them from behind a screen.' And this verse was revealed: 'We certainly created man from an extract of clay' until the end of the verse. When it was revealed, I said: 'Blessed is Allah, the best of creators.' Then it was revealed: 'So blessed is Allah, the best of creators.' And I entered upon the wives of the Prophet ﷺ and said to them: 'Either you desist, or Allah will replace you with better wives than you.' So this verse was revealed: 'Perhaps his Lord, if he divorces you...'\""],[42,"When Umar ؓ was stabbed, Hafsah wailed over him. Umar said: \"Did you not hear the Prophet ﷺ say: 'The one who is wailed over is punished'?\""],[43,"Do not clothe your women in silk, for I heard Umar ؓ say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter.\""],[44,"A hare was brought to Umar ؓ. He said: \"Were it not for the fear of adding or omitting, I would narrate to you the hadith of the bedouin when he brought a hare to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He mentioned that he saw blood on it, so he ordered them to eat it, and he said to the bedouin: 'Come close and eat.' The bedouin said: 'I am fasting.' The Prophet said: 'Which fast are you observing?' He said: 'From the beginning of the month and its end.' The Prophet said: 'If you are fasting, then fast the white nights: the thirteenth, fourteenth, and fifteenth. But send for Ammar.' So they sent for him, and he came. Umar said: 'Are you a witness that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought a hare by the bedouin, and he said: \"I saw it bleeding\"?' Ammar said: 'Yes.'\""],[45,"\"The martyrs are four: a believer with excellent faith who meets the enemy, is true to Allah, and fights until he is killed. That is the one to whom people raise their eyes—he raised his head until a cap that was on his head, or on Umar's head, fell—this one is in the first degree. And a man, a believer with excellent faith, who when he meets the enemy feels as if his skin is being struck by the thorns of a talh tree out of cowardice; a stray arrow comes and kills him. This one is in the second degree. And a believing man who mixed a righteous deed with another evil one; he meets the enemy and is true to Allah until he is killed. This one is in the third degree. And a man who transgressed against himself; he meets the enemy and fights until he is killed. This one is in the fourth degree.\""],[46,"He donated a horse in the path of Allah, then he saw that its owner had neglected it and wanted to sell it. He asked the Prophet ﷺ whether he should buy it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Do not buy it, even if it were for a dirham. The example of the one who returns to his charity is like the dog that returns to its vomit.\""],[47,"I was a guest of Umar b. al-Khattab. He said: \"O Ash'ath, memorize from me three things that I memorized from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Do not ask a man why he beat his wife, and do not sleep except after performing the witr prayer.\" And I forgot the third."],[48,"\"The prayer of travel is two rak'ahs, the night prayer is two rak'ahs, and the Friday prayer is two rak'ahs, complete not shortened,\" on the tongue of the Prophet ﷺ."],[49,"O Commander of the Believers, we have come to ask you about three matters: what is lawful for a man from his wife while she is menstruating; about the ghusl from janaba; and about reciting the Qur'an in houses? 'Umar said: 'Glory be to God! Are you sorcerers? You have asked me about something I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about, which no one has asked me about since.' He said: 'As for what is lawful for a man from his wife while she is menstruating, it is what is above the waist wrapper. As for the ghusl from janaba, he should wash his hand and his private part, then perform wudu, and pour water over his head and body. As for reciting the Qur'an, it is light, so whoever wishes may illuminate his house.'"],[50,"I saw 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ kiss the Stone, then say: 'I kiss you, and I know that you are a stone. Were it not that I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ kiss you, I would not kiss you.'"],[51,"\"If you were to rely on God with true reliance, He would provide for you as He provides for the birds: they go out hungry in the morning and return full in the evening.\""],[52,"While 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ was giving the Friday sermon, a man came. 'Umar said: 'Why do you hold back from the Friday prayer?' He said: 'O Commander of the Believers, it was only that I heard the call, performed wudu, and then came.' He said: 'And wudu as well? Have you not heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"When one of you sets out for Friday prayer, let him perform ghusl\"?'"],[53,"'Umar ؓ gave the Friday sermon and mentioned the Prophet ﷺ and Abu Bakr, then said: 'I saw in a dream as if a rooster pecked me once or twice, and I think it is only for the approach of my term. Some people are asking me to appoint a successor, but God, Mighty and Majestic, will not neglect His religion or His caliphate. By the One who sent His Prophet ﷺ, if something hastens me, the caliphate is among these six men who parted from the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was pleased with them. I will not leave after me anything more important to me than al-kalala, and I have not argued with the Messenger of God ﷺ since I accompanied him about anything as I argued about al-kalala, and he was not harsh with me about anything since I accompanied him as he was harsh with me about al-kalala, until he struck my chest with his hand and said: \"O 'Umar, the verse of summer that was revealed at the end of Surat al-Nisa' suffices you.\" Then, O people, you eat from two plants that I think are nothing but foul: this onion and garlic. I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ, when he found their smell on a man, order him to be taken out to al-Baqi'. So whoever of you must eat them, let him kill them by cooking.'"],[54,"\"Now, whoever is wronged by his governor, let him bring that to me and I will exact retribution for him.\" 'Amr b. al-'As stood and said: 'O Commander of the Believers, if a man disciplines a man from his subjects, will you exact retribution from him?' He said: 'How could I not exact retribution from him when I have seen the Messenger of God ﷺ exact retribution from himself?'"],[55,"\"Whoever monopolizes the food of the Muslims, God will afflict him with leprosy,\" or he said: \"with bankruptcy.\""],[56,"We used to recite among what we recited: (Do not turn away from your fathers, for that is disbelief on your part)."],[57,"I heard 'Umar b. al-Khattab giving a sermon, and he mentioned what had been conquered for the people. He said: 'I have seen the Messenger of God ﷺ twist with hunger all day, not finding even low-quality dates to fill his belly.'"],[58,"He entered ihram for Hajj and 'Umrah together. That was mentioned to 'Umar, and he said: 'You have been guided to the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ.'"],[59,"Al-Subayy b. Ma'bad was a Christian Taghlibi bedouin who embraced Islam. He asked: 'Which deeds are best?' It was said to him: 'Jihad in the path of God.' He wanted to go on jihad, but it was said to him: 'Have you performed Hajj?' He said: 'No.' It was said: 'Perform Hajj and 'Umrah, then go on jihad.' He set out until he reached al-Hawa'it, where he entered ihram for both together. Zayd b. Suhan and Salman b. Rabi'a saw him and said: 'He is more astray than his camel'—or 'he is no more guided than his she-camel.' He went to 'Umar and told him what they said. 'Umar said: 'You have been guided to the Sunnah of your Prophet Muhammad ﷺ.'"],[60,"\"There are three things that the Messenger of God ﷺ clarified that are dearer to me than red camels: the caliphate, al-kalala, and riba.\""],[61,"I heard a hadith from a man and it impressed me, and I desired to write it down. I said: 'Write it for me.' He brought it to me written in a clear script. He said: Al-'Abbas and 'Ali entered upon 'Umar ؓ while they were disputing. He said: With 'Umar were Talhah, al-Zubayr, Sa'd, and 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf ؓ. 'Umar said to them: 'I adjure you by Allah, did you not know, or did you not hear, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed all the property of the Prophet ﷺ is charity, except what he fed his family or clothed them. Indeed we are not inherited from.\"?' They said: 'Yes, indeed.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to spend from his property on his family and give the surplus as charity."],[62,"\"Touch them, for knees have been prescribed for you.\""],[63,"I witnessed 'Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ at Jam' after he had prayed the dawn prayer. He stood and said: 'The polytheists used not to depart until the sun rose, and they would say: \"Shine, Thabir!\" But the Messenger of Allah ﷺ differed from them, so 'Umar departed before sunrise.'"],[64,"\"Beware! Do not be excessive in the dowries of women, for if it were a source of honor in this world and piety before Allah, the most deserving of it among you would be Muhammad ﷺ. He did not marry off any of his daughters, nor did he marry any of his wives, for more than twelve uqiyyah. One of you would be excessive in a woman's dowry until it becomes a ransom for her, and then he says: 'I have burdened myself for you with the hanging of the water-skin,'\" or he said: \"the sweat of the water-skin.\""],[65,"\"Whoever visits my grave\" – or he said: \"Whoever visits me\" – \"I will be an intercessor for him\" – or \"a witness\" – \"and whoever dies in one of the two sacred precincts, Allah will raise him among the secure on the Day of Resurrection.\""],[66,"I arrived in Madinah and entered upon 'Umar when he had been stabbed. He said: 'I enjoin you to treat the people of the covenant well, for they are the covenant of your Prophet ﷺ.'"],[67,"If we follow the Book of Allah, the Exalted, then Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has commanded completion. If we follow the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then the Messenger of Allah did not exit the state of ihram until the sacrificial animal reached its place of sacrifice."],[68,"\"He divorced his wife while she was menstruating. 'Umar went to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he counted it as one divorce.\""],[69,"O Messenger of Allah, I had made a vow during the Jahiliyyah to observe i'tikaf for one night. What do you say? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Observe i'tikaf and fast.'"],[70,"O people, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ built this mosque while we were with him, along with the Muhajirun and the Ansar. When crowding becomes severe, let one of you prostrate on the back of his brother."],[72,"We were with 'Uthman b. 'Affan ؓ in the house while he was besieged. We would enter through an entrance from which we could hear the words of those in the courtyard. 'Uthman ؓ entered, then came out with his color changed. It was said: 'O Commander of the Believers, what is the matter with you?' He said: 'They are threatening to kill me just now, and I was not certain of that from them until today.' We said: 'May Allah suffice you against them, O Commander of the Believers.' He said: 'And for what would they kill me? I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except for one of three reasons: a man who disbelieves after his Islam, or commits adultery after being married, or kills a person without justification.\" By Allah, I have never committed adultery in the Jahiliyyah or in Islam, I have never desired a substitute for my religion since Allah, Mighty and Majestic, guided me, and I have never killed a person. So why do these people want to kill me?'"],[73,"\"The best of you is the one who learns the Quran and teaches it.\""],[74,"One in ihram may neither marry nor give a marriage proposal."],[75,"Whoever completes wudu as Allah has commanded him, the prayers become expiations for what is between them."],[76,"Uthman b. 'Affan ؓ was brought water for wudu for the 'Asr prayer while he was at al-Maqa'id. Uthman said: I have decided to tell you a hadith that I did not think I would tell you. Al-Hakam b. Abi al-'As said: O Commander of the Faithful, it is only good that we should follow, or evil that we should avoid. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought water for wudu while he was at al-Maqa'id. He said: Whoever performs wudu and perfects his wudu, then prays and completes its bowing and prostration, will have expiated for him what is between it and the next prayer as long as he does not commit a mortal sin, meaning as long as he does not commit a major sin."],[77,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought water for wudu while he was at al-Maqa'id for the 'Asr prayer. He said: When a Muslim performs wudu and perfects his wudu, then performs the prayers—Hammad said: I think he said: in congregation—and completes their bowing and prostration, Allah forgives him what is between them as long as he does not commit a mortal sin."],[78,"A man was easygoing as a judge and as one seeking repayment, and as a seller and as a buyer, and he entered Paradise."],[79,"There is no servant who says every morning or every evening: In the name of Allah with whose name nothing on earth or in heaven can cause harm, and He is the All-Hearing, the All-Knowing—but that nothing will harm him."],[80,"By Allah, what prevents me from relating from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ is not that I am not the most retentive of them for his hadith, but I testify that I heard him say: Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[81,"He performed wudu three times three times, and said: This is how the Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed wudu."],[82,"I heard Uthman ؓ say to Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas, Ali, al-Zubayr, and Talha ؓ: I adjure you by Allah, do you not know that the Prophet ﷺ said: Whoever equips the army of hardship, Allah will forgive him, and I equipped them until they were not missing a halter or a hobble? They said: O Allah, yes."],[83,"Everything besides the husk of this food, fresh water, and a house that shelters him is surplus, and the son of Adam has no merit in it."],[84,"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, created one hundred and seventeen qualities. Whoever meets Allah with one of them enters Paradise."],[85,"If a person in ihram has sore eyes, he should drip aloe juice into them."],[86,"My family married me to a Byzantine slave girl of theirs, and she bore me a black boy like me, so I named him 'Abd Allah. Then I had intercourse with her and she bore me another black boy like me, so I named him 'Ubayd Allah. Then a Byzantine slave of ours called Yuhannis became attached to her and had intercourse with her, and she became pregnant and bore a boy like a gecko among geckos. I said, \"What is this?\" She said, \"No, by Allah, this is not from you; this is from Yuhannis.\" He said, \"You have spoken the truth.\" They brought their dispute to 'Uthman and both confessed. 'Uthman said, \"Would you both be pleased that I judge between you with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ? The Messenger of Allah ﷺ judged that the child belongs to the bed, and the fornicator gets the stone. He is your son; you inherit from him and he inherits from you.\" I said, \"Glory be to Allah!\" He said, \"That is it.\" So I used to put him to sleep between the two of them: these two are black and this one is white."],[87,"'Uthman b. 'Affan ؓ said in the mosque of al-Khayf: \"O people, a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ I used to conceal from you out of concern for you. It has now appeared to me that I should disclose it as sincere advice to you. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'A day of the mujahid in the path of Allah is like a thousand days besides it.' So let every man among you look to himself.\""],[88,"\"The pilgrim in ihram may not marry or propose marriage.\""],[89,"\"The witr is not obligatory, but it is a good sunna from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Indeed, Allah is odd and loves the odd, so perform witr, O people of the Qur'an.\""],[90,"\"Obedience is only in what is good.\""],[91,"\"The pen is lifted from three: from the afflicted—or he said: the insane—until he recovers, from the child until he reaches puberty or understands, and from the sleeper until he wakes.\""],[92,"We asked 'Ali: \"Do you have anything of revelation besides what is in the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic?\" He said: \"No, by the One who split the grain and created the soul, I do not know of anything except understanding that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, gives a man in the Book of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, or what is in this sheet.\" He said: I said, \"What is in it?\" He said: \"The blood money, the ransom of the captive, and a Muslim is not killed for an idolater.\""],[93,"I asked 'A'isha about wiping over the leather socks. She said, \"Ask 'Ali, for he used to travel with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\" So I asked him, and he said: \"For the traveler three days and their nights, and for the resident one day and one night.\""],[94,"Fatima ؓ complained about what she suffered from the marks of the millstone on her hand. Some captives were brought to the Prophet ﷺ, so she went but did not find him. She met 'A'isha ؓ and told her. When the Prophet ﷺ came, 'A'isha told him about Fatima's coming to him. The Prophet ﷺ came when we had already taken to our beds, and we got up to rise, but the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"Stay where you are.\" He sat between us until I felt the coolness of his feet on my chest. Then he said, \"Shall I not teach you something better than what you asked for? When you take to your beds, say Allahu akbar thirty-four times, say subhan Allah thirty-three times, and say al-hamdu lillah thirty-three times. That is better for you than a servant.\""],[95,"On the day of the Confederates, he was at one of the openings of the trench and said: \"They kept us from the middle prayer until the sun set. May Allah fill their graves and their houses with fire,\" or \"their graves and their bellies with fire.\""],[96,"I witnessed 'Uthman and 'Ali ؓ between Makkah and Madinah while 'Uthman was forbidding tamattu' or combining the two. When 'Ali saw that, he entered ihram for both together and said, \"Labbayk for an 'umra and a hajj together.\" 'Uthman said, \"Do you see me forbidding the people something while you do it?\" He said, \"I would not abandon the sunna of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ for the saying of any person.\""],[97,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was at a funeral and said, \"Which of you will go to Madinah and not leave there any idol but break it, any image but deface it, and any grave but level it?\" A man from the group stood and said, \"I will, O Messenger of Allah.\" The man set out but seemed to be afraid of the people of Madinah and returned. Then 'Ali ؓ set out and returned, saying, \"I did not come back to you, O Messenger of Allah, until I had left no idol but I broke it, no grave but I leveled it, and no image but I defaced it.\" The Prophet ﷺ said, \"Whoever returns to making any of these,\" and he said concerning him a severe word. And he said to 'Ali, \"Do not be a troublemaker, nor arrogant, nor a merchant—except a merchant of good, for those are the ones outstripped in deeds.\""],[98,"The Prophet ﷺ forbade [an animal] with a slit ear or a broken horn [for sacrifice]."],[99,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade that an animal with a slit ear or a broken horn be offered as a sacrifice."],[100,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Yemen, I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, you have sent me while I am a young man with little knowledge of many judicial matters.' He said, 'Then he struck his hand on my chest and said, \"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will surely make firm your tongue and guide your heart.\"' So no judgment between two parties ever proved too difficult for me."],[101,"When I relate to you a hadith from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, then think of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as the most serene, most guided, and most God-fearing."],[102,"'Ali and 'Uthman ؓ met at 'Usfan. 'Uthman was forbidding mut'ah, so 'Ali said, 'What do you want with something the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did—you forbid it?' 'Uthman said, 'Leave us alone.' 'Ali said, 'I cannot leave you alone.' When 'Uthman saw that, he entered ihram for both together."],[103,"I entered upon 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ with two men—one from us and one from Banu Asad, I think. He sent the two of them on a mission and said, 'You are two sturdy fellows, so act stoutly in your religion.' Then he went to the privy, came out, took a handful of water and wiped with it, and began reciting the Qur'an. He saw that we found that strange, so he said, 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would enter the privy, relieve himself, then come out and eat meat with us and recite the Qur'an, and nothing would prevent him—perhaps he said, \"and nothing would hold him back\"—from the Qur'an except major ritual impurity (janabah).'"],[104,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never joined both his parents for anyone except Sa'd, for he said to him on the day of Uhud, 'Shoot, Sa'd, may my father and mother be your ransom.'"],[105,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade me to recite the Qur'an while bowing, to wear saffron-dyed garments, and to wear a gold ring."],[106,"I felt too shy to ask the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about madhy because of Fatimah, so I ordered a man to ask him. He said, 'It requires wudu'.'"],[107,"When I relate to you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, falling from the sky is dearer to me than saying about the Messenger of Allah ﷺ what he did not say. But when I speak to you from my own opinion, then war is deception."],[108,"A servant does not believe until he believes in four things: he bears witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah who sent me with the truth, believes in death, believes in the resurrection, and believes in the divine decree (qadar)."],[109,"Do not lie about me, for whoever lies about me will enter the Fire."],[110,"\"Do not pray after 'Asr, unless you pray while the sun is still high.\""],[111,"The Prophet ﷺ sent out a military expedition and appointed a man as commander over them, and commanded them to obey him. He kindled a fire for them and ordered them to plunge into it. Some people were about to do so, but others said, 'We only fled from the Fire,' and they refused. Then they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If they had entered it, they would have remained in it until the Day of Resurrection. There is no obedience to any human being in disobedience to Allah, Mighty and Majestic. Obedience is only in what is right.'"],[112,"\"The angels do not enter a house in which there is an image or a person in a state of major ritual impurity.\""],[113,"That 'Ali ؓ said to a man who was giving a religious ruling permitting mut'ah: 'Look at what you are ruling! I bear witness that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade mut'ah marriage and eating the meat of domesticated donkeys.'"],[114,"'Ali ؓ gave a sermon and said: 'O people, carry out the prescribed punishments on your slaves, both those who are married and those who are not. A slave woman of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ committed adultery, and he commanded me to flog her. I went to her and found that she had recently given birth, and I feared that if I flogged her she would die. So I went to the Prophet ﷺ and told him, and he said: \"You have done well.\"'"],[115,"When the House collapsed after Jurhum and Quraysh rebuilt it, when they wanted to place the Stone they disputed over who should place it. They agreed that the first person to enter from this gate would place it. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered from the gate of Banu Shaybah, and he ordered a cloth to be brought and spread out. He took the Stone and placed it in the middle of it, and he ordered each clan to take hold of a side of the cloth and lift it. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ took it and placed it."],[116,"When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me to Yemen, some people dug a pit for a lion. People crowded around the pit, and the lion fell into it. A man fell in after it, and he grabbed hold of another man, and the other grabbed hold of yet another, until they became four. The lion mauled them in the pit and they died. The people took up arms and nearly fought among themselves. He said: I went to them and said: 'Would you kill two hundred men because of four people? Come, let me judge among you with a ruling. If you accept it, it will be a judgment between you, and if you refuse, you may take it up to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he is more entitled to judge.' He said: He gave the first man a quarter of the blood money, the second a third, the third a half, and the fourth the full blood money. He made the blood moneys payable by those who were present at the pit, upon the four tribes. Some of them were displeased and some were pleased. Then they came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and told him the story, and he said: 'I will judge between you.' A man said: 'But 'Ali has already judged between us.' They told him what 'Ali had ruled, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The ruling is as 'Ali ruled.'"],[117,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed the witr prayer at all parts of the night: at its beginning, middle, and end, and his witr ended at the pre-dawn time.\""],[118,"\"I saw us on the night of Badr, and there was none among us but was asleep, except the Prophet ﷺ, for he was praying toward a tree and supplicating. There was no horseman among us except al-Miqdad ؓ.\""],[119,"'Ammar sought permission to enter upon the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'The pure and purified one; give him permission.'"],[120,"He used to wake his family during the last ten nights."],[121,"A silk suit was gifted to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he sent it to me. I wore it, and he said to me: 'I am not pleased for you what I dislike for myself.' So he commanded me, and I tore it into head covers among the women."],[122,"When my father died, I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: 'Your uncle has died.' He said: 'Go and bury him.' I said: 'He died a polytheist.' He said: 'Go and bury him, and do not do anything until you come to me.' So I did, then I came to him, and he ordered me to perform a full ablution."],[123,"When I returned to the Prophet ﷺ after I had buried him, he said something to me for which I would not like to have the whole world."],[124,"When I came to the Prophet ﷺ after burying Abu Talib, he supplicated for me with certain supplications."],[125,"He used to say in his witr prayer: 'O God, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your wrath, and in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You. I cannot enumerate Your praises; You are as You have praised Yourself.'"],[126,"I have forgiven you the zakat on horses and slaves; so bring a quarter of the tithe: from every forty dirhams, one dirham."],[127,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ sent me to Yemen, I said: 'You are sending me while I am young and have little knowledge of much of judicial matters.' He said: 'When the two litigants come to you, do not judge for the first until you hear what the other says. For when you hear what the other says, you will know how to judge. God, Mighty and Majestic, will make your tongue firm and guide your heart.' Ali said: 'After that, I continued to be a judge.'"],[128,"He used to perform the witr prayer at the time of the call to prayer, and pray two rak'ahs at the time of the iqamah."],[129,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray the forenoon prayer."],[130,"I asked Ali ؓ about the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he mentioned that before the noon prayer he prayed four rak'ahs, two rak'ahs after the noon prayer, and four rak'ahs before the afternoon prayer."],[131,"When al-Hasan b. Ali was born, I said: 'Name him Harb.' I had wanted to be called Abu Harb. The Messenger of God ﷺ came and called for him, and said: 'What have you named him?' We said: 'We named him Harb.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'No, he is al-Hasan.' When al-Husayn was born, we named him Harb. The Prophet ﷺ came and said: 'What have you named him?' We said: 'Harb.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'He is al-Husayn.'"],[132,"Al-Hasan b. Ali was the person most resembling the Messenger of God ﷺ from his face to his navel, and al-Husayn was the person most resembling the Prophet ﷺ below that."],[133,"A man prayed beside me, and I heard him asking forgiveness for his parents, who had died as polytheists. I said: 'You ask forgiveness for your parents while they died as polytheists?' He said to me: 'Abraham asked forgiveness for his parents.' I did not know how to reply to him. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and God, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: 'And Abraham's asking forgiveness for his father was only because of a promise he had made to him...' [Quran 9:114]."],[134,"I witnessed 'Ali when a mount was brought for him to ride. When he placed his foot in the stirrup, he said, \"In the name of Allah.\" When he settled on its back, he said, \"Praise be to Allah,\" three times, and he said, \"Allah is greater,\" three times. Then he said, \"Glory be to You! I have wronged myself, so forgive me; indeed none forgives sins but You.\" Then he laughed. I said, \"O Commander of the Believers, what made you laugh?\" He said, \"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do the same as I did, then he laughed. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what made you laugh?' He said, 'Indeed your Lord, mighty and majestic, marvels at His servant when he says, \"Forgive me my sins,\" knowing that no one forgives sins besides Me.'\""],[135,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade — or forbade me — from jī'ah.\""],[136,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me while I was complaining of pain. I was saying, \"O Allah, if my appointed time has come, then give me rest; if it is delayed, then lift me; and if it is a trial, then give me patience.\" He struck me with his foot and said, \"What did you say?\" I repeated it to him. Then he said, \"O Allah, heal him,\" or he said, \"O Allah, grant him well-being.\" 'Ali said: I never complained of that pain after that."],[137,"I was a man who emitted madhy frequently, and the daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was with me. I ordered a man to ask him about madhy. He said, \"When you see it, perform wudu and wash it.\""],[138,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about madhy. He said, \"When you see madhy, perform wudu and wash your penis; and when you see the gushing of water, perform ghusl.\""],[139,"A slave woman belonging to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ committed fornication. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered me to carry out the prescribed punishment on her. I went to her and found that her blood had not yet dried. I came to the Prophet ﷺ and informed him. He said, \"When her blood dries, flog her. Carry out the prescribed punishments on those whom your right hands possess.\""],[140,"He asked 'Ali about the daughter of a brother through suckling. 'Ali said, \"I mentioned the daughter of Hamzah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'She is the daughter of my brother through suckling.'\""],[141,"'Ali ؓ prayed Zuhr in al-Rahabah, then sat to attend to the people's needs until Asr arrived. Then a jug of water was brought to him. He poured a handful and washed his face and hands, and wiped his head and feet. Then he stood and drank the leftover water while standing. Then he said, \"Some people dislike drinking while standing, but I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ do the same as I did, and he said, 'This is the wudu of one who has not broken his ablution.'\""],[142,"A chair was brought to 'Ali ؓ, and he sat on it. Then a jug of water was brought to him. He washed his hand three times, then rinsed his mouth three times and sniffed water three times with one handful, and washed his face three times with one hand, and washed his forearms three times. He placed his hand in the basin, then wiped his head, and brought his hands forward on his head — I do not know whether he also moved them backward. Then he washed his feet three times. Then he said, \"Whoever would like to see the purification of the Prophet ﷺ, this is the purification of the Prophet ﷺ.\""],[143,"I heard Ibn al-Kawwā' ask 'Ali ؓ about the daughter of a brother through suckling. 'Ali said, \"I mentioned the daughter of Hamzah to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he said, 'She is the daughter of my brother through suckling.'\""],[144,"'Ali prayed Zuhr in al-Rahabah, then sat to attend to the people's needs until Asr arrived."],[145,"We saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stand, so we stood; then we saw him sit, so we sat."],[146,"We went out with the Messenger of God ﷺ in a funeral procession until we reached Baqi' al-Gharqad. The Messenger of God ﷺ sat down, and we sat around him. The Messenger of God ﷺ took a stick and began striking the ground with it. Then he raised his head and said, \"There is no soul that breathes but its place in Paradise and its place in the Fire have been known—or written—and whether it is wretched or blessed.\" A man among the people said, \"O Messenger of God, should we not then abandon action and rely on our book? For whoever among us is among the people of blessedness will act for it, and whoever among us is among the people of wretchedness will act for it.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Act, for everyone is facilitated. Whoever is among the people of blessedness will be facilitated for its action, and whoever is among the people of wretchedness will be facilitated for its action. Then he recited: 'As for him who gives and fears, and believes in the best, We will facilitate for him the easy way. But as for him who is miserly and considers himself self-sufficient, and denies the best, We will facilitate for him the hard way' (Qur'an 92:5-10)."],[147,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ began the prayer, he would say the takbir, then say: \"I have turned my face to Him who created the heavens and the earth, as a hanif, and I am not of the polytheists. Indeed, my prayer, my sacrifice, my living, and my dying are for God, Lord of the worlds. No partner has He. With this I have been commanded, and I am the first of those who submit. O God, You are the King, there is no god but You. You are my Lord and I am Your servant. I have wronged myself and confessed my sin, so forgive me all my sins. None forgives sins but You. Guide me to the best of character; none guides to its best but You. Turn away from me its evil; none turns away its evil but You. Here I am at Your service, all good is in Your hands, and evil is not attributed to You. I am through You and to You. Blessed and exalted are You. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance.\" When he bowed, he said: \"O God, to You I have bowed, in You I have believed, and to You I have submitted. My hearing, my sight, my bones, my marrow, and my nerves humble themselves to You.\" When he raised his head, he said: \"God hears the one who praises Him. O God, our Lord, to You is praise, filling the heavens, filling the earth, filling what is between them, and filling whatever You will after that.\" When he prostrated, he said: \"O God, to You I have prostrated, in You I have believed, and to You I have submitted. My face has prostrated to the One who created it, shaped it, and perfected its form, and split its hearing and sight. Blessed is God, the best of creators.\" When he said the taslim, he said: \"O God, forgive me what I have sent ahead and what I have delayed, what I have made public and what I have concealed, and what You know better than I. You are the One who brings forward and the One who delays; there is no god but You.\""],[148,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had cupping done, and he ordered me, so I gave the cupper his fee."],[149,"The Messenger of God ﷺ tied a turban on me on the day of Ghadir Khumm, letting its end hang down behind me. Then he said: \"Indeed, God, Mighty and Majestic, reinforced me on the day of Badr and Hunayn with angels wearing turbans like this. Indeed, the turban is a barrier between disbelief and faith.\" He saw a man shooting with a Persian bow and said, \"Shoot with it.\" Then he looked at an Arab bow and said, \"You should use this and its likes, and the spears of qana, for with these God will enable you in the lands and support you in victory.\""],[150,"Ali ؓ said to me: \"I appoint you to what the Messenger of God ﷺ appointed me: to efface images and level graves.\""],[151,"It was said to the Prophet ﷺ: \"Should we let a donkey mount a horse?\" He said: \"Only those who do not know do that.\""],[152,"The leader of the Kharijites came to Ali ؓ and said to him: \"Fear God, for you will die.\" He said: \"No, by the One who split the grain and created the soul, but I will be killed by a blow from this one that will dye this—and he pointed with his hand to his beard—a covenant made and a decree decreed. The one who fabricates has failed.\""],[153,"The Messenger of God ﷺ allowed Muslims to share in their sacrificial animals: a cow for seven people."],[154,"A man said to the Prophet ﷺ: \"A man loves a people but cannot act as they do.\" He said: \"A person is with those he loves.\""],[155,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded us to inspect the eye and the ear [of sacrificial animals]."],[156,"I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ in a house, and he said: \"O Ali, ask God for guidance, and remember with guidance that He guides you to the path. Ask God for rightness, and remember with rightness that He makes your arrow hit the mark.\""],[157,"We were sitting with Ali ؓ waiting when a funeral procession passed by us, and we stood up for it. He said: \"What is this?\" We said: \"This is what you have brought to us, O Companions of Muhammad. Abu Musa al-Ash'ari narrated to us that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'When the funeral procession of a Muslim man, or a Jew, or a Christian passes by you, stand up for it. For we do not stand up for it, but we stand up for the angels who are with it.'\" Ali said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ did that only once. They were People of the Book, and he used to imitate them in some things, but when he was forbidden, he stopped.\""],[158,"The killer of al-Zubayr b. al-'Awwam asked permission to enter upon 'Ali b. Abi Talib ؓ . 'Ali said: By God, the killer of Ibn Safiyya will surely enter the Fire. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Every prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr."],[159,"\"The middle prayer is the afternoon prayer ('asr)."],[160,"\"Some people of my community will recite the Qur'an but it will not go beyond their collarbones. They will pass out of Islam as the arrow passes out of the game. Their mark is a man with a deformed hand.\" Abu Maryam said: My brother told me, and he had gone out with his master to the Haruriyya at al-Nahrawan. He said: He did not come to them until they had killed his messenger. When he saw that, he rose against them and fought them. When he finished with them, he said: Look for the deformed one. The messengers kept going back and forth but could not find him. Then a man came later and gave him the good news. He said: We found him in a low spot of ground under two men. So he cut off his hands and the small breast, took it, and set it up. He said: By God, I have not lied and I have not been lied to. He said this many times."],[161,"I will not tell you except what Ibn Abi Talib ؓ told me: Among them is one with a defective hand, or a deformed hand, or a withered hand. Were it not that you would become heedless, I would tell you what God promised to those who kill them on the tongue of His Prophet ﷺ. I said to 'Ali ؓ : Did you hear it from Muhammad ﷺ? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Ka'bah, saying it three times."],[162,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade me to wear a ring on the middle finger and the one next to it.\""],[163,"'Ali used to go out to the market and say: God and His Messenger have spoken the truth. It was said to him: Your saying: God and His Messenger have spoken the truth. He said: God and His Messenger have spoken the truth. When I narrate to you from the Messenger of God ﷺ , by God, that I fall from the sky and the birds snatch me away is dearer to me than that I say: I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ what I did not hear. And when I narrate to you from myself, then indeed war is deception. I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: In the last days there will come a people young in age, foolish in intellect, who speak with the words of the best of creation. They recite the Qur'an but it does not go beyond their throats. They pass out of the religion as the arrow passes out of the game. Whoever meets them, let him kill them or fight them, for whoever kills them will have a reward on the Day of Resurrection."],[164,"\"Look for the deformed one.\" So they searched for him but did not find him. They came to him and he said: Go back and look for him, for by God, I have not lied and I have not been lied to, until he said that to me many times. They went back and said: We found him under the slain in the mud. It is as if I were looking at him, an Abyssinian, with a breast like a woman's breast, with small hairs like the small hairs on the tail of a jerboa. 'Ali ؓ was delighted by that."],[165,"\"A servant does not find the taste of faith until he believes in destiny entirely.\""],[166,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ was neither short nor tall, with a large head and beard, coarse palms and feet, large joints, his face tinged with redness, with a long line of hair from the chest to the navel. When he walked, he leaned forward as if descending a slope. I have not seen before him or after him anyone like him.\""],[167,"\"Indeed God, Mighty and Majestic, named war on the tongue of His Prophet ﷺ deception.\""],[168,"I was present with 'Uthman b. 'Affan ؓ when al-Walid b. 'Uqbah was brought, having drunk wine. Humran b. Aban and another man testified against him. 'Uthman said to 'Ali: Carry out the punishment on him. 'Ali ordered 'Abd Allah b. Ja'far, the one with the two wings, to flog him. He began flogging him while 'Ali counted, until he had flogged him forty lashes. Then he said to him: \"Stop; the Messenger of God ﷺ flogged forty, Abu Bakr ؓ flogged forty, and 'Umar ؓ flogged eighty, and all is sunnah, and this is dearer to me.\""],[169,"'Ali ؓ came out to us when the caller called the iqamah, and said: Your Prophet ﷺ commanded the witr and set for it this hour. Give the adhan, O Ibn al-Nabbah, or give the iqamah, O Ibn al-Nabbah."],[170,"Whoever leaves a hair unwashed by water from janaba, Allah will do such-and-such to it with the Fire. That is why I treated my head—or he said: my hair—with hostility, and he used to crop his hair."],[171,"The Prophet ﷺ performed ablution three times each."],[172,"A man said: O Messenger of Allah, I had one hundred uqiyyahs and gave ten uqiyyahs of them as charity. Another said: O Messenger of Allah, I had one hundred dinars and gave ten dinars of them as charity. Another said: O Messenger of Allah, I had ten dinars and gave one dinar of them as charity. He said: All of you have done well, and you are equal in reward; each of you gave a tenth of his wealth as charity."],[173,"I am the first to pray with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[174,"When he passed by the Black Stone and saw crowding around it, he faced it and said takbir, then said: O Allah, in confirmation of Your Book and the Sunnah of Your Prophet ﷺ."],[175,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ruled that debt comes before the bequest, while you recite: after any bequest or debt. Full brothers from the same mother inherit, but not half-brothers from different mothers."],[176,"I witnessed 'Ali ؓ being asked about Hudhayfah. He said: He asked about the names of the hypocrites and was told them. He was asked about himself, and he said: I knew myself. When I asked I was answered, and when I was silent I was approached."],[177,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me a striped silk garment—meaning of silk—and I wore it and went out in it. I saw anger in his face, and he said: I did not send it to you to wear. He said: So I tore it between our women—or my women."],[178,"O 'Ali, I love for you what I love for myself and hate for you what I hate for myself. Do not recite while bowing or while prostrating, do not pray with your hair twisted, the seat of the devil, do not play with pebbles while in prayer, do not wear a gold ring, do not wear qassi, and do not ride on mayathir."],[179,"There is no one on whom I carried out a prescribed punishment who then died and I had to pay blood money, except the punishment for wine, for the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not institute it—or he said: except the punishment for wine, for we have instituted it."],[180,"We have nothing except the Book of Allah and this sheet from the Prophet ﷺ: Madinah is a sanctuary between 'Ayr and Thawr. Whoever introduces an innovation in it or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Allah will not accept from him any compensation or ransom. Whoever gives allegiance to a people without the permission of their masters, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. No compensation or ransom will be accepted from him."],[181,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me two slave boys who were brothers, and I sold one of them. The Prophet ﷺ said: What happened to the two slaves? I said: I sold one of them. He said: Return him."],[182,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ made peace with Quraysh, he wrote: “This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of God, has agreed upon.” They said: “If we knew you were the Messenger of God, we would not have fought you.” So he erased it and wrote: “Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah.”"],[183,"Three men came to him who had shared in the purity of a woman, and he cast lots among them and said: “You are quarrelsome partners.” He assigned the child to the one who won the lot and made the other two liable for two-thirds of the blood-money. He told the Prophet ﷺ about that, and he laughed until his molars showed."],[184,"I heard 'Ali ؓ giving a sermon, and he laughed a laugh I never saw him laugh before, while he was on the pulpit. He said: “I remember praying with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and my father looked in on us while I was praying with the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: ‘My son, what are you two doing?’ I said: ‘We were praying.’ Abu Talib said: ‘By God, by God, you will never surpass me in my backside.’\" He said: “I saw him laugh at his father’s words.” Then he said: “I remember I prayed before the people for years.”"],[185,"I have not suffered from eye inflammation or headache since the Messenger of God ﷺ handed me the banner on the day of Khaybar."],[186,"The Messenger of God ﷺ visited us and spent the night with us while al-Hasan and al-Husayn were asleep. Al-Hasan asked for water, so the Messenger of God ﷺ got up to a water-skin of ours and began squeezing it into a cup, then giving him to drink. Al-Husayn reached for it to drink, but he prevented him and began with al-Hasan. Fatimah said: “O Messenger of God, it is as if he is more beloved to you than the other.” He said: “No, but he asked first.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “I, you, and these two—and I think he said: and this one lying down, meaning 'Ali—will be in one place on the Day of Resurrection.”"],[187,"I said to al-Zubayr ؓ: “What prevents you from narrating from the Messenger of God ﷺ as Ibn Mas'ud and so-and-so and so-and-so narrate?” He said: “By God, I have not been separated from him since I embraced Islam, but I heard him say a word. He said: ‘Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire.’”"],[188,"We used to pray the Friday prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ, then we would hurry to the shade, and there would be only the space of a foot or two feet."],[189,"We heard al-Zubayr ؓ reciting this verse: “And fear a trial which will not strike those who have wronged among you exclusively.” He said: “I recited this verse for a long time and did not think I was among its people, but we have become among its people.”"],[190,"The disease of the nations before you has crept upon you: envy and hatred. Hatred is the shaver; I do not say it shaves hair, but it shaves religion. By the One in whose hand is my soul, you will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another. Shall I tell you what will make that firm for you? Spread peace among yourselves.”"],[191,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me while I was ill and said to me: “Have you made a will?” I said: “Yes, I have bequeathed all my wealth.” He said: “What have you left for your children?” I said: “They are rich with good.” He said: “Bequeath a tenth.” He kept reducing and I kept reducing until he said: “Bequeath a third, and a third is a lot.”"],[192,"I fell ill with a sickness from which I nearly died, and the Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon me. I said: “O Messenger of God, I have abundant wealth, and only one daughter will inherit from me. Should I give all my wealth in charity?” He said: “No.” I said: “Should I give half in charity?” or he said: “Should I bequeath half?” He said: “No.” I said: “O Messenger of God, then what should I bequeath?” He said: “A third, and a third is a lot. If you leave your heirs rich, it is better than leaving them poor, begging from people’s hands.”"],[193,"You will never spend any expenditure except that you will be rewarded for it, even the morsel you raise to your wife’s mouth."],[194,"I fell severely ill and was on the verge of death. The Messenger of God ﷺ came in to see me, and I said, “O Messenger of God, will I be left behind without my emigration?” He said, “You will not be left behind after me such that you do any deed seeking the face of God except that you will increase in rank and degree by it. Perhaps you will be left behind until some people benefit through you and others are harmed through you. O God, complete the emigration of my companions and do not turn them back on their heels. But the wretched one is Saʿd b. Khawlah.” The Messenger of God ﷺ was lamenting for him because he died in Makkah."],[195,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave to some people and withheld from a man. Saʿd said, “O Messenger of God, by God, he is indeed a believer.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Or a Muslim.” Then Saʿd said, “By God, I consider him a believer.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said, “Or a Muslim.” Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said, “I give to a man and leave one who is better than him, for fear that God, Mighty and Majestic, may cast him on his face into the Fire.”"],[196,"\"Whoever claims descent from someone other than his father, knowing that he is not his father, Paradise is forbidden to him.\""],[197,"Saʿd ؓ heard a son of his saying, “O God, I ask You for Paradise and its chambers such-and-such, and I seek refuge in You from the Fire and its fetters and chains.” Saʿd said to him, “You have asked God for abundant good and sought refuge in Him from abundant evil”—or he said, “great evil”—“and I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘There will be people who go to extremes in supplication. It is sufficient for you to say: O God, I ask You for all good, what I know of it and what I do not know, and I seek refuge in You from all evil, what I know of it and what I do not know.’”"],[198,"\"He is not one of us who does not chant the Qurʾān.\""],[199,"\"For the belly of a son of Adam to be filled with pus is better for him than to be filled with poetry.\""],[200,"The Prophet ﷺ said about the plague: \"If it is in a land and you are in it, do not leave it; and if it is in a land and you are not in it, do not enter it.\""],[201,"ʿIkrimah b. Khālid narrated to us, from Yaḥyā b. Saʿd, from Saʿd, from the Prophet ﷺ, the like of it."],[202,"The Prophet ﷺ said to ʿAlī: \"Are you not pleased to be to me as Hārūn was to Mūsā?\""],[203,"\"On the day of Uḥud I saw on the right of the Messenger of God ﷺ and on his left two men wearing white garments, fighting fiercely in defense of the Messenger of God ﷺ. I had not seen them before that day, nor after it.\""],[204,"I prayed beside Saʿd. When I bowed, I clasped my hands and placed them between my knees. My father said to me, \"We used to do that until we were forbidden from it and commanded to place our hands on the knees.\""],[205,"Four verses were revealed concerning my father. He said: My father said: I acquired a sword on the day of Badr, and I brought it to the Prophet ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, give it to me as a share of spoil.\" He said, \"Put it back where you took it from.\" I repeated, \"Will I be left like one who has no use?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Put it back where you took it from.\" Then this verse was revealed: \"They ask you about the spoils of war\"—and in the reading of ʿAbd Allāh it is thus: \"They ask you for the spoils of war,\" the whole verse. He said: And the mother of Saʿd said, \"Has not God commanded obedience to parents? I will not eat food or drink drink until you disbelieve in God.\" She abstained from food and drink until they had to pry her mouth open with a stick. Then it was revealed: \"And We have enjoined upon man goodness to his parents; but if they strive with you to make you associate with Me that of which you have no knowledge, do not obey them.\" A man of the Anṣār prepared food and invited some of the Muhājirūn and some of the Anṣār. We ate and drank until we became drunk, then we began boasting. A man raised the jawbone of a camel and struck Saʿd's nose with it, splitting it. Saʿd's nose was split. That was before wine was forbidden. Then it was revealed: \"O you who believe, do not approach prayer while you are intoxicated,\" and: \"Wine, gambling, stone altars, and divining arrows are only defilement from the work of Satan,\" the verse. The Messenger of God ﷺ entered upon Saʿd while he was ill, and he wanted to bequeath all his wealth. He kept reducing it for him until he reached one-third. He said: The people bequeath one-third."],[206,"The Messenger of God ﷺ left ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib ؓ behind in the expedition of Tabūk. He said: O Messenger of God, do you leave me behind with the women and children? He said: Are you not pleased that you are to me as Hārūn was to Mūsā, except that there is no prophet after me?"],[207,"Happiness for the son of Adam is three, and misery for the son of Adam is three. From the happiness of the son of Adam: a righteous wife, a good mount, and a spacious dwelling—or he said: a good dwelling. And misery for the son of Adam is three: a bad dwelling, a bad woman, and a bad mount."],[208,"I wonder at the Muslim: when a calamity befalls him, he seeks reward and is patient; and when good befalls him, he praises God and gives thanks. Indeed, the Muslim is rewarded in everything, even in the morsel he raises to his mouth."],[209,"We saw ourselves with the Messenger of God ﷺ when we had no food except the leaves of trees, until one of us would defecate as a sheep does. Then the Banū Asad came to chastise me for Islam. I have then surely lost and my effort has gone astray."],[210,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to ʿAlī ؓ: You are to me as Hārūn was to Mūsā."],[211,"I asked Saʿd about buying sult (hulled barley) with white [wheat], and he disliked it. Saʿd said: I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about fresh dates for dry dates. He said: Do fresh dates decrease when they dry? They said: Yes. He said: No—or he forbade it."],[212,"I said: O Messenger of God, which people are most severely tried? He said: The prophets, then the next best, then the next best. A man is tried according to his religion. If his religion is firm, his trial is severe; and if there is weakness in his religion, he is tried accordingly—or to the extent of that. Tribulation does not cease with the servant until he walks upon the earth with no sin upon him."],[213,"ʿUmar said to Saʿd ؓ: They have complained about you in everything, even in prayer. He said: As for me, I used to lengthen in the first two [rakʿahs] and shorten in the last two, and I do not fall short of what I followed from the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: That is what was thought of you—or my thought of you."],[214,"The people of Kufa complained about Saʿd to ʿUmar, so he removed him and appointed ʿAmmār over them. They said: Saʿd does not pray well. ʿUmar mentioned that to him. Saʿd said: As for me, I used to lead them in the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ, not falling short of it: the two evening prayers. I prolong in the first two and shorten in the last two. ʿUmar said: That is what was thought of you, O Abā Isḥāq."],[215,"\"Whomever you catch cutting something from the trees—meaning the trees of the Ḥaram—his spoils are yours. Its trees are not to be cut or chopped.\" Saʿd saw young men cutting, so he took their belongings. They went to their masters and told them that Saʿd had done such and such. They came to him and said: O Abā Isḥāq, your servant—or your clients—took the belongings of our servants. He said: Rather, I took it. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whomever you catch cutting from the trees of the Ḥaram, his spoils are yours. But ask me from my wealth whatever you wish."],[216,"The Prophet ﷺ rejected celibacy for ʿUthmān b. Maẓʿūn. Had he permitted it for him, we would have castrated ourselves."],[217,"The Messenger of God ﷺ united his parents for me on the day of Uḥud."],[218,"There is no death I could die more beloved to me than to be killed defending my property unjustly."],[219,"The Banu Najiyah were mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: \"They are a clan from me.\" He said: And I think he said: \"And I am from them.\" Then either the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Weep for Samah b. Lu'ayy,\" and a man said: \"The attachment to Samah has clung,\" or the man said that, and the Messenger of God ﷺ responded to him."],[220,"When 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf had prayed and the Prophet ﷺ came, he began to step back, but the Prophet ﷺ gestured to him: stay as you are. So the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed following the prayer of 'Abd al-Rahman."],[221,"The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned Ramadan and said: \"It is a month whose fasting God has made obligatory upon you, and I have established its night prayer as a sunnah. Whoever fasts it and prays it at night out of faith and seeking reward will emerge from his sins as on the day his mother bore him.\""],[222,"'Umar did not take the jizyah from the Magians until 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf ؓ testified that the Prophet ﷺ took it from the Magians of Hajar."],[223,"I heard from a man a hadith that pleased me, so I said: write it down. He brought it to me written down, inscribed. He said: 'Ali and al-'Abbas entered upon 'Umar, and with him were 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf, al-Zubayr b. al-'Awwam, and Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas. He said: I adjure you by God—did you not hear, or did you not know, that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"All the wealth of the Prophet is charity except what he feeds his family and clothes them with. We are not inherited from.\"? They said: Yes indeed."],[224,"Whoever spends an excellent expenditure in the way of God, Mighty and Majestic, the good deed is multiplied by seven hundred. And whoever spends on himself, or on his family, or visits a sick person, or removes something harmful, the good deed is multiplied by ten times its like. And fasting is a shield as long as one does not tear it. And whoever God, Mighty and Majestic, afflicts in his body, he has an expiation."],[225,"God, Mighty and Majestic, began this matter as prophethood and mercy, and it will be caliphate and mercy, and it will be a biting kingship, and it will be tyranny, compulsion, and corruption in the earth. They will deem lawful private parts, wine, and silk, and they will be given victory over that and provided for forever until they meet God."],[226,"Expel the Jews of the Hijaz from the Arabian Peninsula."],[227,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when he came upon a people pollinating date palms. He said: \"What are these people doing?\" I said: They are pollinating the date palms, placing the male into the female. He said: \"I do not think this accomplishes anything.\" Then he said: If it benefits them, let them do it. Do not hold me to account for conjecture, but when I tell you something from God, Mighty and Majestic, I do not lie about God at all."],[228,"One day we mentioned to the Messenger of God ﷺ what passes in front of us of animals while we are praying, and he said: \"Let one of you place in front of him something like the rear part of a saddle, and whatever passes in front of him will not harm him.\""],[229,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about the meat of game that a person in the permitted state gives as a gift to a person in the sacred state, and he allowed it."],[230,"Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr, and whoever is killed defending his blood is a martyr."],[231,"Zayd b. 'Amr and Waraqah b. Nawfal went out seeking the religion until they came to a monk in Mosul. He said to Zayd b. 'Amr: \"From where have you come, O owner of the camel?\" He said: \"From the house of Ibrahim.\" He said: \"And what do you seek?\" He said: \"I seek the religion.\" He said: \"Return, for it is about to appear that which you seek in your land.\" As for Waraqah, he became a Christian. Zayd said: \"As for me, Christianity was offered to me, but it did not suit me.\" So he returned, saying: \"Labbayk, truly, truly, in worship and servitude. I seek righteousness, not the transient. Is one who emigrates like one who merely says, 'I believe in what Ibrahim believed'?\" And he said: \"I reject for You, O Allah, a humiliated, submissive one. Whatever You burden me with, I will bear.\" Then he fell down and prostrated. He said: His son came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, my father was as you have seen and as has reached you, so ask forgiveness for him.\" He said: \"Yes, for on the Day of Resurrection he will be a nation alone.\" He said: Zayd b. 'Amr b. Nufayl came upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and with him was Zayd b. Harithah, while the two of them were eating from a travel provision of theirs. They invited him to their food, but Zayd b. 'Amr said to the Prophet ﷺ: \"O son of my brother, we do not eat from what is slaughtered on stone altars.\""],[232,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on Hira', and with him were Abu Bakr, 'Umar, 'Uthman, 'Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Sa'd, and 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf ؓ. He said: \"Be still, Hira', for upon you are only a prophet, a truthful one, or a martyr.\" Sa'id mentioned that he was with them."],[233,"I witnessed al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah delivering a sermon, and he disparaged 'Ali. Sa'id b. Zayd b. 'Amr b. Nufayl al-'Adawi—of 'Adi Quraysh—ؓ stood up and said: \"I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Ten are in Paradise: the Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr, 'Umar, 'Uthman, 'Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Sa'd b. Malik, and 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf' ؓ. If I wished, I would name the tenth.\" Then he named him and said: \"Sa'id b. Zayd.\""],[234,"Marwan sent us to reconcile between Sa'id b. Zayd b. 'Amr b. Nufayl and a woman called Arwa, who claimed something of land against him. Sa'id said: \"Do you think I would take anything from her land when I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever wrongs a span of land will be collared with it from seven earths'?\""],[235,"Whoever seizes property with his oath, may Allah not bless it for him."],[236,"Marwan wanted to take his land, but he refused him and said: \"If they come to me, I will fight them; I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever is killed defending his property is a martyr.'\""],[237,"Whoever takes as a client someone without the permission of his clients, upon him is the curse of Allah."],[238,"I asked Sa'd b. Ibrahim about Banu Najiyah, and he said: \"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'They are a tribe from me,' and I think he said: 'and I am from them.'\" I said: \"Who narrates this from the Prophet ﷺ?\" He said: \"Sa'id b. Zayd.\""],[239,"He has not believed in Allah who has not believed in me, and he has not believed in me who has not loved the Ansar."],[240,"There is no prayer without ablution, and there is no ablution for one who does not mention the name of Allah over it."],[241,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ drew a line for us and said: \"This is the path of Allah.\" Then he drew lines on its right and left and said: \"These are paths; on every one of them is a devil calling to it.\" Then he recited: \"And this is My path, straight...\" the verse."],[242,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and greeted him with salam, but he did not respond to me. Then what is old and what is new seized me, and I said: O Messenger of God, has something happened concerning me? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: God, Mighty and Majestic, brings about for His Prophet whatever He wills of His affair, and among what He has brought about is that you should not speak during the prayer."],[243,"\"God, Mighty and Majestic, looked into the hearts of the servants, and chose Muhammad, and sent him with His messages, and selected him by His knowledge. Then He looked into the hearts of people after him, and chose for him his companions, and made them supporters of His religion and ministers of His Prophet ﷺ. Whatever the believers see as good is good in God's sight, and whatever the believers see as ugly is ugly in God's sight.\""],[244,"\"The servant does not cease to be truthful and strive for truthfulness until he is recorded with God as a siddiq, and he does not cease to lie and strive for lying until he is recorded with God as a kadhdhab.\""],[245,"\"Insulting a believer is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief.\""],[246,"When we prayed behind the Messenger of God ﷺ, we used to say: Peace be upon God, peace be upon Gabriel, peace be upon Michael. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ turned to us and said: Do not say 'Peace be upon God,' for God, Mighty and Majestic, is al-Salam. But say: 'Greetings are for God, and prayers and good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of God and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger.'"],[247,"Umar surpassed the people by the supplication of the Messenger of God ﷺ concerning Umar: O God, support the people through Umar."],[248,"Ibn al-Nawwahah and Ibn Uthal came as messengers of Musaylimah to the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to them: \"Do you both testify that I am the Messenger of God?\" They said: \"We testify that Musaylimah is the Messenger of God.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I believe in God and His messengers. If I were to kill a messenger, I would kill you both.\""],[249,"\"God, Mighty and Majestic, took Abraham as a close friend, and your companion is the close friend of God. The Prophet of God ﷺ is the most honored of creatures in the sight of God, Mighty and Majestic, on the Day of Resurrection.\" Then he recited: \"It may be that your Lord will raise you to a praiseworthy station.\""],[250,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ disapproved of night conversation with us after the evening prayer.\""],[251,"\"A person is with the one he loves.\""],[252,"\"Every treacherous one will have a banner on the Day of Resurrection, and it will be said: This is the treachery of so-and-so.\""],[253,"\"I am informed of your gathering, and nothing prevents me from coming out to you except fear that I might bore you. The Messenger of God ﷺ used to take turns with us in admonition, fearing weariness upon us.\""],[254,"Whoever dies while ascribing a rival to God will enter the Fire. 'Abdullah said: And I say: whoever dies while not ascribing a rival to God, God will admit him to Paradise."],[255,"When there are three people, two should not converse privately to the exclusion of the third, for that would grieve him."],[256,"Reviling a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."],[257,"A man asked 'Abdullah about the saying of God, Mighty and Majestic: 'from water not stagnant' or 'yasin.' 'Abdullah said: Have you read the entire Qur'an except this? He said: Yes. He said: There are people who recite it, scattering it like the scattering of bad dates; it does not go beyond their collarbones. I know the pairs of surahs that the Messenger of God ﷺ used to combine. He said: So we told 'Alqama, and he asked him. He said: Twenty surahs from the Mufassal; the Messenger of God ﷺ used to combine every two surahs in one rak'ah."],[258,"We said: O Messenger of God, will we be held accountable for what we did in the Jahiliyyah? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Whoever does good in Islam will not be held accountable for what he did in the Jahiliyyah and Islam, and whoever does evil in Islam will be held accountable for what he did in the Jahiliyyah and Islam."],[259,"How bad it is for one of them to say: I forgot such-and-such a verse. Rather, he was made to forget. So keep reminding each other of the Qur'an, for by the One in whose hand is my soul, it slips away from men's chests more readily than camels from their hobbles."],[260,"Whoever swears a false oath to seize thereby property, being sinful in it, will meet God, Mighty and Majestic, while He is angry with him. He said: Then al-Ash'ath b. Qays al-Kindi came out to us and said: What did Abu 'Abd al-Rahman narrate to you? We said: Such-and-such a hadith. He said: He spoke the truth. It was revealed concerning me. I disputed with a man over a well before the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Your evidence or his oath.' I said: Then he will swear and he is sinful. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Whoever swears a false oath, being sinful or wicked in it, to seize thereby property, will meet God, Mighty and Majestic, while He is angry with him. And it was revealed: 'Indeed, those who purchase with the covenant of God and their oaths a small price...' the verse."],[261,"Indeed, before the Hour there will be days of harj, days in which knowledge will disappear and ignorance will appear."],[262,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: Which sin is greatest? He said: That you ascribe a rival to God while He created you. He said: Then which? He said: That you kill your child for fear that he will eat your property. He said: Then which? He said: That you commit adultery with your neighbor's wife."],[263,"And he recited this verse: 'And those who do not call upon another god besides God, and do not kill the soul which God has forbidden except by right, and do not commit adultery.'"],[264,"No one is more protective of honor than God, Mighty and Majestic, and for that reason He forbade immoralities, what is apparent of them and what is hidden. And no praise is more beloved to Him than praising God, and for that reason He praised Himself. And no one loves excuses more than God, Blessed and Exalted."],[265,"A man came to Ibn Mas'ud and said: I recited the Mufassal tonight in one rak'ah. 'Abdullah said: Babbling like the babbling of poetry! I knew the pairs of surahs that the Messenger of God ﷺ used to combine. He mentioned twenty surahs from the Mufassal, two surahs in each rak'ah."],[266,"A woman should not embrace another woman and then describe her to her husband so that it is as if he is looking at her."],[267,"The first thing that will be judged — or decided — among people on the Day of Resurrection is bloodshed."],[268,"When it was revealed: Those who believe and do not mix their faith with wrongdoing, they said: Which of us has not erred? Until this verse was revealed: Do not associate anything with God; indeed, associating partners with Him is a tremendous wrongdoing."],[269,"The Messenger of God ﷺ led us in prayer and added or omitted something — the one who forgot whether it was Ibrahim from 'Alqama, or 'Alqama from 'Abdullah — when he finished his prayer it was said: O Messenger of God, has something new happened in the prayer? He said: \"No, and what is that?\" So we mentioned to him what he had done. He bent his leg and faced the qibla, then prostrated twice, then turned his face toward us and said: If something had happened in the prayer I would have informed you, but I am a human being like you; I forget as you forget, so if I forget, remind me. And whichever of you is uncertain about his prayer, let him consider what is most likely correct and complete it on that basis, then say the salam, and prostrate twice."],[270,"He was standing with 'Abdullah at 'Arafa during the caliphate of 'Uthman. 'Uthman said to 'Abdullah: Shall I marry you to — Abu Dawud said: Shu'ba or someone else said in this chain: — Shall I marry you to a young woman who will remind you of what you have forgotten? 'Abdullah said, so that 'Alqama could hear: The Messenger of God ﷺ told us: Whoever among you is able to marry, let him marry, and if not, let him fast, for fasting is a shield for him."],[271,"\"I indeed know the paired surahs that the Messenger of God ﷺ used to join together.\" He said: So we ordered 'Alqama to ask him, and he said: Twenty surahs from the mufassal, the Messenger of God ﷺ used to join between each two surahs in one rak'a."],[272,"\"The people with the most restrained killing are the people of faith.\""],[273,"Ibn Mas'ud took his hand, and Ibn Mas'ud mentioned that the Prophet ﷺ took his hand and taught him the tashahhud: Greetings are for God, and prayers and good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of God and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. When you have said that, your prayer is complete; if you wish, stand, and if you wish, remain seated."],[274,"He prayed the noon prayer with five units, and it was said to him: Has the prayer been increased? The Prophet ﷺ said: And what is that? They said: You prayed five. So he prostrated twice after he had said the salam."],[275,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ lay down on a reed mat, and the mat left marks on his skin. I began to wipe it from him and say: May my father and mother be your ransom, O Messenger of God, if only you had told us so we could spread something for you to protect you from it to sleep on. He said: What do I have to do with this world? What am I and this world? I and this world are only like a rider who took shade under a tree, then moved on and left it.\""],[276,"\"About His saying, Mighty and Majestic: He certainly saw some of the greatest signs of his Lord, he said: He saw Gabriel ﷺ on a green rafraf that filled the horizon of the sky.\""],[277,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ saying takbir in every lowering and raising, and standing and sitting, and saying salam to his right and to his left, until I saw the whiteness of his cheek.\" And I saw Abu Bakr and 'Umar ؓ doing that."],[278,"Regarding the saying of Allah, Mighty and Majestic: “The Hour has drawn near and the moon has split,” he said: The moon split during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ."],[279,"“The people are saying that you were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the night of the jinn.” He said: “None of us accompanied him, but we lost him in Makkah, so we searched for him in the mountain passes and the valleys. I said: ‘He has been assassinated or snatched away.’ So we spent the worst night a people ever spent. When morning came, we saw him coming toward us. We said: ‘O Messenger of Allah, we spent the worst night a people ever spent; we lost you.’ He said: ‘The caller of the jinn came to me, so I went and recited the Quran to them.’ He went with us and showed us their dwellings and their fires. They asked him for provision, and he said: ‘Every bone upon which the name of Allah has not been mentioned, when it falls into your hands, will have more meat than it did; and every piece of dung is fodder for your animals.’ Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade us to use those two for istinja’, and he said: ‘They are provision for your brothers among the jinn.’”"],[280,"He heard the Prophet ﷺ reciting: “Then is there any who will remember?”"],[281,"The Prophet ﷺ recited Surat al-Najm in Makkah and prostrated in it, and those with him prostrated except an old man who took a handful of pebbles or dust and raised it to his forehead, saying: “This suffices me.” Abdullah said: “I saw him killed as a disbeliever on the day of Badr.”"],[282,"Let none of you assign to Satan a share of his prayer, seeing it as obligatory that he should only depart to his right; I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ most often departing to his left."],[283,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that he had been intimate with a woman short of intercourse. The Prophet ﷺ did not respond to him until Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: “And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and in the approaches of the night”—the verse. A man said: “O Messenger of Allah, is this specifically for him or for all the people?” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Rather, for all the people.”"],[284,"He used to greet to his right: “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah and His blessings,” and to his left: “Peace be upon you and the mercy of Allah.”"],[285,"The Prophet ﷺ entered the privy, so I followed him and placed for him two stones and a piece of dung. He came out, took the two stones, and threw away the dung, saying: “It is impure.”"],[286,"When captives were brought to him, he gave the entire household together, and he disliked separating them."],[287,"The blood of a Muslim is not lawful except for one of three: the married adulterer, a life for a life, and one who abandons his religion and separates from the community."],[288,"He is not from us who strikes the cheeks, tears the garments, and calls with the call of jahiliyyah."],[289,"We asked Abdullah about the souls of the martyrs—and had it not been for Abdullah we would have found no one to tell us. He said: The souls of the martyrs are with Allah in the crops of green birds, which roam in the rivers of Paradise wherever they wish, then return to lanterns beneath the Throne. He, Mighty and Majestic, says to them: “What do you desire?” They say: “We desire nothing”—he said it three times—“except to be returned to the world and killed.”"],[290,"Selling the ones whose milk has been withheld in the udder to deceive the buyer is a fraud, and fraud is not lawful for a Muslim."],[291,"When Quraysh became obstinate against the Messenger of God ﷺ, he supplicated against them for years of famine until they ate carrion and bones, until a man would stand and see between him and the sky something like smoke. That is His saying, exalted is He: 'The day when the sky will bring visible smoke.'"],[292,"Whoever has knowledge, let him speak with his knowledge. And whoever does not have knowledge—or he said: Whoever is asked about what he has no knowledge of—let him say: 'God knows best,' for God, mighty and majestic is He, said to His Prophet ﷺ: 'Say: I do not ask you for any reward for it except love of relatives.'"],[293,"The moon split during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ. Quraysh said: 'This is the magic of Ibn Abi Kabsha.' He said: They said: 'Wait for what the travelers bring to you, for Muhammad cannot bewitch all the people.' He said: The travelers came and said: 'That is true.'"],[294,"Verily, the evil does not expiate the bad, but the good expiates the bad."],[295,"You will see after me favoritism and matters you will reject. We said: 'O Messenger of God, what do you command us?' He said: 'Give them their right that He has assigned to them, and ask God for your right.'"],[296,"Verily, the creation of one of you is gathered in his mother's womb for forty nights, then he becomes a clinging clot for the like of that, then he becomes a lump of flesh for the like of that. Then an angel is sent to him and is commanded with four words: his provision, his term, his deeds, and whether he is wretched or blessed. Then the spirit is breathed into him. By God, one of you—or a man among you—may do the deeds of the people of the Garden until there is only a cubit between him and it, then the decree overtakes him, and he does the deeds of the people of the Fire and enters it. And a man among you—or one of you—may do the deeds of the people of the Fire until there is only a cubit between him and it, then the decree overtakes him, and he does the deeds of the people of the Garden and enters it."],[297,"The best of my community is my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people whose oaths precede their testimonies, and they testify before they are asked to testify."],[298,"If I were to take a close friend from my community, I would have taken Abu Bakr."],[299,"A man keeps telling the truth until he is recorded as a truthful one, and a man keeps lying until he is recorded as a liar."],[300,"We came to the Prophet ﷺ regarding a companion of ours, asking his permission for cauterization—that we should cauterize him. He remained silent. Then we repeated it, and he remained silent. Then we repeated it a third time, and he remained silent. Then we repeated it again, and he said: 'Burn him with heated stones, burn him,' and he disliked that."],[301,"He used to supplicate with this supplication: 'O God, I ask You for guidance, piety, chastity, and self-sufficiency.'"],[302,"We did not know what to say in every two rak'ahs except to glorify, magnify, and praise our Lord. Muhammad ﷺ was taught the openings of good and its comprehensive words—or its comprehensive words and its conclusions—so he commanded us to say in every two rak'ahs: All greetings, prayers, and pure words are due to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger. Then let each of you choose the supplication that pleases him most and supplicate with it."],[303,"I came to al-Aswad b. Yazid—who was a brother and friend to me—and said: Abu al-Ahwas adds in the tashahhud on the authority of 'Abdullah: 'and the blessed words.' He said: 'Go to him and forbid him from this, and tell him: 'Abdullah taught 'Alqamah the tashahhud, counting them on his hand.'"],[304,"Fighting a Muslim is disbelief, and insulting him is wickedness. Indeed, it is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days."],[305,"We asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about monkeys and pigs: Are they from the descendants of the Jews? He said: No. Allah, Mighty and Majestic, never cursed a people and transformed them so that they would have descendants. But this is a creation that already existed. When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, became angry with the Jews and transformed them, He made them like those creatures."],[306,"The Prophet ﷺ gave two salutations in the prayer."],[307,"Do not insult Quraysh, for its scholar will fill the earth with knowledge. O Allah, You have made the first of them taste punishment—or calamity—so make the last of them taste bounty."],[308,"Do not be impressed by a man with wide forearms who sheds blood, for he has a killer with Allah who does not die. And do not be impressed by a man who earns wealth unlawfully, for if he spends it or gives it in charity, it will not be accepted from him; if he leaves it, it will not be blessed for him; and if any of it remains, it will be provision for him to the Fire."],[309,"The Hour will not come except upon the worst of people."],[310,"When Allah gives you wealth, let it be seen upon you. Give from what is surplus, and begin with those you support. You are not blamed for having just enough. Hands are three: the hand of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, is the highest; the hand of the giver is next to it; and the hand of the beggar is the lowest until the Day of Resurrection."],[311,"Whoever would be pleased to meet Allah, Mighty and Majestic, tomorrow as a Muslim, let him maintain these five prayers where the call to them is given. Allah has prescribed for your Prophet ﷺ the ways of guidance, and they are among the ways of guidance. I do not think any of you but has a place of prayer in his house where he prays. If you were to pray in your houses and abandon your mosques, you would abandon the Sunnah of your Prophet ﷺ. If you abandoned the Sunnah of your Prophet, you would go astray. No Muslim performs ablution and does it well, then walks to the prayer, except that a good deed is written for him with every step he takes, a degree is raised for him thereby, and a sin is expiated from him thereby—so much so that we used to take short steps. I have seen us when none stayed behind from it except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was known. I have seen a man supported between two men until he was placed in the row."],[312,"If I were to take an intimate friend, I would take Abu Bakr as an intimate friend, but he is my brother and companion. Indeed, your companion is the intimate friend of Allah."],[313,"Whoever kills a snake, it is as if he killed an unbeliever."],[314,"I had considered ordering a man to lead the people in prayer, then I would stay behind and go to those who stay away from the Friday prayer, and burn their houses down upon them."],[315,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me to recite: “Indeed, I am the Provider, Possessor of Strength, the Firm.”"],[316,"I performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he prayed two rak'ahs at Mina, and with Abu Bakr, who prayed two rak'ahs at Mina, and with 'Umar, who prayed two rak'ahs. Would that my share of four rak'ahs were two accepted rak'ahs."],[317,"He performed Hajj with 'Abdullah and he threw the jamrah with seven pebbles, placing the House on his left and Mina on his right, and he said: This is the standing place of the one upon whom Surat al-Baqarah was sent down."],[318,"We were on a military expedition in which 'Abd al-Rahman b. Yazid was present, and it spread among the people that some disliked saying “Surat al-Baqarah” and “Al 'Imran,” saying instead “the surah in which the cow is mentioned” and “the surah in which the family of 'Imran is mentioned.” 'Abd al-Rahman said: I was with 'Abdullah at Mina when he entered the valley, and he placed the jamrah on his right eyebrow, then faced the Ka'bah and threw seven pebbles, saying Allahu akbar with each pebble. When he finished he said: From here—by the One besides whom there is no god—did the one upon whom Surat al-Baqarah was sent down throw."],[319,"'Abdullah prayed the dawn prayer at Muzdalifah in the darkness before dawn and said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not pray this prayer at this time except in this place."],[320,"\"Whoever asks while having enough to be independent will come on the Day of Resurrection with scratches or marks on his face.\" It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what suffices him? He said: \"Fifty dirhams or their equivalent in gold.\""],[321,"Regarding His saying, Mighty and Majestic: “The heart did not lie about what it saw,” he said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ saw Jibril in a green robe of fine silk, filling what is between the heaven and the earth."],[322,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in a tent, about forty of us, and he said: “Would you be pleased to be a quarter of the people of Paradise?” They said: Yes. He said: “Would you be pleased to be a third of the people of Paradise?” Then he said: “By the One in whose hand is my soul, I hope that you will be half of the people of Paradise. That is because Paradise is entered only by a Muslim soul, and you among the polytheists are but like a white hair on the hide of a black bull, or a black hair on the hide of a red bull.”"],[323,"While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was prostrating, with some people of Quraysh around him, and there was the afterbirth of a camel, they said: Who will take the afterbirth of this slaughtered camel—or camel—and throw it on the Prophet's back? 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt came and threw it on the Prophet's back ﷺ. Fatimah came, removed it from his back, and cursed those who had done that. 'Abdullah said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ invoke against them except on that day, when he said: O Allah, deal with the leaders of Quraysh. O Allah, deal with Abu Jahl b. Hisham, 'Utbah b. Rabi'ah, Shaybah b. Rabi'ah, 'Uqbah b. Abi Mu'ayt, and Umayyah b. Khalaf—or Ubayy b. Khalaf. Shu'bah was uncertain. 'Abdullah said: I saw them killed on the day of Badr and thrown into the well—or he said: into a pit—except that Ubayy b. Khalaf—or Umayyah b. Khalaf—was a heavy man, and he fell apart before he could be brought to the pit."],[324,"I frequented 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud for a year, and I never heard him say during it: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said,” except that one day a hadith came up, and he said: “The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said,” and distress overcame him, and sweat began to pour from his eyes, then he said: “Either more than that, or less than that, or close to that.”"],[325,"\"He would supplicate three times and seek forgiveness three times.\""],[326,"When it was the day of Badr, I came upon Abu Jahl while he was struck down. I struck him with my sword, but it did nothing, and his sword flew off. I struck him again, then I came to the Prophet ﷺ on a hot day, as if I were lifted from the ground. I said, 'O Messenger of God, this enemy of God, Abu Jahl, has been killed.' The Prophet ﷺ said, 'By God, has he been killed?' I said, 'By God, he has been killed. Come with us and I will show him to you.' He came to him and looked at him, then said, 'This was the Pharaoh of this community.'"],[327,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and asked him about the Night of Decree. He said, 'Which of you remembers the night of al-Sahbawat?' 'Abdullah said, 'I, by God—may my father and mother be my ransom—I remember it. I had in my hand some small dates with which I was having my pre-dawn meal, hiding behind the rear of my saddle from the dawn, and that was when the moon rises.'"],[328,"The prophets used to ride donkeys, wear wool, and milk sheep. The Messenger of God ﷺ had a donkey named 'Ufayr."],[329,"The Messenger of God ﷺ, in the first two rak'ahs, was as if he were on hot coals. He said: He would move his lips with something. I would say, 'Until he stands.' He would say, 'Until he stands.'"],[330,"When one of you follows a funeral procession, let him take hold of the four sides of the bier, then afterwards he may volunteer or leave off, for that is from the sunnah."],[331,"The polytheists preoccupied us from the Zuhr, 'Asr, Maghrib, and 'Isha' prayers. The Messenger of God ﷺ ordered Bilal, so he gave the call to prayer and the iqamah, and we prayed Zuhr. Then he gave the iqamah, and we prayed 'Asr. Then he gave the iqamah, and we prayed Maghrib. Then he gave the iqamah, and we prayed 'Isha'. Then he said, 'There is no group on earth remembering God, Mighty and Majestic, other than you.'"],[332,"Whoever would like to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it according to the recitation of Ibn Umm 'Abd."],[333,"Have mercy on those on earth, and the One in heaven will have mercy on you."],[334,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a journey. A man entered a thicket and took out from it the egg of a red sparrow. The red sparrow came fluttering over the head of the Messenger of God ﷺ and his companions. He said, 'Which of you has bereaved this one?' A man from the group said, 'I took its egg.' He said, 'Return it, return it, out of mercy for it.'"],[335,"You will certainly be afflicted, and you will be aided, and conquest will be granted to you. Whoever among you lives to see that, let him fear God, enjoin what is right, and forbid what is wrong."],[336,"The Messenger of God ﷺ taught us the sermon of need: 'Praise belongs to God—or indeed praise belongs to God—we seek His help and His forgiveness, and we seek refuge in God from the evils of our own selves. Whomever God guides, none can lead astray, and whomever He leads astray, none can guide. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His messenger.' Then he recites the three verses: 'O you who believe, fear God as He should be feared' to the end of the verse. And he recites: 'O people, fear your Lord, who created you from a single soul' the verse. Then he recites: 'O you who believe, fear God and speak a right word; He will set right for you your deeds' to the end of the verse. Then you speak about your need."],[337,"The Prophet ﷺ used to say often: 'Glory be to You, our Lord, and with Your praise. O God, forgive me.' When the chapter 'When God's help and victory comes' was revealed—'then glorify with praise of your Lord and seek His forgiveness; indeed He is ever accepting of repentance'—he said: 'Glory be to You and with Your praise. O God, forgive me. Indeed You are the Accepting of repentance, the Merciful.'"],[338,"While I was praying one night, the Prophet ﷺ passed by me, along with Abu Bakr and Umar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Ask, and you will be given.' Umar said: 'So Abu Bakr and I raced. I never raced Abu Bakr to any good except that I found he had beaten me to it. Then I went off and said: I have a supplication that I almost never abandon: O Allah, I ask You for faith that does not turn back, and coolness of the eye that does not cease—or he said: does not perish—and the companionship of the Prophet ﷺ in the highest Garden of Eternity.'"],[339,"I entered the mosque of Kufa on Friday, and there was a man whom the people had gathered around. If they could have put him inside their bellies, they would have, out of love for him. And there he was, narrating. He said: 'Abdullah said: Do not multiply testimony, saying \"So-and-so was killed as a martyr, and so-and-so was killed as a martyr.\" If you must praise a people as having been martyred, then praise the expedition that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to a tribe. They did not remain but a short while before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us and said: \"Indeed, your brothers have met their Lord. Indeed, they asked Allah, mighty and glorious, to convey on their behalf that they were pleased, and He was pleased with them. So if you are to praise a people as martyrs, then praise those.\""],[340,"Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."],[341,"He cursed the consumer of riba, the one who gives it, and its two witnesses—or he said: its witness and its scribe."],[342,"The likeness of the one who helps his people upon falsehood is like a camel that has fallen and is being dragged by its tail."],[343,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ encamped at a place and went off to relieve himself. He came back and found that a man had lit a fire on an ant colony, either in a tree or on the ground. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Who did this?' A man from the group said: 'I did.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Put it out, put it out.'"],[344,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent us to the Negus, and we were eighty men. With us were Ja'far b. Abi Talib and Uthman b. Maz'un. Quraysh sent Umara and Amr b. al-As, and they sent a gift with them to the Negus. When they entered upon him, they prostrated to him and presented the gift. They said: 'Some people from our tribe have turned away from our religion and have settled in your land.' He said: 'Where are they?' They said: 'They are in your land.' So the Negus sent for them. Ja'far said: 'I am your spokesman today.' So they followed him until they entered upon the Negus, and they did not prostrate to him. He said: 'What is wrong with you that you do not prostrate to the king?' He said: 'Allah, mighty and glorious, sent His Prophet ﷺ to us and commanded us not to prostrate except to Allah.' The Negus said: 'And what is that?' He was informed, and Amr b. al-As said: 'They disagree with you about Jesus.' He said: 'What do you say about Jesus and his mother?' He said: 'We say as Allah, mighty and glorious, said: He is the Spirit of Allah and His word that He cast to the chaste virgin, whom no human touched and no child rent.' The Negus picked up a stick and said: 'O assembly of priests and monks, you do not add to what they say even the weight of this.' He said: 'Welcome to you and to the one from whom you came. I bear witness that he is a prophet, and I wish I were with him so that I could carry his sandals—or he said: serve him. So settle wherever you wish in my land.' Ibn Mas'ud came and hurried, and he witnessed Badr."],[345,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when he smiled. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, why did you smile?' He said: 'I marvel at the believer and his anxiety over illness. If he knew what is in illness, he would love to remain ill until he meets Allah, mighty and glorious.'"],[346,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ raised his gaze to the sky, then lowered it. We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, why did you do that?' He said: 'I marveled at two angels from among the angels who descended to the earth seeking a servant at his place of prayer but did not find him. Then they ascended to their Lord and said: \"O Lord, we used to record for Your believing servant in his day and night such and such deeds, but we found that You had detained him in Your snare, so we recorded nothing for him.\" He, mighty and glorious, said: \"Record for My servant his deeds in his day and night, and do not reduce anything from him. Upon Me is the reward for what I detained him from, and for him is the reward of what he used to do.\""],[347,"Whoever says in his bowing three times: 'Glory be to my Lord, the Magnificent,' his bowing is complete, and that is the minimum. And whoever says in his prostration three times: 'Glory be to my Lord, the Most High,' his prostration is complete, and that is the minimum."],[348,"Let not Bilal's call to prayer deceive you about your pre-dawn meal, for he only calls so that your standing one may return and your sleeping one may awaken. And not this dawn that is like this—meaning the bright spread one—but the dawn that is like this—meaning the elongated one."],[349,"He saw a Bedouin wearing a cloak that he let trail while praying. He said to him: 'The one who drags his garment out of pride in prayer is not in a lawful state with Allah, neither permitted nor forbidden.'"],[350,"\"The nations were shown to me at the gathering place, and I saw my community filling the plain and the mountain, and their large number and their appearance pleased me. It was said to me: Are you satisfied? I said: Yes. He said: And with these are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning, who do not cauterize, do not practice augury, do not seek ruqya, and upon their Lord they rely.\" 'Ukkasha b. Mihsan al-Asadi stood up and said: O Messenger of God, pray to God to make me one of them. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O God, make him one of them.\" Another stood up and said: Pray to God, Mighty and Majestic, to make me one of them. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"'Ukkasha has preceded you to it.\""],[351,"I was a young boy pasturing sheep for 'Uqba b. Abi Mu'ayt in Makkah. The Messenger of God ﷺ and Abu Bakr came upon me, having fled from the idolaters. He said: \"O boy, do you have milk to give us to drink?\" I said: I am entrusted, and I will not give you to drink. They said: \"Do you have a young she-camel that no stallion has mounted yet?\" I said: Yes. I brought it to them, Abu Bakr hobbled it, and the Messenger of God ﷺ took the udder and supplicated, and the udder filled with milk. Abu Bakr brought him a hollowed rock, and he milked into it. Then he and Abu Bakr drank, then they gave me to drink. Then he said to the udder: \"Shrink,\" and it shrank. Later I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: Teach me some of this good speech — meaning the Qur'an. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"You are a taught boy.\" I took from his mouth seventy surahs, in which no one disputes with me."],[352,"On the day of Badr we were two on a camel and three on a camel. The Prophet's ﷺ riding companions were 'Ali and Abu Lubaba al-Ansari. When their turn to walk came, they said: O Messenger of God, ride, we will walk instead of you. He said: \"You are not stronger at walking than I, nor do I desire less reward than you.\""],[353,"He used to cut a siwak from an arak tree for the Prophet ﷺ, and the wind would bend him over, and there was thinness in his shins, so the companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ laughed. He said: \"What makes you laugh?\" They said: At the thinness of his shins. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"By the One in whose hand is my soul, he is heavier in the balance than Uhud.\""],[354,"\"Augury is shirk, and there is none of us but God removes it by reliance.\""],[355,"A man of the people of the suffa died, and they found two dinars in his shawl. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Two brands of fire.\""],[356,"Zirr b. Hubaysh passed by us, and I stood up to him and asked him about the saying of God, Mighty and Majestic: 'He certainly saw of the signs of his Lord the greatest.' Zirr said: 'Abdullah said: He saw Jibril in his form, having six hundred wings."],[357,"\"I never saw the Messenger of God ﷺ not fasting on Friday.\""],[358,"The Messenger of God ﷺ \"used to fast three days at the beginning of each month.\""],[359,"We said: O Messenger of God, how will you recognize those of your community whom you have not seen on the Day of Resurrection? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Brightly marked with white on their faces, hands, and feet, and with white blazes on their legs, from the traces of ablution.\""],[360,"\"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[361,"\"Some people sat in the mosque: two Qurayshis and a Thaqafi — or two Thaqafis and a Qurayshi. One of them said: Do you think God hears what we say? One of them said: If we raise our voices He hears, and if we do not raise them He does not hear. The other said: If He hears any of it, He hears all of it. I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and God, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: 'And you were not concealing yourselves lest your hearing testify against you...' the verse.\""],[362,"An imam for the people of Makkah performed two taslims, so 'Abdullah said: \"Whence did he learn that?\""],[363,"There is no night-talk after the prayer except for one of two men: a traveler or one praying."],[364,"They distracted us from the middle prayer—the 'Asr prayer. May Allah fill their houses and graves with fire."],[365,"Indeed, the truest speech is the Book of Allah, the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad ﷺ, the worst of matters are their innovations, and indeed what you are promised will surely come, and you cannot frustrate [Him]. And truly far off is what is not coming."],[366,"Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has not sent down any disease but that He has sent down for it a cure, except old age. So take to the milk of cows, for they graze on every kind of tree."],[367,"There is no envy except in two cases: a man whom Allah has given wealth and empowered him to spend it in the way of truth, and a man whom Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has given wisdom and knowledge, so he judges by it and teaches it to the people."],[368,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was suffering from a fever, so I touched him and said: O Messenger of Allah, you are suffering from a severe fever. He said: Yes, I suffer a fever as severe as two men among you. I said: That is because you have a double reward? He said: Yes, and by the One in whose hand is my soul, no Muslim is afflicted with any harm—illness or anything else—except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sheds his sins from him as a tree sheds its leaves."],[369,"He used to seek refuge in prayer from the accursed Shaytan—from his blowing, his spitting, and his poking."],[370,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: Which deed is best? He said: Prayer at its proper time. I said: Then which—or he said: Then what? Abu Dawud was uncertain—he said: Then kindness to parents. I said: Then what—or then which?—he said: Striving in the path of Allah. He told me these, and if I had asked for more, he would have added."],[371,"When he pronounced the taslim, he would say: O Allah, You are Peace, and from You is peace. Blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor."],[372,"In some of his supplications he would say: O Allah, as You have made my creation good, so make my character good."],[373,"A man came to Abu Musa and asked him about a man who left behind his daughter, his son's daughter, and his sister. He said: To the daughter half, and to the sister half. Go to 'Abdullah, and he will agree with me. So the man came to 'Abdullah and mentioned that to him, and he said: Then I would have gone astray and would not be of the rightly guided. I will judge in this case with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ: to the daughter half, to the son's daughter one-sixth, and to the sister the remainder. He then went to Abu Musa and informed him, and he said: Do not ask us about anything as long as this scholar is among you."],[374,"\"The Prophet ﷺ was on a journey, so he delayed Zuhr and performed 'Asr early, combining them, and delayed Maghrib and performed 'Isha early, combining them.\""],[375,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on his return from al-Hudaybiyah, and we stopped to rest at night. He said, \"Who will guard us for our prayer?\" – and Shu'bah said, \"Who will keep watch over us?\" – Bilal said, \"I will.\" Al-Mas'udi said in his narration: \"You will fall asleep.\" He said, \"Who will guard us for our prayer?\" Ibn Mas'ud said: I said, \"I will.\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"You will fall asleep.\" He said: So I kept watch over them until, when dawn was approaching, what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ had said overtook me, and I slept. We did not wake except with the sun. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ got up and did what he used to do, then said, \"If Allah, Mighty and Majestic, had willed that you not sleep through it, you would not have slept. But He willed that it should be for those after you, so this is for whoever of you sleeps or forgets.\" Shu'bah said in his narration: \"Thus do, whoever of you sleeps or forgets.\" And al-Mas'udi said in his narration – and it is not in Shu'bah's narration: The mount of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ went astray, so we searched for it, and found it by a tree, its nose-rein caught on the tree. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, no hands could have untied it.\""],[376,"\"O 'Abdullah, do you know which of the bonds of Islam is most reliable?\" I said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"Allegiance for the sake of Allah, love for the sake of Allah, and hatred for the sake of Allah. O 'Abdullah, do you know which of the people is most knowledgeable?\" I said, \"Allah and His Messenger know best.\" He said, \"The most knowledgeable of people is the one most knowledgeable of the truth when people differ, even if he is deficient in knowledge, and even if he crawls on his backside.\""],[377,"\"Do not acquire estates, lest you become desirous of the world.\""],[378,"I heard Shimr b. 'Atiyyah al-Asadi reporting from a man of Tayyi', from his father, from 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud, from the Prophet ﷺ something similar."],[379,"\"He forbade the acquisition of multiple properties.\""],[380,"I was with my father, and I was beside him, in the presence of 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud. My father said to him, \"Did you hear the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Remorse is repentance?\" He said, \"Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[381,"\"Whoever comes to a soothsayer and believes what he says has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad ﷺ.\""],[382,"The fortune-tellers are the soothsayers of the Persians. Whoever believes in a soothsayer has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad ﷺ."],[383,"\"The millstone of Islam will turn for thirty-five, or thirty-six, or thirty-seven years. If they perish, then it is the way of those who perished. If their religion remains established for them, it will remain for seventy years.\" 'Umar said, \"O Messenger of Allah, for what has passed or what remains?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, \"For what remains.\""],[384,"He said to the women, \"Give charity, for you are the majority of the people of the Fire.\" A woman who was not from the elite of the women, or from the most intelligent of them, said, \"O Messenger of Allah, in what – or because of what or why?\" He said, \"Because you curse frequently and are ungrateful to your husbands.\""],[385,"Did you hear it from him? He said, \"Yes, more than fifty times.\" He said, \"Your Prophet ﷺ was given the keys of the unseen except the five: Indeed, Allah has knowledge of the Hour... to the end of the surah.\""],[386,"He forbade a gold ring, or a gold circle."],[387,"I recited a verse, and a man recited it differently. So we came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned that to him. Shu'bah said: The best of my knowledge is that the Messenger of God ﷺ said to them both: Do not differ, for those before you differed and were destroyed."],[388,"The foreleg was the most beloved part of the sheep to the Messenger of God ﷺ, the foreleg of the sheep, and it had been poisoned in it, and he thought that the Jews had poisoned it."],[389,"Then God, Mighty and Majestic, permits intercession. The Holy Spirit, Gabriel, stands up, then Ibrahim, the Friend of God, stands up, then 'Isa or Musa—Abu al-Za'ra' said: I do not know which of them he said—then your Prophet ﷺ stands up fourth and intercedes. He does not intercede for anyone after him in more than what he intercedes. That is the Praiseworthy Station of which God, Mighty and Majestic, said: 'It may be that your Lord will raise you to a Praiseworthy Station.'"],[390,"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ curse women who pluck their eyebrows, those who file their teeth for beauty, and those who tattoo, those who alter God's creation."],[391,"Part of the Sunnah is the major ablution (ghusl) on Friday."],[392,"We were sitting with 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud when a red wind blew. A man came whose only refrain was saying: 'O 'Abdullah, the Hour has come! O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, the Hour has come!' He sat up straight, anger showing on his face, for he had been reclining on a couch of his. He said: The Hour will not come until no inheritance is divided and no booty is rejoiced over. Then he said: An enemy of the Muslims will gather against them, and he gestured with his hand. I said to Abu Qatadah: You mean Syria? He said: Yes. He said: At that fighting there will be a severe apostasy. He said: The Muslims will seek reinforcements from one another. They will meet and fight a severe battle. He said: Then a detachment will be singled out for death, which will not return except victorious. They will meet and fight until night separates them. These and those will withdraw, each not victorious, and the detachment will perish. On the second day, a detachment will be singled out for death. They will meet and fight until night separates them. These and those will withdraw, each not victorious, and the detachment will perish. On the third day, a detachment will be singled out for death. They will meet and fight until night separates them. These and those will withdraw, each not victorious, and the detachment will perish. On the fourth day, the rest of the Muslims will advance against them, and God, Mighty and Majestic, will grant them victory. A man will look at a family of a father: they used to number a hundred, and not one of them remains except one man. So what inheritance would be divided or what booty would be rejoiced over? He said: While they are like that, they hear something greater than that: the Dajjal has left them behind among their children and families. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Their commander will send a scouting party of ten horsemen. I indeed know their names, their fathers' names, and the colors of their horses. On that day they will be the best horsemen on earth, or among the best horsemen on earth."],[393,"Among the signs of the Hour are that mosques are taken as thoroughfares, that a man greets another man only because he knows him, that a man and his wife trade together, and that the dowers of women and horses become expensive, then become cheap, and will not become expensive until the Day of Resurrection."],[394,"We came to Ibn Mas'ud and heard him saying: 'God and His Messenger have spoken the truth. God and His Messenger have spoken the truth.' We said: 'O Abu 'Abd al-Rahman, what is this?' He said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ said: The Night of Decree is in the middle of the seven; the sun rises with no rays.' So I watched it, and it was as the Messenger of God ﷺ said."],[395,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ praying in sandals and leather socks."],[396,"The Messenger of God ﷺ disliked ten things: yellow dye—meaning khaluq—, wearing a gold ring, incantations except with the mu'awwidhat, withdrawing semen from its place, displaying adornment to other than its proper place, tying amulets, dragging the lower garment, spoiling a child without making it forbidden, changing gray hair, and playing with dice."],[397,"I entered with 'Abdullah b. Mas'ud upon Khabbab, who had cauterized himself. 'Abdullah said: 'Do you not know that we have been forbidden from this, and it is disliked for us?' Khabbab said: 'The affliction became severe, and the doctors said: You have no cure except that.' 'Abdullah said: 'I did not fear you would do this.'"],[398,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought captives, and he began giving the whole household together, and he disliked separating them."],[399,"Abdullah sold al-Ash'ath b. Qays slaves from the slaves of the emirate. He sent to him demanding payment. Al-Ash'ath said, 'You sold me for ten thousand.' Abdullah said, 'I sold you for twenty thousand.' Abdullah said, 'Choose a man between me and you.' Al-Ash'ath said, 'By God, I will choose, and you are between me and myself.' Abdullah said, 'By God, I will judge between me and you with a judgment I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ: When the two parties to a sale differ and there is no evidence between them, it is according to what the owner of the merchandise says, or they may mutually rescind.'"],[400,"Beware of the insignificant sins, for they gather upon a man until they destroy him. The Messenger of God ﷺ struck a parable for them, like the parable of a people who camped in a desert land, and the people's food was prepared. One man came with a stick, and another came with a small stick, until they gathered from that a black mass. Then they kindled a fire, and it cooked what was thrown into it."],[401,"The one who consumes riba, the one who gives it, its two witnesses, its scribe, the woman who tattoos and the woman who asks to be tattooed for beauty, the one who makes lawful and the one for whom it is made lawful, the one who withholds zakat, and the one who reverts to being a Bedouin after his emigration—all are cursed on the tongue of Muhammad on the Day of Resurrection."],[402,"God, mighty and majestic, has not forbidden any sacred thing but that He knew someone among you would violate it. Indeed, I am holding you by your waist-wrappers lest you tumble into the Fire as flies tumble."],[403,"I am a man who will be taken. So learn the Quran and teach it to people, learn the shares of inheritance and teach them to people, learn knowledge and teach it to people. For I will be taken, and knowledge will decrease and tribulations will appear until two people differ over an obligatory share and find no one to judge between them."],[404,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ one night until we prolonged the conversation, then we returned to our families. When morning came, we went to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: The prophets were presented to me with their nations and their followers from their nations. A prophet passed with three from his nation, a prophet with a band from his nation, a prophet with a small group from his nation, a prophet with one man from his nation, and a prophet with no one from his nation. Then Moses b. ʿImran passed by me in a throng of the Children of Israel. When I saw them, they amazed me. I said, 'O Lord, who is this?' He said, 'This is your brother Moses b. ʿImran and those who followed him from the Children of Israel.' I said, 'O Lord, where is my nation?' He said, 'Look to your right.' I looked, and there were the hillocks—the hillocks of Makkah—filled with the faces of men. I said, 'O Lord, who are these?' It was said, 'These are your nation.' It was said, 'Are you pleased?' I said, 'Yes, I am pleased.' It was said, 'Look to your left.' I looked, and the horizon was filled with the faces of men. I said, 'O Lord, who are these?' It was said, 'These are your nation.' It was said, 'Are you pleased?' I said, 'Yes, O Lord, I am pleased.' It was said, 'With these are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning.' Then ʿUkkasha b. Mihsan, brother of Banu Asad, rose and said, 'O Messenger of God, pray to God to make me one of them.' He said, 'O God, make him one of them.' Then another man rose and said, 'O Messenger of God, pray to God to make me one of them.' He said, 'ʿUkkasha b. Mihsan has preceded you to it.' He said: And it was mentioned to us that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'May my father and mother be your ransom. If you can be among the seventy, then be. If you are unable and fall short, then be among the people of the hillocks. If you are unable and fall short, then be among the people of the horizon, for I saw there many people mingling.' He said: And it was mentioned to us that men among the believers—or people among the believers—debated among themselves, saying, 'What do you think these seventy thousand are?' They came to say about their affair: 'People born in Islam who continued to act upon it until they died upon it.' Their talk reached the Prophet of God ﷺ, and he said: 'It is not as you say, but they are those who do not cauterize, do not seek ruqya, do not take omens, and upon their Lord they rely.' And it was mentioned to us that the Prophet of God ﷺ said: 'I hope that those who follow me from my nation will be a quarter of the people of Paradise.' We said takbir. He said: 'I hope they will be half.' He said: They said takbir, and he recited this verse: 'A multitude of the former and a multitude of the latter.'"],[405,"I have wrongfully taken my mushaf. Whoever can wrongfully take a mushaf, let him do so, for God, mighty and majestic, said: 'And whoever defrauds will bring what he defrauded on the Day of Resurrection.' I took from the mouth of the Messenger of God ﷺ seventy surahs, while Zayd b. Thabit was a boy among boys. So shall I abandon what I took from the mouth of the Messenger of God ﷺ?"],[406,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to a people's rubbish dump and urinated standing. Then he called for water. I brought him water, and he performed wudu and wiped over his leather socks."],[407,"It was said to Hudhayfah, 'Abu Musa is strict about urinating.' Abu Dawud said: Jarir said in this hadith: 'Abu Musa used to urinate in a bottle and was strict about urinating.' Hudhayfah said: 'I wish he would not do that. I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ when he came to a people's rubbish dump and urinated standing.'"],[408,"Umar said, 'Who will tell us about the tribulation?' Hudhayfah said, 'I will.' He said, 'You?' He said, 'O Commander of the Faithful, the tribulation of a man in his family and wealth is expiated by fasting, charity, enjoining good, and forbidding evil.' He said, 'I am not asking you about that. I am asking you about the tribulation before the Hour, which surges like the waves of the sea.' He said, 'O Commander of the Faithful, between you and it is a closed door.' Umar said, 'Tell me about the door: will it be broken or opened?' He said, 'Rather, it will be broken.' Umar said, 'Then it will never be closed until the Day of Resurrection.' Abu Wa'il said: We said to Masruq, 'Ask Hudhayfah who the door is.' He asked him, and he said, 'The door is Umar.'"],[409,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ stood for night prayer, he would rub his mouth with the siwak."],[410,"The hypocrites today are worse than they were in the time of the Prophet ﷺ: then they used to conceal it, but today they make it manifest."],[411,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought al-Buraq, a white riding beast, larger than a donkey and smaller than a mule. He and Gabriel did not leave its back until they brought him to Jerusalem, then Gabriel ascended with him to heaven. Gabriel asked for the gate to be opened, and he showed him Paradise and Hellfire. Then he said to me: Did he pray in Jerusalem? I said: Yes. He said: What is your name, bald one? I recognize your face but I do not know your name. I said: I am Zirr b. Hubaysh. He said: Where do you find that he prayed? I recited the verse 'Glory be to Him who made His servant travel by night' to the end. He said: Had he prayed, you would have prayed there as you pray in the Sacred Mosque. I said to Hudhayfah: Did he tie the beast to the ring to which the prophets used to tie it? He said: Would he fear that it might run away from him when God had brought it to him?"],[412,"The people of Najran came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: Send us a trustworthy man. He said: I will certainly send you a man who is truly trustworthy, truly trustworthy, truly trustworthy. The Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ looked up eagerly for it. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ sent Abu Ubaydah b. al-Jarrah."],[413,"Islam is eight shares: Islam is one share, prayer is one share, zakah is one share, pilgrimage is one share, fasting Ramadan is one share, commanding good is one share, forbidding evil is one share, and jihad in the path of God is one share. He who has no share has indeed failed."],[414,"People will be gathered on a single plain, and no soul will speak. The first one called will be Muhammad ﷺ, and he will say: Here I am and at Your service; good is in Your hands, and evil is not to You. The guided one is he whom You guide; Your servant is before You. I am from You and to You. Blessed and exalted are You, our Lord. Glory be to You, Lord of the House. This is His saying, Mighty and Majestic: 'It may be that your Lord will raise you to a praiseworthy station.'"],[415,"He prayed with the Prophet ﷺ at night. In his bowing he would say: 'Glory be to my Lord, the Mighty,' and in his prostration he would say: 'Glory be to my Lord, the Most High.' Whenever he came to a verse of mercy he would pause and ask, and whenever he came to a verse of punishment he would pause and seek refuge."],[416,"He prayed with the Prophet ﷺ—Abu Dawud said: meaning the night prayer. When he said the takbir, he said: God is the greatest, possessor of dominion, might, pride, and greatness. Then he recited al-Baqarah. Then he bowed, and his bowing was like his standing. In his bowing he kept saying: 'Glory be to my Lord, the Mighty, glory be to my Lord, the Mighty.' Then he raised his head from bowing and stood like his bowing, and he said: 'Praise belongs to my Lord.' Then he prostrated, and his prostration was like his standing. In his prostration he would say: 'Glory be to my Lord, the Most High.' Then he raised his head from prostration, and between the two prostrations he would say: 'Lord, forgive me; Lord, forgive me,' and he sat for as long as his prostration. Hudhayfah said: He prayed four rak'ahs, reciting in them al-Baqarah, Al Imran, al-Nisa, and al-Ma'idah or al-An'am."],[417,"There is nothing wrong with me after what I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. If you fight one another, I will enter my house, and if someone enters upon me, I will say: Here, take my sin and your sin."],[418,"We have been preferred over people by three things: our rows have been made like the rows of angels, the earth has been made a mosque for us and its dust a means of purification, and I was given the last verses of Surah al-Baqarah from a treasure beneath the Throne."],[419,"Every good deed is charity."],[420,"People will certainly come out of Hellfire stinking, after the Fire has scorched them, and they will enter Paradise by the mercy of God and the intercession of the intercessors. They will be called the Jahannamis."],[421,"This tribe of Mudar will not leave any righteous servant of God on earth without afflicting him and destroying him, until God sends against them forces from Him or from heaven, and He will humble them so that they cannot defend even the tail of a watercourse."],[422,"It was said to Hudhayfah about a man: \"Indeed this one informs the rulers.\" Hudhayfah said: \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'No talebearer will enter Paradise.'\""],[423,"\"Whoever sells a house and does not put its price into a house, he is not blessed.\""],[424,"Qays narrated to us, from Yusuf, from Abu 'Ubaydah b. Hudhayfah, from Hudhayfah, raising it similarly."],[425,"The Messenger of God ﷺ narrated two hadiths to us. I have seen one of them and I am waiting for the other. He narrated to us: \"Trustworthiness descended in the roots of men's hearts, and they learned from the Qur'an and learned from the Sunnah.\" Then he narrated to us about its removal. He said: \"A man among you sleeps a sleep, and a black dot is made in his heart, and its trace remains in his interior like a blister, like an ember you rolled on your foot and it blistered. You see it raised, with nothing in it. People wake up with no trustworthy one among them. Indeed a time passed over me when I did not care which of you I did business with: if he was a Muslim, his Islam would return it to me; if he was a Jew or a Christian, his official would return it to me. But now I have reached the point that I do not do business with any of you except so-and-so and so-and-so. And there will come upon the people a time when it will be said of a man: 'How witty he is, how intelligent he is,' while there is not in his heart faith equal to the weight of a barley grain.\""],[426,"The Messenger of God ﷺ took hold of the muscle of my shin and said: \"The right of the lower garment is to here, and if you refuse then to here, and if you refuse then there is no right of the lower garment in the two ankles,\" or \"no right of the two ankles in the lower garment.\""],[427,"We said to Hudhayfah: \"Tell us of a man close in guidance and manner to the Messenger of God ﷺ so that we may keep to him.\" He said: \"I know no one closer in guidance and manner to the Messenger of God ﷺ until the wall of his house conceals him than Ibn Umm 'Abd.\" 'Abd al-Rahman said: And Hudhayfah said: \"The preserved ones among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ know that Ibn Umm 'Abd is among the closest of them to God in means.\""],[428,"I said: \"O Messenger of God, I am a man sharp of tongue, and most of that is upon my family.\" He said: \"Where are you from seeking forgiveness? Indeed I seek forgiveness from my Lord one hundred times a day.\""],[429,"\"The fear prayer is two rak'ahs and four prostrations. If a matter presses you, fighting and speaking have become lawful for you.\""],[430,"Hudhayfah asked for water, and a village chief brought him a silver vessel, so he threw it at him and said: \"I only did this because I had warned him about it. The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade drinking from vessels of gold and silver, and wearing silk brocade and silk. And he said: 'It is for them in this world and for you in the Hereafter.'\""],[431,"\"Do not say: 'What God wills and what so-and-so wills,' but say: 'What God wills alone.'\""],[432,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ made partnership among the Muslims in their sacrificial animals: a cow from seven.\""],[433,"\"I was sitting with Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman and Abu Mas'ud al-Badri when the people of Kufah went out to Sa'id b. al-'As and turned him back, and that was the day of al-Jar'ah. He said: I heard Abu Mas'ud say: 'I did not think that it would return without blood being shed in it.' Hudhayfah said: 'But I, by God, I knew that it would return on its heels without a cupping glass of blood being shed in it. I knew nothing of that except a thing I learned while Muhammad ﷺ was alive: a man wakes up a believer and by evening there is nothing of his religion with him, and by evening a believer and wakes up with nothing of his religion with him. He fights in the faction of the people—or he said: in the fitnah of the day; Abu Dawud was uncertain—God will kill him tomorrow; his heart is turned upside down and his buttocks rise above him.' He said: I said: 'His lower part?' He said: 'His buttocks.'\""],[434,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stood among us and told us what will happen until the Day of Resurrection, except that I did not ask him: What will drive the people of Madinah out of Madinah?"],[435,"In the last days there will be people who say: There is no decree. If they fall ill, do not visit them, and if they die, do not attend them, for they are the party of the Dajjal, and it is incumbent upon God, Mighty and Majestic, to join them with him."],[436,"A man sat in the middle of the circle, and Hudhayfah said: Cursed upon the tongue of Muhammad ﷺ, or he said: The Messenger of God ﷺ cursed the one who sits in the middle of the circle."],[437,"A man came to Hudhayfah and said: Do you not see that so-and-so has died? He said: The One who caused him to die is able to cause you to die. Then he sat in the middle of the circle, so he said to him: Get up, for the Messenger of God ﷺ cursed the one who sits in the middle of the circle."],[438,"The Dajjal will come forth with him a river and a fire. Whoever enters his river, his burden of sin is incurred and his reward is removed, and whoever enters his fire, his reward is made incumbent and his burden of sin is removed."],[439,"We were sitting in the mosque with the Messenger of God ﷺ, and Bashir was a man who restrained his speech. Abu Thalabah came and said: O Bashir b. Sad, do you remember the hadith of the Messenger of God ﷺ about the rulers? Hudhayfah was sitting with Bashir, so Hudhayfah said: I remember his sermon. Abu Thalabah sat down, and Hudhayfah said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: You are in prophethood as long as God wills it to be, then He will remove it when He wills to remove it. Then there will be a caliphate upon the pattern of prophethood, and it will remain as long as God wills it to remain, then He will remove it when He wills to remove it. Then there will be a biting monarchy, and it will remain as long as God wills it to remain, then He will remove it when He wills to remove it. Then there will be tyranny, and it will remain as long as God wills it to remain, then He will remove it when He wills to remove it. Then there will be a caliphate upon the pattern of prophethood. Then he fell silent. He said: Then Umar arrived with Yazid b. al-Numan in his company, so I wrote to him reminding him of the hadith. I wrote to him: I hope that the Commander of the Faithful will be after the biting monarchy and the tyranny. He said: Yazid took the letter and brought it to Umar, and he was pleased with it and it delighted him."],[440,"The Hour will not come until you kill your imam, and you fight with your swords, and the worst of you inherit your world."],[441,"I have not seen any dwellings except dwellings that were with Muhammad ﷺ, nothing defends against this."],[442,"We said: O Messenger of God, if only you would appoint a successor. He said: If I appoint a successor and you disobey, punishment will descend upon you. But whatever Ibn Mas`ud recites to you, recite it, and whatever Hudhayfah tells you, accept it, or he said: listen to it."],[443,"I came to al-Yashkuri, and he said: What has brought you, O Banu Layth? He said: We said: We have come to ask you about the hadith of Hudhayfah. He said: Prices of animals rose, so we came to al-Kufah to bring animals from it. I said to my companion: I will enter the mosque, and if the market is open I will go out to it. I entered the mosque, and there was a circle as if their heads had been cut off, gathered around a man. I came and stood, and said: Who is this? He said: Are you from the people of al-Kufah? I said: No, rather from the people of al-Basrah. He said: If you were from the people of al-Kufah, you would not ask about this. This is Hudhayfah b. al-Yaman. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, is there after this good any evil? He said: O Hudhayfah, learn the Book of God and follow what is in it. I said: O Messenger of God, is there after this good any evil? He said: A truce upon corruption. I said: O Messenger of God, what is a truce upon corruption? He said: The hearts of people will not return to what they were upon. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Then there will be a blind and deaf tribulation, callers of misguidance - or he said: callers of the Fire - and for you to bite onto a stump - meaning a tree - is better for you than to follow any one of them."],[444,"Prices of animals rose, so we came to al-Kufah to bring animals from it. I entered the mosque, and there was a man, a tall man of fine teeth, known to be from the men of the Hijaz, and people craning their necks toward him. He said: Do not rush me, I will tell you. We had only recently been in ignorance, so when Islam came, I found a matter the like of which I had never seen before. God granted me understanding in the Quran, and the people used to ask the Messenger of God ﷺ about good, while I asked him about evil. I said: O Messenger of God, is there after this good any evil, as there was evil before it? He said: Yes. I said: What is the protection, O Messenger of God? He said: The sword. I said: Does the sword have any remainder? What comes after it? He said: There will be a truce upon corruption. He said: I said: What comes after the truce? He said: Callers of misguidance. If you see then a caliph of God, Mighty and Majestic, on earth, then cling to him, even if he strikes your back and takes your wealth. And if you do not see a caliph, then flee until death overtakes you while you are biting onto the stump of a tree. I said: O Messenger of God, what comes after that? He said: The Dajjal."],[445,"O Abu Dharr, give glad tidings to the people that whoever says: There is no god but God, enters Paradise."],[446,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was on a journey, and Bilal was with him. He wanted to announce the iqama, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Delay.' Then he wanted to announce the iqama, and he said: 'Delay.' Then he wanted to announce the iqama, and he said: 'Delay' three times—that is, for the noon prayer—until we saw the shade of the hillocks. Then he announced the iqama and the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed. Then he said: 'The intense heat is from the scorching breath of Hell, so delay the prayer.'"],[447,"The wealthy are the lowliest—or the poor—on the Day of Resurrection."],[448,"A bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, the hyena has devoured us.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'I fear for you from other than the hyena more than I do from the hyena, when the world is poured upon you in abundance. Would that my community would not wear gold.'"],[449,"There will be people from my community whose mark is the shaving of heads. They recite the Quran but it does not go beyond their throats. They pass through the religion—or through Islam—as an arrow passes through the game. They are the worst of creation and creatures."],[450,"There will be leaders who delay the prayer beyond its proper times. So pray the prayer at its time, then go to them. If they have already prayed, you will have secured your prayer; otherwise, pray with them and it will be a supererogatory prayer for you."],[451,"When you make a broth, increase its water, then look to a household among your neighbors and give them some of it kindly."],[452,"When Abu Dharr came to Uthman from Syria, he said: 'O Commander of the Believers, do you think that I am of a people—by God, I am not of them and shall not reach them—who recite the Quran but it does not pass their collarbones, who pass through Islam as an arrow passes through the game and do not return to it until the arrow returns to its notch? Their mark is the shaving of heads. By God, if you ordered me to stand, I would not sit as long as my legs could support me, and if you bound me with the two handles of a saddle, I would not loosen it until you are the one who loosens me.'"],[453,"The Messenger of God ﷺ commanded me to hear and obey, even if it be an Abyssinian slave with amputated limbs."],[454,"A man's prayer is cut off if there is not in front of him something like the back of a saddle—by a woman, a donkey, and a black dog. He said: I said to Abu Dharr: 'What about a black dog as opposed to a red one?' He said: 'O nephew, I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ just as you asked me, and he said: \"The black dog is a devil.\"'"],[455,"The Prophet ﷺ struck his thigh and said: 'How will you be when you remain among people who delay the prayer? So pray the prayer at its time, then go to them. If you are in the mosque when it is established, then pray with them.'"],[456,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, a man does a deed for his own sake, and people love him because of it?' He said: 'That is the immediate glad tidings for the believer.'"],[457,"I was between the Kaaba and its curtains when the Messenger of God ﷺ entered the mosque. He began with the Black Stone and touched it, then circumambulated the House seven times, and prayed behind the Maqam two units."],[458,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ when he had finished his prayer, and I said: Peace be upon you. He said: And upon you. He said: Thus I was the first to greet him with the greeting of Islam."],[459,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"How long have you been here?\" He said: I said: For thirty days and nights. He said: \"Thirty days and nights!\" I said: Yes. He said: \"Then what was your food?\" I said: I had no food or drink except the water of Zamzam, and I have grown fat until the folds of my belly have creased, and I do not find on my liver any weakness of hunger. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: \"It is blessed; it is food that nourishes and a cure for sickness.\""],[460,"I remained with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ as long as I remained. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"A land of palm trees has been shown to me, and I do not think it is other than Yathrib. Will you convey from me to your people what Allah may benefit them through you and reward you among them?\" I said: Yes. He said: So I set out and met Unays, who said to me: What have you done? I said: I have submitted and believed. He said: I have no desire to turn away from your religion, for I have submitted and believed. He said: We came to our mother and presented Islam to her. She said: I have no desire to turn away from the religion of you two, and she said: I have submitted and believed. He said: We came to our people and presented Islam to them. Half of them submitted, and the other half said: When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrives we will submit. He said: Ima' b. Rahada al-Ghifari used to lead them in prayer, and he was their chief. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to Madinah, the remaining half submitted. And our brothers from Aslam came and said: We submit on the same basis as our brothers from Ghifar. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"It is Ghifar; may Allah forgive it, and Aslam; may Allah keep it safe.\""],[461,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"O Abu Dharr,\" I said: At your service and at your pleasure, O Messenger of Allah. He said: \"How will you be when people are struck by hunger, and you come to your bed but cannot return to your mosque, and you come to your mosque but cannot return to your bed?\" He said: I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: \"Keep to chastity.\" He said: \"How will you be when people are struck by much death, so that a house - meaning a grave - will be for a servant?\" He said: I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: \"Keep to patience.\" Then he said: \"How will you be when you see the stones of al-Zayt sunk in blood?\" He said: I said: Allah and His Messenger know best, or: What Allah and His Messenger have chosen for me. He said: \"Keep to those you belong to,\" or \"Join those you belong to.\""],[462,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"O Abu Dharr, do you know where the sun goes when it sets?\" He said: I said: No. He said: \"It goes to the Throne and prostrates, and it is given permission to return. It was said to it: Return from where you came, so it returns from where it came. That is its resting place.\""],[463,"\"Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, even like a sandgrouse's nest, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise.\""],[464,"I said: O Messenger of Allah, which mosque was first set down for people? He said: \"The Sacred Mosque, then the Aqsa Mosque.\" He said: I said: How much was between them? He said: \"Forty years. And wherever the prayer overtakes you, pray, for that is a mosque.\""],[465,"From the Prophet ﷺ in what he relates from his Lord, Blessed and Exalted, he said: I have forbidden oppression for Myself and have forbidden it for My servants, so do not wrong one another. Every son of Adam errs by night and day, then he seeks My forgiveness and I forgive him, and I do not care."],[466,"\"A good deed is multiplied ten times, and an evil deed is counted once or I forgive it. Whoever meets Me with an earth-full of sin but does not associate anything with Me, I will meet him with an earth-full of forgiveness. Whoever intends a good deed but does not do it, a good deed is written for him. Whoever intends an evil deed but does not do it, nothing is written against him. Whoever draws near to Me a handspan, I draw near to him a cubit. Whoever draws near to Me a cubit, I draw near to him a fathom.\""],[467,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"It would not please me to have Mount Uhud in gold, and a third night pass while I have a dinar - or he said a mithqal - of it, except that I set it aside for a debtor.\""],[468,"We fasted Ramadan with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and he did not lead us in night prayer at all during the month, until the night of the twenty-fourth, the seventh remaining. He prayed with us until nearly a third of the night had passed. On the night of the twenty-fifth he did not pray with us. On the night of the twenty-sixth, the fifth remaining, he prayed with us until nearly half the night had passed. I said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would continue with us for the rest of our night. He said: \"No. When a man prays with the imam until he finishes, the standing of a whole night is written for him.\" On the night of the twenty-seventh he did not pray with us. On the night of the twenty-eighth, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ returned to his family and the people gathered for him, and he prayed with us until we almost missed the pre-dawn meal. Then, O son of my brother, he did not pray with us at all for the rest of the month."],[469,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: \"Three people Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection, nor speak to them, and they will have a painful punishment.\" I said: O Messenger of Allah, who are these? They have failed and lost. He said: \"The one who reminds others of his gifts, the one who lets his lower garment hang below his ankles, and the one who sells his goods by a false oath.\""],[470,"Talk would reach me from Abu Dharr, and I used to desire to meet him, so I met him and said: O Abu Dharr, talk used to reach me from you, and I used to desire to meet you. He said: May your father be devoted to God! You have indeed met me, so ask. I said: It has reached me that you relate that the Messenger of God ﷺ told you that God, Mighty and Majestic, loves three and hates three. He said: I do not think I would lie about my close friend. I said: Who are the three whom He loves? He said: A man who meets the enemy and fights, and you will indeed find that in the Book you have: God loves those who fight in His way in ranks. I said: And who? He said: A man who has a bad neighbor who harms him, and he bears his harm patiently, so God will suffice him against him through life or death. He said: And who? He said: A man who was with a group on a journey, and they stopped to rest at night, and sleep and drowsiness had weighed heavily upon them, so they laid down their heads and slept, while he got up, performed ablution, and prayed out of fear of God and desire for Him. I said: Who are the three whom God hates? He said: The miserly who reminds others of his favors, and the arrogant boaster, and you will indeed find in the Book of God: God does not love any arrogant boaster. He said: Who is the third? He said: The trader who swears much, or the seller who swears much."],[471,"Wiping the pebbles once, and that I not do it is dearer to me than a hundred black-eyed camels."],[472,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about everything, even wiping the pebbles. He said: Once."],[473,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said about things in which a man is rewarded, even in his having intercourse with his wife. It was said: O Messenger of God, how can that be when it is his desire that he fulfills? He said: Do you think that if he had done it unlawfully, he would not be burdened with sin? They said: Yes. He said: Thus, he is rewarded."],[474,"I was granted five things that no prophet before me was granted: the earth was made for me a mosque and a means of purification; I was aided with awe over my enemy for a month's journey; I was sent to the red and the black; spoils of war were made lawful for me, though they were not lawful for any prophet before me; and I was granted intercession, which is attainable for my community: whoever of them dies without associating anything with God."],[475,"Did the Messenger of God ﷺ shake hands with you when you met him? He said: He never met me except that he shook my hand. Once I came and was told that the Prophet ﷺ had asked for you, so I went to him, and he met me and embraced me, and that was better and better."],[476,"I said to Abu Dharr: If I had seen the Messenger of God ﷺ, I would have asked him about something. He said: What is it? I said: I would ask him: Did you see your Lord, Mighty and Majestic? Abu Dharr said: I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ: Did you see your Lord? He said: Light, how could I see Him?"],[477,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: O Abu Dharr, when you fast three days of the month, fast the thirteenth, fourteenth, and fifteenth."],[478,"When a man is in his prayer, mercy faces him, so let him not wipe the pebbles or gravel with his foot."],[479,"Whoever bathes on Friday, anoints himself with his oil, perfumes himself from the perfume of his house, then comes to the Friday prayer and does not separate two people, then prays, and when the imam speaks, listens and is silent, he will be forgiven what is between him and the next Friday."],[480,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was in the mosque and sat down with him. He said: O Abu Dharr. I said: At your service. He said: Have you prayed? I said: No. He said: Get up and pray. So I prayed, then came back and sat with him. He said: O Abu Dharr, have you sought refuge in God from the evil of the devils of the jinn and humans? I said: Are there devils among humans? He said: Yes, O Abu Dharr. Then he said to me: Shall I direct you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise? I said: Yes, O Messenger of God, may my father and mother be your ransom. He said: There is no might and no power except with God, for it is a treasure from the treasures of Paradise. I said: What about prayer, O Messenger of God? He said: A good thing established, so whoever wishes may do little and whoever wishes may do more. I said: What about fasting, O Messenger of God? He said: An obligatory duty that suffices. I said: What about charity, O Messenger of God? He said: Multiplied many times over, and with God is more. I said: Which of them is best? He said: Effort from one of little means, and secrecy to a poor person. I said: O Messenger of God, which verse that God sent down to you is greatest? He said: God, there is no deity but He, the Living, the Eternal. I said: Which of the prophets was first, O Messenger of God? He said: Adam. I said: Was he a prophet? He said: Yes, a prophet with whom God spoke. I said: How many were the messengers, O Messenger of God? He said: Three hundred and fifteen, a great multitude."],[481,"The Messenger of God ﷺ left us, and there is no bird flapping in the sky except that he mentioned to us some knowledge about it."],[482,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw two sheep butting each other, and said to me: 'O Abu Dharr, do you know why they are butting each other?' I said: 'No.' He said: 'But your Lord knows, and He will judge between them on the Day of Resurrection.'"],[483,"I swear by God, this verse—'These two opponents dispute concerning their Lord'—was revealed only about these six individuals: Hamzah, 'Ali, 'Ubaydah b. al-Harith, 'Utbah, Shaybah, and al-Walid b. 'Utbah."],[484,"We were at the gate of Mu'awiyah (may God have mercy on him), and Abu Dharr was with us. He mentioned that he was fasting. When we entered and the tables were set, Abu Dharr began to eat. He said: I looked at him, and he said: 'O Ahmar, what is wrong with you? Do you want to distract me from my food?' I said: 'Did you not tell us that you were fasting?' Or I said: 'Did you not claim that you were fasting?' He said: 'Yes.' Then he said to me: 'Have you read the Qur'an?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'Perhaps you have read the singular form but not the doubled reward: Whoever brings a good deed shall have ten times its like.' Then he said: 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Fasting the month of patience and three days of every month—I think he said: is the fasting of a lifetime, but this is what is certain—removes the malady of the chest.' He said: I said: 'What is the malady of the chest?' He said: 'The filth of Satan.'"],[485,"The deeds of my community—their good and their evil—were presented to me. I saw among their best deeds the removal of something harmful from the road, and I saw among their evil deeds the spittle in the mosque that is not buried."],[486,"I saw Abu Dharr in the mosque of Quba' praying, wearing a Qatari striped cloak. I greeted him, but he did not return my greeting. When he finished his prayer, he returned my greeting. I said: 'Are you Abu Dharr?' He said: 'Yes.' He said: 'I found the climate of Madinah unhealthy, so the Messenger of God ﷺ ordered for me a small herd of camels and commanded me to drink from their milk and their urine'—then Ayyub fell silent at 'their urine'—'and I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ among a group of his companions in the shade of the mosque. When he saw me, he said: \"O Abu Dharr.\" I said: \"I am ruined, O Messenger of God.\" He said: \"What has ruined you?\" or he said: \"What is that?\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, I am far from water and I become junub. Should I pray without wudu'?\" or he said: \"without purification?\" He called for water for me, and a black slave girl came with a wooden bowl containing water that was sloshing, not full. I concealed myself behind the camel and performed ghusl.' He said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: \"O Abu Dharr, pure earth is sufficient for you even if you do not find water for ten years, but when you find water, let it touch your skin.\""],[487,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, appoint me to a position of authority.' He said: 'O Abu Dharr, you are weak, and it is a trust. On the Day of Resurrection it will be disgrace and regret except for one who takes it with its right and fulfills what is due from him in it.'"],[488,"A man said: 'O Messenger of God, a man fights to be seen, and fights for reputation, and fights for booty—who is in the path of God?' He said: 'Whoever fights so that the word of God is supreme, he is in the path of God.'"],[489,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, a man fights to be mentioned, and fights to be seen, and fights for such-and-such—who is in the path of God?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever fights so that the word of God is highest, he is in the path of God.'"],[490,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ leaning on a staff and said: 'O Messenger of God, a man fights to be mentioned, and fights for such-and-such.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Whoever fights so that the word of God is supreme, he is in the path of God, Mighty and Majestic.'"],[491,"Feed the hungry, free the captive, and visit the sick."],[492,"God, Mighty and Majestic, spreads out His hand at night to accept the repentance of the one who sinned during the day, and during the day to accept the repentance of the one who sinned at night, until the sun rises from the west."],[493,"God, Mighty and Majestic, does not sleep, nor is it befitting for Him to sleep. He lowers the measure and raises it. The deeds of the night are raised to Him during the day, and the deeds of the day during the night. Al-Mas'udi added: 'His veil is fire; if He removed it, the splendors of His face would burn everything that His sight reaches.'"],[494,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ named himself to us with names, some of which we remembered. He said: 'I am Muhammad, Ahmad, al-Muqaffi, al-Hashir, the Prophet of repentance, and the Prophet of mercy.'"],[495,"We were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and we ascended a valley. When they descended into it, they raised their voices with takbir and tahlil, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on a mule. He said: 'O people, have mercy on yourselves. You are not calling upon one who is deaf or absent. You are calling upon One who is All-Hearing, All-Seeing.'"],[496,"The example of the believer who recites the Quran is like that of the citron: its fragrance is pleasant and its taste is pleasant. The example of the believer who does not recite the Quran is like that of the date: its taste is pleasant but it has no fragrance. The example of the wicked person who recites the Quran is like that of the sweet basil: its fragrance is pleasant but its taste is bitter. The example of the wicked person who does not recite the Quran is like that of the colocynth: its taste is bitter and its fragrance is bitter."],[497,"Upon every Muslim there is a charity due each day. They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what if he does not find anything?' He said: 'He works with his hands, benefits himself, and gives charity.' They said: 'What if he does not do that?' He said: 'He helps the needy person in distress.' They said: 'What if he is unable?' He said: 'He enjoins good and forbids evil.' They said: 'What if he is unable?' He said: 'Let him refrain from evil, for that is charity for him.'"],[498,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him and Mu'adh to Yemen and said to them: 'Cooperate with each other, make things easy and do not make them difficult, give glad tidings and do not repel.'"],[499,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, a drink is made among us from honey called bit', and a drink from barley called mizr, and both of them intoxicate.' The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Every intoxicant is forbidden.'"],[500,"Every intoxicant is forbidden."],[501,"No believer dies except that Allah admits into the Fire in his place a Jew or a Christian."],[502,"We came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ to ask him for mounts. He said: 'By Allah, I will not provide you with mounts, and I have nothing to mount you on.' Then he was brought some camels and mounted us on three with white foreheads. When we returned, I said to my companions: 'By Allah, Allah will not bless us. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ swore that he would not provide us with mounts. Let us go back.' We said: 'O Messenger of Allah, you swore that you would not provide us with mounts.' He said: 'I did not carry you; nothing carried you except Allah. By Allah—if Allah wills—I do not swear an oath and then see something better than it except that I expiate my oath and do that which is better.'"],[503,"If a man frees his slave woman and then gives her a new dowry, he will have two rewards."],[504,"Three people will be given their reward twice: a man who had a slave woman and disciplined her with good discipline, taught her with good teaching, then freed her and married her; a man from the People of the Book who believed in his prophet and then lived to see the Prophet ﷺ and believed in him; and a slave who fulfills the rights of Allah and the rights of his masters."],[505,"The believer to the believer is like a building, parts of it support other parts."],[506,"\"Many men have attained perfection, and none among women have attained perfection except Maryam bt. 'Imran and Asiyah the wife of Pharaoh. And the excellence of 'A'ishah over women is like the excellence of tharid over all other food.\""],[507,"That Humamah—a man from the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ—raided Isfahan with al-Ash'ari, and Isfahan was conquered in the time of 'Umar ؓ. He said: \"O Allah, Humamah claims that he loves to meet You. O Allah, if he is truthful, then make him steadfast in his truthfulness; and if he is lying, then impose it upon him even if he dislikes it. O Allah, do not return Humamah from this journey of his.\" Then he died in Isfahan. Al-Ash'ari stood up and said: \"O people, by Allah, based on what we heard from your Prophet ﷺ, and the extent of our knowledge is only that Humamah is a martyr.\""],[508,"\"Silk and gold have been made lawful for the females of my Ummah and forbidden for its males.\""],[509,"That when al-Ash'ari became gravely ill, his wife wept over him, and he said: \"Do you not know what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said?\" He (the narrator) said: I asked the woman afterwards: \"What did he say?\" She said: \"He is free from the one who shaves, wails, and tears.\""],[510,"When Allah, Mighty and Majestic, takes the son of a servant, He says to His angels: \"What did My servant say?\" They say: \"He praised You and said: 'Indeed we belong to Allah and to Him we shall return.'\" He says: \"Build a house for him and call it the House of Praise.\""],[511,"\"No one of this Ummah—nor any Jew or Christian—hears of me and then does not believe in me except that he will be among the people of the Fire.\""],[512,"\"Whoever plays with dice has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.\""],[513,"\"The fingers are equal.\" I said: \"For each finger, ten camels?\" He said: \"Yes.\""],[514,"Al-Ash'ari prayed the 'Isha' prayer with his companions while he was between Makkah and Madinah, then he prayed a rak'ah in which he recited one hundred verses from al-Nisa' or al-Baqarah. It was said to him: \"What is this?\" He said: \"I did not fail to place my feet where the Messenger of Allah ﷺ placed his, and to do what he did.\""],[515,"\"Whoever fasts the whole year, Hellfire will be constricted for him like this,\" and he tied a knot with ninety."],[516,"\"Whoever fasts the whole year, Hellfire will be constricted for him like this,\" and he tied a knot with ninety."],[517,"\"The example of a righteous companion is like that of a perfume seller: if he does not give you some of his perfume, you will still get some of its fragrance. And the example of an evil companion is like that of a blacksmith: if his fire does not touch you, you will still get some of its smoke.\""],[518,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ while he was making his camel kneel at al-Batḥāʾ. He said to me, \"How did you enter iḥrām?\" I said, \"Labbayka with an iḥrām like the iḥrām of the Prophet ﷺ.\" He said, \"You have done well. Perform ṭawāf around the House and between al-Ṣafā and al-Marwah, then exit iḥrām.\" I did so, and I went to a woman of Banū Qays who removed lice from my head. I began giving fatwās to people accordingly. A man said to me, \"O ʿAbd Allāh b. Qays, go slowly with some of your fatwās, for you do not know what the Commander of the Believers has introduced concerning the rites after you.\" I said, \"Whoever I gave a fatwā to, let him go slowly, for the Commander of the Believers is coming to you, so follow him.\" Then he arrived, and I went to him and mentioned that to him. He said, \"If we follow the Book of God, the Book of God commands us to complete; if we follow the Sunnah of the Messenger of God ﷺ, the Messenger of God ﷺ did not exit iḥrām until the sacrificial animal reached its place.\""],[519,"Al-Ashʿarī prayed with his companions. When he sat in his prayer, a man behind him said, \"Prayer has been coupled with righteousness and zakāh.\" When al-Ashʿarī finished his prayer, he said, \"Which of you said such-and-such words?\" The people remained silent. He said, \"O Ḥiṭṭān, perhaps you said it.\" I said, \"I did not say it, but I feared you would rebuke me for it.\" Al-Ashʿarī said, \"Do you not know what you say in your prayer? The Messenger of God ﷺ addressed us and taught us our Sunnah and explained to us our prayer. He said: 'Straighten your rows, then let one of you lead you. When the imām says takbīr, say takbīr. When he says \"wa-lā al-ḍāllīn,\" say \"āmīn,\" and God will answer you. When he bows, bow, for the imām bows before you and rises before you.' The Prophet of God ﷺ said, 'That is for that.' When he says, 'Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah,' say, 'Allāhumma Rabbanā laka al-ḥamd,' and God will hear you, for God, Mighty and Majestic, said on the tongue of His Prophet ﷺ, 'Samiʿa Allāhu li-man ḥamidah.' When he says takbīr and prostrates, say takbīr and prostrate, for the imām prostrates before you and rises before you.' The Prophet of God ﷺ said, 'That is for that.' When it is time for the sitting, let the first thing one of you says be: 'Al-taḥiyyātu li-llāhi, al-ṭayyibātu al-ṣalawātu li-llāhi, al-salāmu ʿalayka ayyuhā al-nabiyyu wa-raḥmatu Allāhi, al-salāmu ʿalaynā wa-ʿalā ʿibādi Allāhi al-ṣāliḥīn, ashhadu an lā ilāha illā Allāhu wa-anna Muḥammadan ʿabduhu wa-rasūluhu.'\""],[520,"Al-Ashʿarī sought permission to enter upon ʿUmar three times, but he did not grant him permission, so he turned back. ʿUmar sent to him, \"What made you go back?\" He said, \"I sought permission three times and was not granted permission, and I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, 'If one seeking permission asks three times and is not granted permission, let him go back.'\" ʿUmar said, \"You must bring me someone who knows this, or I will do such-and-such to you.\" Abū Saʿīd said, \"Al-Ashʿarī came to me trembling, his face turned yellow. He stood at a circle of the Prophet's ﷺ companions and said, 'I adjure by God, any man who knows anything about this must stand up for it, for I fear this man for myself.' I said, 'I am with you.' Another said, 'And I am with you.' So he was relieved.\""],[521,"I heard a black man, who had come to Baṣrah with Ibn ʿAbbās, say: \"When Ibn ʿAbbās came to Baṣrah, he was told of ḥadīths from Abū Mūsā, from the Prophet ﷺ. Ibn ʿAbbās wrote to him asking about them. Al-Ashʿarī wrote back to him: 'You are a man of your time, and I did not relate anything from the Prophet ﷺ of those, except that I was with the Messenger of God ﷺ when he wanted to urinate. He turned to a soft spot by a wall and urinated, and said, \"The Children of Israel, when urine touched any of them, would cut it off with scissors.\"'\" Abū Saʿīd said, \"So if any of you wants to urinate, let him prepare for his urine.\""],[522,"\"If you have arrows with you, take them by their points so you do not wound a Muslim or tear his garment.\" Al-Ashʿarī said, \"And these people are commanding me to point them at the pupils of the Muslims' eyes.\""],[523,"A funeral procession passed by the Prophet ﷺ while they were walking quickly with it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Let there be tranquility upon you.\""],[524,"A funeral procession was brought past the Prophet ﷺ while it was being hastened, and it was shaking like a water-skin. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Keep to a moderate pace in walking with your funerals.\""],[525,"\"There is no marriage except with a guardian.\""],[526,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ supplicated against a people, he would say, \"O God, I place You at their throats, and I seek refuge in You from their evils.\""],[527,"\"If you had seen us with our Prophet ﷺ when rain fell on us, you would have compared our smell to nothing but the smell of sheep.\""],[528,"ʿUmar met Asmāʾ bt. ʿUmays and said, \"What a good people you are, were it not that we preceded you in emigration.\" She mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"Rather, you have emigration twice: emigration to the land of Abyssinia and emigration to Madinah.\""],[529,"A man used to say, \"I have divorced you; I have taken you back.\" That reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said, \"What is the matter with men who play with the limits of God?\""],[530,"When the funeral procession of a Muslim man, or a Jew, or a Christian passes by you, stand up for it; for we do not stand up for it, but we stand up for the angels who are with it."],[531,"The gardens of al-Firdaws are four: two gardens of gold, their ornaments, vessels, and whatever is in them, and two gardens of silver, their ornaments, vessels, and whatever is in them. And between them and seeing their Lord, Mighty and Majestic, there is only the cloak of pride on His face in the Garden of Eden. Then it splits into rivers in a hollow in the Garden of Eden, then it splits in the garden into rivers."],[532,"Paradise is under the shade of the swords."],[533,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with two men from my people, and we reached him while he had a toothstick with which he was cleaning his teeth. They asked him for an appointment to office, so he said: O Abu Musa, is it for this that you have come? He said: I said: By God, O Messenger of God, it is not for this that I came, and they did not inform me of what was in their minds. He said: Then I saw him raise his upper lip with his toothstick and say: By God, we do not give it to one who asks for it from among you. Then he sent me and left the two of them."],[534,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and I did not consider Ibn Mas'ud to be other than from his family because of his kindness to them."],[535,"Al-Ash'ari addressed us from the pulpit of al-Basra and said: Verily, the wine that was forbidden in al-Madinah is the mixture of unripe dates and dried dates."],[536,"The demise of my community will be by stabbing and the plague. They said: O Messenger of God, this stabbing we have known, but what is the plague? He said: A stabbing by your enemies from the jinn, and in each there is martyrdom."],[537,"By the One in whose hand is my soul, indeed al-ma'ruf (the good) and al-munkar (the evil) are two creatures that will be set up for people on the Day of Resurrection. As for al-ma'ruf, it will promise its people good and congratulate them; and as for al-munkar, it will say: Get away from you, get away from you, and they will be able to do nothing but cling to it."],[538,"The Prophet ﷺ made him recite: that it sets in a spring of black mud."],[539,"A time came upon me when I used to say: The children of the Muslims are with the Muslims, and the children of the polytheists are with the polytheists, until..."],[540,"The boy whom al-Khidr ﷺ killed was created an unbeliever, and a love from him was cast upon his parents."],[541,"Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me to recite the Qur'an to you. He said: Then he recited to him: \"Lam yakun\" and he recited to him: \"Indeed, the custom of the religion with Allah is the Hanifiyyah, not the polytheistic, nor the Jewish, nor the Christian, and whoever does good, it will never be denied to him.\" And he recited to him: \"If the son of Adam had a valley, he would seek a second to it; and if he were given a second, he would seek a third to it; and nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam except dust, and Allah turns in mercy to whoever repents.\""],[542,"O Zirr, how many verses do you read in Surah al-Ahzab? He said: I said: Such-and-such verses. He said: It used to rival Surah al-Baqarah, and we used to recite in it: \"And the old man and the old woman, if they commit adultery, stone them both absolutely, as a punishment from Allah and His Messenger.\" Then it was lifted among what was lifted."],[543,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about them, and he said: \"It was said to me, so I said to you, so say.\" Ubayy said: Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to us while we were saying."],[544,"\"Were it not for fear of your authority, I would place my hands over my ears and then call out: Indeed, the Night of Decree is in the last ten, in the seven, before it three and after it three—a report from one who has not belied me, from a report of one who has not belied him.\""],[545,"That Gabriel ﷺ came to the Prophet ﷺ at the stones of al-Mira', and he said to him: O Gabriel, I have been sent to an unlettered nation, among them the old woman, the old man, the boy, the girl, and the harsh man who has never read a book at all. He said: Then Gabriel said: The Qur'an was sent down in seven modes."],[546,"The Dajjal was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ — or he said: The Prophet ﷺ mentioned the Dajjal — and he said: \"One of his eyes is like a green glass, and seek refuge in Allah from the punishment of the grave.\""],[547,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ taught me to recite, so in that let them rejoice.\""],[548,"That the Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the Witr: \"Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High,\" and \"Say: O disbelievers,\" and \"Say: He is Allah, the One.\" Then when he said the salam, he said: \"Glory be to the King, the Holy\" three times, raising his voice on the third."],[549,"\"For ablution there is a devil called al-Walahan, so beware of him,\" or he said: \"so fear him.\""],[550,"\"Indeed, the food of the son of Adam has been struck as a parable for the world, even if he salts and seasons it.\""],[551,"\"When death came to Adam ﷺ , he said: O my sons, I long for fruit of Paradise. So his sons went seeking, and they saw the angels, and they said: Where are you heading, O sons of Adam? They said: Our father has longed for fruit of Paradise, so we went to seek that for him. They said: Return, for the taking of your father's soul has been commanded. So they came back until they reached Adam ﷺ . When Hawwa' saw them, she recognized them, and she clung to Adam. He said: Away from me, for it is from your side that I have been brought to this; leave me with the angels of my Lord. He said: Then they took his soul while they watched, and they washed him while they watched, and they shrouded him while they watched, and they embalmed him while they watched, and they prayed over him. Then they turned to them and said: O sons of Adam, this is your sunnah for your dead, and this is your way.\""],[552,"\"O Abu al-Mundhir, which verse in the Book of Allah is the greatest?\" I said: The Verse of the Throne. He said to me: \"May knowledge be pleasurable to you, Abu al-Mundhir; by the One in whose hand is my soul, it has a tongue on the Day of Resurrection that glorifies Allah at the leg of the Throne.\""],[553,"There was a man from my close kin, and his house was the farthest house in Madinah. He said: Abu Uthman said, while he was narrating among the elders: What is between you and the bridge, or farther. He said: Asim said: I mentioned that to Muhammad b. Sirin, and he said: If it was the farthest house in Madinah, then it is farther than the bridge. Then at the end of that he said: I had only been seeking the reward for (walking) the distance. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: You shall have what you sought."],[554,"I set out early with Zayd b. Suhan and Salman b. Rabi'ah, and I found a whip and picked it up. They said to me: Throw it down. I said: No, but I will announce it; if I find someone who recognizes it, (good), otherwise I will make use of it. I refused them both. When we returned from our military expedition, it was decreed for me that I performed Hajj. So I came to Madinah and met Ubayy b. Ka'b. I told him about the matter of the whip and what they had said. Ubayy b. Ka'b said: I found a purse containing one hundred dinars at the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: Announce it for a year. I announced it, but found no one who recognized it, three times. He said: Keep note of its count, its tie, and its container; if its owner comes, (give it to him), otherwise make use of it. He said: So I made use of it. Shu'bah said: I met Salamah after that and he said: I do not know whether it was three years or one year. This hadith pleased me, so I said to Abu Sadiq: Come and hear it from him."],[555,"He used to observe i'tikaf during the last ten days of Ramadan. Then he traveled one year and did not observe i'tikaf. The following year, he observed i'tikaf for twenty days."],[556,"The Messenger of God ﷺ led us in prayer and said: Is so-and-so present? They said: No. He said: These two prayers – meaning 'Isha' and Fajr – are the heaviest upon the hypocrites. If they knew what was in them, they would come to them even if they had to crawl. The first row is like the row of the angels. If you knew its excellence, you would race to it. A man's prayer with another man is purer than his prayer alone, and his prayer with two men is purer than his prayer with one man. Whatever is more is more beloved to God, Mighty and Majestic."],[557,"I came to Madinah to meet the companions of Muhammad ﷺ, and there was no one among them I was more eager to meet than Ubayy b. Ka'b. I stood in the first row, and Umar came out with the companions of Muhammad ﷺ. Then a man came and looked at the faces of the people and recognized them, except me. He moved me aside and stood in my place. I did not understand my prayer. When he had prayed, he said to me: Young man, may God not grieve you. I did not do what I did out of ignorance, but the Messenger of God ﷺ said to us: Be in the row that is closest to me. I looked at the faces of the people and recognized them, except you. Then he began to speak, and I have never seen men stretch their necks toward anything as they stretched them toward him. I heard him say: The people of the knot have perished, by the Lord of the Ka'bah – he said it three times – they have perished and caused others to perish. Indeed, I do not grieve for them, but I grieve for those Muslims whom they cause to perish. And that man was Ubayy b. Ka'b."],[558,"Some poetry contains wisdom."],[559,"The Prophet ﷺ was at the water of Banu Ghifar when Jibril ﷺ came to him and said: God, Mighty and Majestic, commands you to teach your community the Qur'an according to one harf. He said: I ask God for His pardon and forgiveness, for my community cannot bear that. Then he came to him a second time and said: God, Mighty and Majestic, commands you to teach your community the Qur'an according to two harfs. He said: I ask God for His pardon and forgiveness, for my community cannot bear that. Then he came to him a third time and said: God commands you to teach your community the Qur'an according to three harfs. He said: I ask God for His pardon and forgiveness, for my community cannot bear that. Then he came a fourth time and said: God commands you to teach your community the Qur'an according to seven harfs. Whichever harf they recite according to, they have hit the mark."],[560,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ sent Mu'adh to Yemen, he said to him: How will you judge if a case is presented to you? He said: I will judge by the Book of God. He said: And if you do not find it in the Book of God? He said: I will judge by the Sunnah of the Messenger of God ﷺ. He said: And if you do not find it in the Sunnah of the Messenger of God? He said: I will exert my own judgment and spare no effort. He said: Then he struck his hand on my chest and said: Praise be to God who has guided the messenger of the Messenger of God ﷺ to what pleases the Messenger of God."],[561,"O Messenger of God, tell me of a deed that will admit me into Paradise. He said: Excellent, excellent! You have asked about something great, yet it is easy for the one for whom God makes it easy. Perform the prescribed prayer, give the obligatory zakah. Shall I not tell you of the head of the matter, its pillar, and its highest peak? The head of the matter is Islam; whoever submits is safe. Its pillar is prayer, and its highest peak is jihad in the path of God. Shall I not point you to the gates of goodness? Fasting is a shield, charity extinguishes sin, and a servant's standing in the depths of the night. Then he recited: 'Their sides forsake their beds...' to the end of the verse. Shall I not tell you of what controls all of that? He said: Then a rider or a band of riders appeared, and the Messenger of God ﷺ pointed with his hand to his tongue. I said: Will we be held accountable for what we say with our tongues? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: May your mother be bereaved of you, O Mu'adh! Is there anything that casts people on their faces into the Fire except the harvests of their tongues?"],[562,"As long as you remain silent, you are safe. When you speak, it is either for you or against you."],[563,"The one with three has made it obligatory. Mu'adh said: I said: O Messenger of God, and the one with two? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: And the one with two. He said: meaning the one who has sent ahead three of his children."],[564,"Whoever sleeps in a state of purity and then wakes during the night, and asks God for anything of the affairs of the Hereafter or this world, He will give it to him. Thabit said: Then the man came to us who..."],[565,"If you wish, I will tell you the first thing that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will say to the believers on the Day of Resurrection, and the first thing they will say. They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: He will say to the believers: \"Did you love to meet Me?\" They will say: Yes, our Lord. He will say: \"Why?\" They will say: We hoped for Your pardon and Your mercy. He will say: \"I have made My mercy incumbent upon you.\""],[566,"\"Do you know what Allah's right upon His servants is?\" He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: \"Allah's right upon His servants is that they worship Him and do not associate anything with Him, and their right upon Allah, Mighty and Majestic, if they do that, is that He will not punish them.\""],[567,"That the Prophet ﷺ came to Madinah and prayed facing Jerusalem for seventeen months, then this verse was revealed to him: \"We have certainly seen the turning of your face toward the heaven...\" to the end of the verse. He said: So Allah turned him toward the Kaaba."],[568,"That when the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent Mu'adh to Yemen, he commanded him to take from every adult a dinar or its equivalent in Ma'afir cloth."],[569,"Mu'adh b. Jabal was brought a case of a man who had died upon other than Islam and left behind his son as a Muslim, so Mu'adh made him inherit from him, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Islam increases and does not decrease."],[570,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined in an expedition he undertook—and that was in the expedition of Tabuk—between Zuhr and 'Asr, and between Maghrib and 'Isha'.\" He said: I said: What did he intend by that? He said: He intended not to cause hardship for his community."],[571,"Two men insulted each other in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and one of them became so angry that his nose seemed to split from anger. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Indeed, I know a word which, if he were to say it, his anger would depart: I seek refuge in Allah from Satan the accursed.\""],[572,"I entered the mosque and there were about twenty of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ in it, and among them was a man with dark, wide eyes and brilliant front teeth. Whenever they differed about something, he would state an opinion and they would adopt his opinion. I asked about him and found he was Mu'adh b. Jabal. The next day I entered the mosque and found him standing praying toward a pillar. I sat close to him, and when I did that he shortened his prayer. I said: By Allah, I love you for the sake of Allah's majesty. He said: \"By Allah?\" I said: By Allah. He said: \"Those who love one another for the sake of Allah's majesty will be in Allah's shade—I think he said on the Day of Resurrection—on the Day when there is no shade except His shade. The prophets, martyrs, and righteous will envy them for their nearness to Allah.\""],[573,"I will only tell you what I heard from the tongue of Muhammad ﷺ: My love is due for those who love one another for My sake, My love is due for those who maintain ties for My sake, My love is due for those who are sincere to one another for My sake—or he said: My love is due for those who give to one another for My sake."],[574,"As for me, I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Gabriel ﷺ came to me from Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and said: O Muhammad, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, says: I have made five prayers obligatory upon your community. Whoever fulfills them with their ablution, their times, their bowing, and their prostration, then he has a covenant with Me that I will admit him to Paradise by them. And whoever meets Me having neglected any of that—or a word like it—then he has no covenant with Me; if I will, I punish him, and if I will, I have mercy on him."],[575,"Whoever loves to meet Allah, Allah loves to meet him, and whoever hates to meet Allah, Allah hates to meet him."],[576,"The dream of a believer is one part of forty-six parts of prophethood."],[577,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out intending to inform his companions of the Night of Decree, but two men argued, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"I went out intending to inform you of the Night of Decree, but two men argued, and it was withdrawn from me. So seek it in the last ten nights: in the seventh remaining, or the ninth remaining, or the fifth remaining.\""],[578,"\"My dear son, fear God, and know that you will never fear God until you believe in God and believe in the decree, all of it, its good and its evil. If you die upon other than this, you will enter the Fire. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'The first thing God created was the Pen. He said, \"Write.\" It said, \"My Lord, what shall I write?\" He said, \"Write the decree: what has been and what will be forever.\"'\""],[579,"\"And the woman who dies in childbirth, her child will drag her on the Day of Resurrection by her umbilical cord to Paradise.\""],[580,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ took a pledge from us as he took from the women: that we would not associate anything with God, would not steal, would not commit adultery, would not kill our children, and would not disobey him in what is right. Whoever among you commits a violation of what was forbidden and is punished for it, that is an expiation for him. Whoever is deferred, his affair is with God, Mighty and Majestic: if He wills, He will punish him, and if He wills, He will forgive him.\""],[581,"\"None of you should slander one another.\""],[582,"\"Silver for silver, gold for gold, dates for dates, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, salt for salt, equal for equal,\" or he said: \"weight for weight.\" Thus al-Rabī' narrated it."],[583,"The Prophet ﷺ visited 'Abd Allāh b. Rawāḥah, and he did not make room for him on his bed. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"What do you count as the martyrs of my community?\" He said: \"Those killed in the path of God.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Then the martyrs of my community would be few. Being killed is martyrdom, the plague is martyrdom, stomach disease is martyrdom, and a woman killed by her child in childbirth is martyrdom.\""],[584,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ about the saying of God, Mighty and Majestic: \"For them are good tidings in the life of this world and in the Hereafter.\" He said: \"It is the righteous dream that a Muslim man sees or is seen for him.\""],[585,"When revelation descended upon the Messenger of God ﷺ, it was recognizable in him. When the verse \"or until God makes for them a way\" was revealed, and when the revelation lifted, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Take, take. God has made a way for them: the virgin with the virgin, one hundred lashes and banishment for a year; the previously married with the previously married, one hundred lashes and stoning with stones.\""],[586,"\"When a man performs the prayer well and completes its bowing and prostration, the prayer says: 'May God preserve you as you have preserved me,' and it is raised up. When he performs the prayer poorly and does not complete its bowing and prostration, the prayer says: 'May God waste you as you have wasted me,' and it is folded up like an old garment is folded, and it is struck with it upon his face.\""],[587,"\"Some people of my community will drink wine, calling it by other than its name.\""],[588,"\"Whoever is afflicted in his body by the amount of half his blood money and pardons, half of his sins will be expiated for him, and if it is a third or a quarter, then according to that amount.\" A man said: \"By Allah, did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ?\" 'Ubadah said: \"By Allah, I heard it from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.\""],[589,"The Prophet ﷺ went out at sunset and heard a sound, so he said: \"The Jews are being punished in their graves.\""],[590,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed with Abu Ayyub al-Ansari. When he ate some food, he would send him the leftovers, and he would look at the place where the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ hand had been and put his own hand there. One day he sent him some food, and he did not see in it the trace of the Messenger of Allah's ﷺ fingers. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, I did not see the trace of your fingers.\" He said: \"There was garlic in it.\" Shu'bah said in his hadith: \"Is it forbidden?\" The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"No.\" Hammad said in his hadith: \"O Messenger of Allah, you sent me back what you did not eat.\" He said: \"You are not like me; an angel comes to me, and I am not like you.\""],[591,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined—meaning at Muzdalifah—Maghrib and 'Isha'.\""],[592,"\"When one of you sneezes, let him say: 'Praise be to Allah in every situation,' and let the one who responds to him say: 'May Allah have mercy on you all,' and let him say: 'May Allah guide you all and set your affairs aright.'\""],[593,"\"It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days; they meet and this one turns away and this one turns away, and the best of them is the one who initiates the greeting.\""],[594,"He said: \"Witr is a duty or an obligation. Whoever wishes may perform witr with seven, and whoever wishes may perform witr with five, and whoever wishes may perform witr with three, and whoever wishes may perform witr with one. Whoever is overcome, let him gesture.\""],[595,"\"Whoever fasts Ramadan and then follows it with six from Shawwal, that is the fasting of the year.\""],[596,"The Prophet ﷺ \"forbade confining an animal to shoot it.\" Abu Ayyub said: \"Even if it were a chicken, I would not confine it.\" 'Abd al-Rahman—who had killed four 'iljs—when he heard this hadith, freed four slaves."],[597,"I came to Abu Ayyub al-Azdi and shook his hand, and he saw that my fingernails were long. He said: \"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ asking him, and he said: 'One of them asks me about the news of heaven, while he leaves his fingernails like the talons of birds, in which impurity and dirt collect.'\""],[598,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stayed with me, and he used to pray four rak'ahs before Zuhr. I asked him about that, and he said: \"The gates of heaven are opened and are not closed until Zuhr is prayed.\" He said: I said: \"O Messenger of Allah, do you say the taslim between them?\" He said: \"No, except at the end of them.\""],[599,"\"O Abu Ayyub, shall I not guide you to a charity whose place Allah and His Messenger approve of?\" He said: \"Yes.\" He said: \"You reconcile between people when they have become corrupt, and bring them close when they have become distant.\""],[600,"We were at Constantinople, with Fadala b. Ubayd al-Ansari in command of the people of Syria and Uqba b. Amir al-Juhani in command of the people of Egypt. A great rank of the Byzantines came out against us, and a great rank of the Muslims went out against them. A man from the Muslims charged the Byzantine rank and fought among them, then came back. The people shouted and said, \"Glory be to God! He has thrown himself into destruction.\" Abu Ayyub al-Ansari stood up and said, \"O people, you are interpreting this verse other than its proper interpretation. This verse was revealed concerning us, the Ansar. When God, Mighty and Majestic, made His religion mighty and increased its supporters, we said among ourselves secretly from the Messenger of God ﷺ, 'Our wealth has been lost; if only we could stay with it and repair what has been lost of it.' Then God, Mighty and Majestic, sent down this verse to refute what we had resolved in ourselves, to stay with our wealth and repair what had been lost of it. The destruction we intended to do was that, and we were commanded to go on expeditions.\" Abu Ayyub kept going on expeditions until God, Mighty and Majestic, took him."],[601,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray Maghrib at the breaking of the fast of the fasting person, hastening before the rising of the star."],[602,"When this verse was revealed, \"When the help of God comes, and the victory,\" the Messenger of God ﷺ recited it to its end, then said, \"I and my companions are one side, and the people are another side. There is no emigration after the victory.\" Abu Said said: I narrated this hadith to Marwan b. al-Hakam—who was governor over Madinah—and he said, \"You have lied,\" while Zayd b. Thabit and Zayd b. Arqam were with him. I said, \"If these two wished, they would tell you, but this one fears that you would remove him from the charity, and this one fears that you would remove him from the leadership of his people.\" He raised the whip against me, and when they saw that, they said, \"He has spoken the truth.\""],[603,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ died, the orators of the Ansar stood up. Some of them began to say, \"O company of the Emigrants, when the Messenger of God ﷺ sent one of you, he paired him with one of us. We think that this matter should be undertaken by two men: a man from you and a man from us.\" Zayd b. Thabit stood up and said, \"The Messenger of God ﷺ was from the Emigrants, and we were the supporters of the Messenger of God ﷺ. The imam will be from the Emigrants, and we will be his supporters, just as we were the supporters of the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" Abu Bakr, may God have mercy on him, said, \"May God reward you, O company of the Ansar, with good, and make firm your speaker. By God, if you had said other than this, we would not have made peace with you.\""],[604,"We had the pre-dawn meal with the Messenger of God ﷺ, then we went out to the prayer."],[605,"The Messenger of God ﷺ looked toward Yemen and said, \"O God, turn their hearts.\" Then he looked toward Syria and said, \"O God, turn their hearts.\" Then he looked toward Iraq and said, \"O God, turn their hearts, and bless us in our sa' and our mudd.\""],[606,"I walked with Anas, and he began to shorten his steps. He said, \"O Thabit, why don't you ask me why I am doing this to you?\" He said, \"Why are you doing it?\" He said, \"I walked with Zayd b. Thabit, and he did the same to me, and said, 'Why don't you ask me why I am doing this to you?'\" He said, \"So I asked him, and Zayd said, 'This is how the Messenger of God ﷺ did with me, and he said to me, \"O Zayd, do you know why I am doing this to you?\" I said, \"Why did you do it?\" He said, \"I wanted our steps to the mosque to be many.\"'\""],[607,"When he went out to Uhud, a group of those who were with him turned back. The companions of the Prophet ﷺ became two factions concerning them: a faction saying, \"We should kill them,\" and a faction saying, \"No.\" Then this verse was revealed: \"What is the matter with you, that you are two factions concerning the hypocrites, while God has cast them back for what they earned\"—the whole verse."],[608,"It is Tayba, and it expels its dross just as fire expels the dross of silver."],[609,"Abu Bakr ؓ sent for me after the battle of the people of Yamama, and Umar b. al-Khattab ؓ was with him. He said, \"This one came to me and informed me that the killing has intensified among the reciters of the Quran—meaning on the day of Yamama—and I fear that the killing will intensify among the reciters of the Quran in other places, and the Quran will be lost. I think you should collect it.\" I said, \"How can you do something the Messenger of God ﷺ did not do?\" By God, if they had tasked me with moving a mountain, it would have been dearer to me than what they tasked me with."],[610,"I missed a verse I used to hear the Messenger of God ﷺ recite. I searched for it and found it with Khuzayma b. Thabit: \"Among the believers are men who have been true to what they pledged to God.\" I appended it to its surah."],[611,"This wealth is green and sweet, so do not sell fruits until their ripeness appears."],[612,"\"I missed a verse I used to hear the Messenger of God ﷺ recite, so I searched for it and found it with Khuzayma b. Thabit: 'There has come to you a Messenger from among yourselves' — the verse — so I inserted it into its surah.\""],[613,"Wadi'a al-Ansari sent me to Zayd b. Thabit to ask him about the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ in times of fear. I went to him and asked him, and he related that the Messenger of God ﷺ prayed with his companions, dividing them into two groups: one group facing their enemy and one group facing him. He prayed one rak'a with those who were with him, then they went to the positions of their brothers, and then the others came and he prayed one rak'a with them. Thus the Messenger of God ﷺ had two rak'as, and the people had one rak'a each."],[614,"\"I recited 'The Star' to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he did not prostrate in it.\""],[615,"They were writing the masahif in the presence of Zayd b. Thabit, and they came to this verse, so Zayd b. Thabit said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'As for the old man and the old woman, when they commit adultery, stone them absolutely as a punishment from God and His Messenger.'"],[616,"\"Three things on which the heart of a Muslim does not harbor deceit: sincerity of action for God, Mighty and Majestic, giving sincere counsel to those in authority, and adhering to the community; for their supplication encompasses those behind them.\""],[617,"\"Whoever's intention is this world, God, Mighty and Majestic, scatters his affairs, places poverty before his eyes, and nothing of this world comes to him except what has been decreed for him. Whoever's intention is the Hereafter, God, Mighty and Majestic, places richness in his heart, gathers his affairs for him, and this world comes to him submissively.\""],[618,"\"May God brighten a person who hears from us a hadith and memorizes it until he conveys it. For perhaps a bearer of understanding carries it to one who has more understanding than him, and perhaps a bearer of understanding is not himself a faqih.\""],[619,"\"Indeed, if God, Mighty and Majestic, were to punish the inhabitants of His heavens and the inhabitants of His earth, He would punish them without wronging them. If He were to have mercy on them, His mercy would be better for them than their deeds. If you had the like of Uhud in gold and spent it in the path of God, it would not be accepted from you until you believe in the divine decree, all of it, its good and its evil. If you die upon other than this, you will enter the Fire.\""],[620,"\"'Umra belongs to the heir,\" or he said, \"its way is the way of inheritance.\""],[621,"\"When one of you goes to relieve himself, let him not clean himself with his right hand, nor touch his private part with his right hand.\""],[622,"\"When the call to prayer is given, do not stand until you see me.\""],[623,"\"When the prayer is established, do not stand until you see me, for I have come.\""],[624,"\"Do not soak dates and raisins together, but soak each of them separately.\""],[625,"\"The Prophet ﷺ would breathe into the vessel, or he would breathe three times, three times.\""],[626,"\"The Prophet ﷺ used to recite in the first two rak'ahs of Zuhr and 'Asr, sometimes letting us hear a verse, and he would make the first rak'ah long and the second shorter, and he would recite in the two rak'ahs of Maghrib.\""],[627,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave a sermon and mentioned jihad, and he did not prefer anything over it except the prescribed prayers.\""],[628,"A man stood up and said: \"O Messenger of Allah, tell me, if I am killed in the path of Allah, where will I be?\" He said: \"If you are killed in the path of Allah, patient and seeking reward, advancing and not retreating, then you will be in Paradise.\" Then he fell silent, and we thought that revelation was coming down upon him. Then he said: \"Where is the man?\" He said: \"Here I am.\" He said: \"Unless he has a debt, for he will be held accountable for it. Thus Jibril ﷺ asserted.\""],[629,"When a funeral was brought to him, he would ask about it. If it was praised well, he would pray over it; if it was spoken of badly, he would say to its family: \"Take care of it yourselves,\" and would not pray over it."],[630,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent him out as a scout while his companions were in ihram, and he was not in ihram. He said: We saw a wild donkey, and I asked them to lend me a whip, but they refused to lend me, so I snatched it from one of them. I caught it and slaughtered it. They refused to eat with me, so they went to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, we did something we do not know what it is. They told him, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"Eat, and feed us.\""],[631,"He went with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ in the year of Hudaybiyyah. My companions entered ihram, but I did not. The Prophet ﷺ went on, and I was with my companions. Some of them began to laugh at each other, so I looked and saw a wild donkey. I charged at it, stabbed it, and brought it down. I sought their help, but they refused to help me. We ate from it, and I feared that my people would be cut off, so I went urging my horse, seeking the Prophet ﷺ. I met a man from Ghifar in the middle of the night and said: Where did you leave the Prophet ﷺ? He said: At al-Suqya. I said: O Messenger of Allah, your companions send you greetings and the mercy of Allah, and they feared that they would be cut off without you, so wait for them, O Messenger of Allah. Then I said: O Messenger of Allah, I caught a wild donkey and I have some of it left over. The Prophet ﷺ said to the people: \"Eat,\" and they were in ihram."],[632,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite in the first two rak'ahs of Zuhr the Opening of the Book and two surahs, making us hear a verse, and he would prolong the first rak'ah more than the second. In the last two, he recited the Opening of the Book. He would recite with us in the Fajr prayer, prolonging the first rak'ah more than the second."],[633,"\"When one of you enters the mosque, let him pray two rak'ahs before sitting down.\""],[634,"I used to see dreams that made me ill. I mentioned that to Abu Qatadah, and he said: I too used to see dreams that made me ill, until I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"A good dream is from Allah. If one of you sees what he likes, let him not tell it except to someone he loves. If he sees what he dislikes and wakes up, let him spit to his left three times and seek refuge in Allah from its evil and from the evil of Satan, and not tell anyone about it, for it will not harm him.\""],[635,"\"I hope to be rewarded by Allah, Mighty and Majestic, for expiating the year,\" and regarding fasting on the day of 'Arafah he said: \"I hope to be rewarded by Allah for expiating the year before it and the year after it.\""],[636,"A bedouin asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about his fasting, and he became angry until that was visible in his face. Then ʿUmar b. al-Khaṭṭāb ؓ stood up and said: “We are content with God as Lord, with Islam as religion, and with you as Prophet. I seek refuge in God from the anger of God and the anger of His Messenger.” ʿUmar kept repeating that until he calmed down. Then he said: “O Messenger of God, what do you say about a man who fasts the entire age?” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “He neither fasted nor broke his fast,” or he said: “He has not fasted and he has not broken his fast.” He said: “O Messenger of God, how about one who fasts two days and breaks his fast one day?” He said: “And who is able to do that?” He said: “O Messenger of God, how about one who breaks his fast two days and fasts one day?” He said: “I would love to be given the strength to do that.” He said: “O Messenger of God, what do you say about fasting on Monday?” He said: “That is the day on which I was born and on which it was sent down to me.” They said: “O Messenger of God, what do you say about a man who fasts one day and breaks his fast one day?” He said: “That is the fast of my brother Dāwūd.” They said: “O Messenger of God, what do you say about fasting on the day of ʿĀshūrāʾ?” He said: “I count on God that it will expiate the year.” He said: “O Messenger of God, what do you say about fasting on the day of ʿArafah?” He said: “I count on God, Mighty and Majestic, that it will expiate the year before it and the year after it.”"],[637,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ dug the trench, the people were carrying one brick at a time, while ʿAmmār was recovering from an illness he had. He began carrying two bricks at a time. Abū Saʿīd said: My companions told me that the Messenger of God ﷺ was brushing the dust from his head and saying: “Woe to you, O son of Sumayyah! The transgressing party will kill you.”"],[638,"“The best of horses is the one with a blaze on its forehead, a white upper lip, black in color, with white on its legs, and a white right foreleg. If it is not black, then a dark bay with these markings.”"],[639,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came to us while we were building the mosque, and he said: “Make it spacious, and you will fill it.”"],[640,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to lead the people in prayer while carrying Umāmah bt. Abī al-ʿĀṣ, carrying her on his neck. When he bowed he put her down, and when he rose he lifted her up."],[641,"A man said: “O Messenger of God, I pray behind so-and-so, and he prolongs the prayer until sometimes I lag behind!” He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ became angry with an anger I never saw him show in any admonition before, then he said: “Among you are those who drive people away. Whoever leads the people in prayer should keep it light for them, for among them are the weak, the elderly, and those with needs.”"],[642,"A man among us called Abū Shuʿayb prepared food for the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “Come, you and five others with you.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Will you permit me to bring a sixth?”"],[643,"We used to carry heavy loads, and a man would come with a large charity and it would be said: “He is showing off!” And another man would come with half a ṣāʿ. Then this verse was revealed: “Those who criticize the volunteers among the believers concerning charities,” up to His saying: “a painful punishment.”"],[644,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ with a bridled she-camel as charity. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: “On the Day of Resurrection you will have seven hundred bridled she-camels for it.”"],[645,"A man came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: “Give me a mount, for I am stranded.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Go to so-and-so and ask him.” He went to him and asked him, and he gave him a mount. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Whoever guides to a good deed has the like of the reward of the one who does it,” or he said: “of its doer.”"],[646,"“The prayer of a man is not sufficient if he does not keep his backbone straight—or he said: his back—in bowing and prostration.”"],[647,"The Prophet ﷺ used to straighten our shoulders, meaning in prayer, and say: “Stand straight and do not differ, lest your hearts differ. Let those of you with maturity and sound judgement stand nearest to me, then those next to them, then those next to them.” Abū Masʿūd said: “Today you differ more severely.”"],[648,"\"Whoever recites the two verses from Surat al-Baqarah in a night, they will suffice him.\""],[649,"\"When a man spends on his family a maintenance, seeking reward from God for it, it is a charitable donation for him.\""],[650,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to perform the witr prayer at the beginning of the night, in its middle, and at its end.\""],[651,"\"Would any of you be unable to recite one third of the Quran every night?\" We said, \"And who can manage that, O Messenger of God?\" He said, \"'Say: He is God, One' is one third of the Quran.\""],[652,"\"The one who should lead the people in prayer is the one who has most knowledge of the Book of God and has been reciting it longest. If they are equal in recitation, then the one who made the hijrah first. If they are equal in hijrah, then the eldest among them. And no man should lead another in prayer in his own home or in his own place of authority, nor should he sit on his special seat, except with his permission,\" or he said, \"unless he gives you permission.\""],[653,"We entered with the Prophet ﷺ into a house and he said: \"This matter will not cease to be among you, and you its guardians, as long as you do not introduce new deeds. But when you introduce them, God, Mighty and Majestic, will set over you the worst of His creation and they will strip you as a branch is stripped of its bark.\""],[654,"\"Shall I not lead you in prayer as the Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray?\" He said: We said, \"Yes.\" He said: \"Then he led us in four rak'ahs, the noon or the afternoon prayer, and he placed his hands on his knees and spread his fingers apart. He said: Then he raised his head and stood straight until every part of him settled into place. He did that until he finished his prayer.\" Then he said, \"This is how the prayer of the Messenger of God ﷺ was.\""],[655,"\"Among what people have retained from the words of the earlier prophethood is: If you feel no shame, do as you wish.\""],[656,"\"Riba is only in the delayed payment.\""],[657,"I entered upon the Messenger of God ﷺ in the Ka'bah and he saw images. He said: He called for a bucket of water, and I brought it to him. He began to wipe them away and say: \"May God fight a people who depict what they do not create.\""],[658,"He returned from 'Arafat with the Prophet ﷺ, and he was moving at a brisk pace, but when he came to an open space, he urged his mount on."],[659,"\"The Prophet ﷺ commanded me to raid Ubna in the morning and to burn.\""],[660,"I charged at a man, and he said, 'There is no god but Allah.' I thrust the sword into him and killed him. He said to me, 'O Usamah, what will you do with \"There is no god but Allah\" on the Day of Resurrection?' He repeated it many times until I wished that I had not embraced Islam except at that hour."],[661,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and he was distressed. I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, what is the matter with you?' He said, 'Gabriel promised me, but I have not seen him for three days.' He said, 'Then a dog appeared, coming out of one of the houses, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that it be killed. Then Gabriel appeared, and he said, \"O Gabriel, when you promised me, you used to come to me. What is the matter with you now?\" He said, \"We do not enter a house in which there is a dog or images.\""],[662,"We were sitting with Zayd b. Thabit, and they sent for Usamah b. Zayd and asked him about the middle prayer. He said, 'It is Zuhr. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to pray it in the midday heat.'"],[663,"I rode behind the Messenger of Allah ﷺ from Arafah to Jam'. He came to a mountain pass, dismounted, and urinated, then he did not pray until he came to Jam'."],[664,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said about the plague: 'If it breaks out in a land and you are in it, do not leave it. And if it is in a land and you are not in it, do not enter it.'"],[665,"A disbeliever does not inherit from a Muslim, nor does a Muslim inherit from a disbeliever."],[666,"Usamah b. Zayd used to ride to his property in Wadi al-Qura, and he would fast on Mondays and Thursdays. I said to him, 'Do you fast even though you have grown old and become weak?' He said, 'I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ fasting on Monday and Thursday. I said, \"O Messenger of Allah, do you fast on Monday and Thursday?\" He said, \"Indeed, deeds are presented on Monday and Thursday.\"'"],[667,"A man came from the countryside and was seized by pain, so he returned. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'I hope that its mountain passes will not appear before us'—meaning the mountain passes of Madinah."],[668,"I passed by Ali and al-Abbas while they were sitting in the mosque. They said, 'O Usamah, ask permission for us to enter upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ.' I said, 'O Messenger of Allah, here are Ali and al-Abbas seeking permission.' He said, 'Do you know what brought them?' I said, 'No, by Allah, I do not know.' He said, 'But I know what brought them.' He said, 'So he gave them permission, and they entered, greeted, and sat down. They said, \"O Messenger of Allah, which of your family is most beloved to you?\" He said, \"Fatimah bt. Muhammad.\""],[669,"During the illness in which he died, he said, 'Bring my companions in to me.' They entered upon him while he was covered with a Ma'afiri cloak. He said, 'May Allah curse the Jews; they took the graves of their prophets as places of worship.'"],[670,"He departed from Arafah with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and his mount did not lift a foreleg going until he reached Muzdalifah."],[671,"A daughter of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent to him that her son was dying and she would like him to come. He sent back greetings and said, 'To Allah belongs what He takes and what He gives, and everything with Him has an appointed term. Let her be patient and seek reward.' She sent the messenger back, adjuring him to come. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood up, and with him were Mu'adh b. Jabal, Sa'd, and Ubayy b. Ka'b. He said, 'The child was brought to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and his soul was rattling in his chest. The eyes of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ overflowed. Sa'd said, \"O Messenger of Allah, what is this?\" He said, \"This is mercy that Allah places in the hearts of whomever He wills of His servants, and Allah, Mighty and Majestic, has mercy on His servants only those who are merciful.\""],[672,"A necklace of ‘A’ishah made of Yemeni agate was lost during one of the journeys of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and ‘A’ishah was with the Messenger of God ﷺ on that journey. ‘A’ishah searched for her necklace until the night was well advanced. Abu Bakr came and became angry with her and said: 'You have detained the people in a place where there is no water.' He said: Then the verse of tayammum was revealed. Abu Bakr came and said: 'You, by God, my little daughter, as far as I know, are blessed!' ‘Ubayd Allah said: ‘Ammar used to relate that the people began that day wiping the ground with their palms and wiping their faces with them, then they would return and strike another blow and wipe their hands up to the shoulders and armpits, then they prayed."],[673,"A man came to ‘Umar and mentioned that he had been on a journey, became junub, and could not find water. He said: 'He should not pray.' ‘Ammar said: 'Do you not remember, O Commander of the Faithful, when you and I were on a military expedition and we became junub and could not find water? As for you, you did not pray, but as for me, I rolled in the dust and prayed. When we came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, we mentioned that to him. He said to you: \"As for you, it was not appropriate for you to abandon the prayer. As for you, O ‘Ammar, it was not appropriate for you to roll as an animal rolls. It would have sufficed you\"—and the Messenger of God ﷺ struck the ground with his hand to the dust, then said: \"like this,\" and he blew on it and wiped his face and hands up to the wrist, and it does not include the forearms.'"],[674,"A man came to ‘Umar."],[675,"I became junub while I was with the camels and could not find water, so I rolled as an animal rolls. Then I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he said: 'Tayammum would have sufficed you.'"],[676,"The fitrah is: rinsing the mouth, sniffing water into the nose, using the toothstick, trimming the moustache, clipping the nails, plucking the armpit hair, shaving the pubic hair, washing with water after relieving oneself, circumcision, and washing the knuckles."],[677,"A dayyuth will not enter Paradise."],[678,"I saw ‘Ammar ibn Yasir on the day of Siffin, a dark-skinned old man, with a spear in his hand, and it was trembling. He looked at ‘Amr ibn al-‘As, who had the banner in his hand, and said: 'This is a banner I fought against three times with the Messenger of God ﷺ. By God, if they strike us until they drive us to the palm-fronds of Hajar, I would know that our course is upon the truth and that they are upon misguidance.'"],[679,"The two-faced one in this world will have two faces in the Fire on the Day of Resurrection."],[680,"I saw ‘Ammar perform wudu’ and pass his fingers through his beard, and he said: 'Thus I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do.'"],[681,"I came to my family from a journey and they anointed me with saffron. When morning came, I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and greeted him, but he did not welcome me or show me joy. He said: 'Go and wash this off you.' He said: So I washed it off, and then I came, and some of it remained on me. I greeted him, but he did not welcome me or show me joy, and said: 'Go and wash this off you.' So I washed it off. Then I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and greeted him, and he returned my greeting and welcomed me, and said: 'The angels do not attend the funeral of a disbeliever with good, nor one anointed with saffron, nor one who is junub.' And he gave a concession for the junub, if he wants to eat or sleep, to perform wudu’."],[682,"The likeness of my community is that of rain; it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end."],[683,"I said to ‘Ammar: 'O Abu al-Yaqzan, do you think that this matter you have brought about is by your own opinion, or is it something the Messenger of God ﷺ entrusted to you?' He said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ did not entrust us with anything except what he entrusted to all the people.'"],[684,"That 'Ammar ؓ was carrying with them—meaning the rocks—so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Woe to you, O son of Sumayya—the transgressing party will kill you."],[685,"I saw 'Ammar b. Yasir pray two rak'as and made them brief, so I said to him—or a man said to him: O Abu al-Yaqzan, you made them brief! He said: O son of my brother, did you see me shorten any of their limits? He said: No. He said: I hastened to ward off the whisperings, and I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: A man may pray a prayer and have only half of it, and he may pray a prayer and have only a third of it, and he may pray a prayer and have only a quarter of it. He said: until he reached a tenth."],[686,"And a man mentioned 'A'isha in his presence and disparaged her, so he said: Be silent, ugly and rejected—would you harm the beloved of the Messenger of God ﷺ?"],[687,"I was with Salman under a tree, and he took a dry branch from it, shook it, and its leaves fell off. Then he said: Will you not ask me why I do this? I said: And why do you do it? He said: Thus did the Messenger of God ﷺ, then he said: 'O Salman, will you not ask me why I do this?' I said: And why do you do this, O Messenger of God? He said: When a Muslim performs wudu' and perfects it, then prays the five prayers—he said, I think he said: 'in congregation—his sins fall away just as the leaves of this tree fall away.' And the Messenger of God ﷺ recited: And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approaches of the night. Indeed, good deeds remove evil deeds."],[688,"Locusts were mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: The most numerous of God's creation—I do not deem them lawful, nor do I deem them unlawful."],[689,"A man from the People of the Book said to a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ: Your companion has taught you even how to relieve yourselves! He said: He forbade us from facing the qibla with our private parts or turning our backs to it, and he commanded us to clean ourselves with three stones that contain neither bone nor dung."],[690,"In the Torah: the blessing of food is wudu' before it. I mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: The blessing of food is wudu' before it and after it."],[691,"I saw Salman al-Farisi, and he saw a man wanting to remove his leather socks during wudu', so Salman ordered him to wipe over his leather socks, his turban, and his hair. And Salman said: I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ wipe over his head covering and his leather socks."],[692,"I accompanied Salman, and he mentioned the treasures of Kisra and said: The One who gave them to you, bestowed them upon you, and opened them for you will withhold His storehouse. While Muhammad ﷺ was alive, they would wake up with no dinar, no dirham, and no mudd of food—so how is this, O brother of Banu 'Abs? He said: Then he passed by threshing floors being winnowed and said: The One who gave them to you, bestowed them upon you, and opened them for you will withhold His storehouse. While Muhammad ﷺ was alive, they would wake up with no dinar, no dirham, and no mudd of food—so how is this, O brother of Banu 'Abs?"],[693,"O Salman, do not hate me, lest you depart from your religion. I said: O Messenger of God, how could I hate you when through you God guided us? He said: You would hate the Arabs, and thus hate me."],[694,"Whoever performs ghusl on Friday, anoints himself with his oil, perfumes himself from his household's perfume, then comes to Jumu'ah and does not separate between two people, and prays; and when the imam speaks, he listens and remains silent—he will be forgiven whatever is between that and the next Jumu'ah."],[695,"I witnessed Jarir b. 'Abdullah al-Bajali when al-Mughira b. Shu'ba died, and I heard Jarir delivering a sermon. He said: Intercede for your governor, for he loved well-being. Listen and obey until a governor comes to you. Now then, I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of God ﷺ upon Islam, and he stipulated to me sincere counsel for every Muslim. By the Lord of this mosque, I am indeed a sincere counselor to you."],[696,"Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him."],[697,"We were with Jarir b. 'Abdullah on a military expedition, and we were struck by severe hunger. Jarir wrote to Mu'awiya: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever does not show mercy to people, Allah will not show mercy to him.' He said: So Mu'awiya wrote back that they should return. He said: And he provisioned them."],[698,"There is no people among whom acts of disobedience are practiced while they are more powerful and more numerous than those who practice them, and then they do not change it, except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will envelop them all with a punishment."],[699,"O Jarir, make the people listen,\" meaning during the Farewell Pilgrimage. He said: \"Do not revert after me to being disbelievers, striking the necks of one another."],[700,"The Prophet ﷺ addressed us from a small pulpit, urging us to give charity and forbidding us from mutilation."],[701,"Whoever is deprived of gentleness is deprived of good."],[702,"When the collector of zakah comes to you, he should not leave you except while he is pleased."],[703,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ wiped over the leather socks."],[704,"Dig a side niche for the grave and do not dig a trench in the middle, for the side niche is for us and the trench is for others."],[705,"We were sitting with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ at the beginning of the day, when a group of people came, barefoot, naked, wearing striped cloaks, with their swords hanging on them—or he said: girded with swords—most of them from Mudar, indeed all of them from Mudar. I saw the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ change because of the poverty he saw in them. He entered, then came out, and ordered Bilal, who gave the call to prayer, and he prayed the noon prayer. Then he delivered a sermon and said: 'O people, fear your Lord, who created you from a single soul'—to the end of the verse. Then he said: 'O you who believe, fear Allah, and let every soul consider what it has sent ahead for tomorrow'—to the end of the verse. 'Let a man give charity from his dinar, from his dirham, from his garment, from a saa' of his wheat, from a saa' of his dates,' until he said: 'even with half a date.' He said: Then a man from the Ansar brought a purse that his hand could hardly hold, indeed it could not hold it, and handed it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. Then the people followed one another in giving charity, and I saw before the Messenger of Allah ﷺ two heaps of food and clothing, and the face of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ began to shine as if it were gilded. And he said: 'Whoever sets a good precedent in Islam, he will have its reward and the reward of those who act upon it after him, without their rewards being diminished in anything. And whoever sets an evil precedent in Islam, he will bear its burden and the burden of those who act upon it after him, without their burdens being diminished in anything.'"],[706,"The Muhajirun and the Ansar are allies of one another in this world and the Hereafter."],[707,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the sudden glance. He said: 'Avert your gaze.'"],[708,"\"The runaway slave: no prayer is accepted from him until he returns to his masters.\""],[709,"Zayd b. Arqam used to pray over our funerals and say four takbirs. One day he said five takbirs over it. He was asked about that, and he said: \"The Prophet ﷺ said five takbirs over it.\""],[710,"The Ansar said: \"O Messenger of God, every people have followers, and we have all followed you. So supplicate God for us to make our followers from among us!\" He did so and supplicated for them."],[711,"We used to sit with Zayd b. Arqam and say: \"Narrate to us, narrate to us.\" He would say: \"We have grown old and forgotten, and narrating hadith from the Messenger of God ﷺ is a serious matter.\""],[712,"\"You are not a part of a hundred thousand – or seventy thousand – parts of those who will come to me at the Basin.\" At that time they were eight hundred or nine hundred."],[713,"\"The first one to pray with the Messenger of God ﷺ was 'Ali.\""],[714,"\"These latrines are frequented by devils, so when one of you comes to relieve himself, let him say: I seek refuge in God from the male and female devils.\""],[715,"\"O God, forgive the Ansar, the children of the Ansar, and the children of the children of the Ansar.\""],[716,"Anas lost sons, and Zayd b. Arqam wrote to him that the Prophet ﷺ said: \"O God, forgive the Ansar, the children of the Ansar, and the children of the children of the Ansar.\""],[717,"I said to Zayd b. Arqam: \"How many expeditions did the Messenger of God ﷺ go on?\" He said: \"Nineteen expeditions.\""],[718,"I said to Zayd b. Arqam: \"How many expeditions did you go on with the Messenger of God ﷺ?\" He said: \"Seventeen expeditions.\""],[719,"What was the first expedition the Messenger of God ﷺ went on? He said: \"Dhu al-'Ushayra, or Dhu al-'Usayra.\""],[720,"I witnessed Mu'awiya asking Zayd b. Arqam: Did you witness with the Messenger of God ﷺ two festivals that coincided on one day? He said: Yes. He said: How did he act? He said: He prayed the festival prayer, then he granted a dispensation regarding the Friday prayer, saying: \"Whoever wishes to pray, let him pray.\""],[721,"The Prophet ﷺ \"commanded them to treat pleurisy with Indian aloeswood and oil.\""],[722,"He saw people sitting with a storyteller, and when the sun rose they hastened to the pillars to pray. Zayd b. Arqam said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: The prayer of the penitent is when the young camels feel the heat of the sun."],[723,"I asked Zayd b. Arqam and al-Bara' b. 'Azib about money exchange. I asked one of them and he said: Ask the other, for he is better than me! I asked them both and they told me that the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade selling gold for silver on credit."],[724,"\"A group of my community will continue to fight for the truth until the command of God comes.\""],[725,"\"Whoever narrates a hadith from me while he thinks it is false is one of the liars.\""],[726,"Two matters about which I do not ask anyone among the people: a man praying behind another man from his subjects, for I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ pray behind 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf, and wiping over the leather socks, for I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ wipe over them."],[727,"The \"Prophet ﷺ wiped the top of his leather socks.\""],[728,"He used to pray until his feet became swollen. He said: It was said to him: O Messenger of God, do you do this when your past and future sins have been forgiven? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Should I not be a grateful servant?"],[729,"When Ibrahim, the son of the Messenger of God ﷺ, died, the sun eclipsed. The people said: The sun eclipsed because of the death of Ibrahim. The Messenger of God ﷺ came out and said: O people, the sun and the moon do not eclipse for the death or life of anyone, but they are two signs among the signs of God, Mighty and Majestic. So when that happens, pray until it clears."],[730,"\"Al-Mughira b. Shu'ba led us in prayer and he stood up after the first two rak'ahs. They said subhan Allah to him, but he continued his prayer. When he finished, he prostrated twice, then said the salam, and said: This is how the Messenger of God ﷺ did.\""],[731,"A man from Hudhayl had two wives, and one of them threw a tent pole at the other and caused her to miscarry. He said: What do you think of one who did not eat, drink, cry out, or raise its voice? It was said: \"Is it rhymed prose like the rhymed prose of the Jahiliyya?\" He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled regarding it with a ghurra and placed it upon the woman's 'aqila."],[732,"He has not relied upon Allah who seeks ruqyah or cauterizes."],[733,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man with a long mustache, so he called for a siwak and a blade, placed the siwak under the mustache, and trimmed it along it."],[734,"I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wipe over the turban and the leather socks."],[735,"Whoever sells wine, let him also butcher pigs."],[736,"The rider is behind the funeral procession, and the walker may be wherever he wishes relative to it: in front of it close by, or to its right close by, or to its left close by."],[737,"The miscarried fetus is prayed over, and supplication is made for its parents for forgiveness and mercy."],[738,"We set out with al-Nu'man b. Muqarrin and came to the non-Arab 'the one with the eyebrow' (Dhu al-Hajib). They sent to us: 'Send a man to me that I may speak with him.' He said: The people that day chose al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah. My father said: It is as if I am looking at a one-eyed man with a shield of his; and there he was al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah. We came to the non-Arab, and he said: 'Allah (mighty and majestic) sent among us a prophet, and Allah promised him victory, so what...'"],[739,"The first to come to us in Madinah - meaning in the Hijrah - were Mus'ab b. 'Umayr and Ibn Umm Maktum, and they used to teach the Qur'an. Then Sa'd, Bilal, and 'Ammar came. Then 'Umar b. al-Khattab came with twenty others. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ came, and I never saw the people of Madinah rejoice at anything as they rejoiced at the arrival of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ; slave women in the streets began saying: 'The Messenger of Allah ﷺ has come!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ had not yet arrived when I had already recited 'Glorify the name of your Lord the Most High' and 'By the night when it covers' among the surahs of the Mufassal."],[740,"When this verse was revealed: 'Not equal are those who sit among the believers,' the Messenger of Allah ﷺ called Zayd b. Thabit and called for a shoulder blade so that he could write it down. Then Ibn Umm Maktum came and mentioned his disability, so this verse was revealed: 'other than those who have a disability.'"],[741,"The people captured donkeys on the day of Khaybar - meaning domestic donkeys - so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered a caller, and he called out: 'Overturn the cooking pots.'"],[742,"A man said to him: 'O Abu 'Umarah, did you flee from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on the day of Hunayn?' Al-Bara' said: 'But the Messenger of Allah ﷺ did not flee. The Hawazin were a people of archers, and when we met them and charged at them, they were defeated. The people turned to the spoils, and they faced us with arrows, so the people fled. I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ that day while Abu Sufyan b. al-Harith was holding the bridle of the mule, and the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was on his white mule, and the Prophet ﷺ was saying: 'I am the Prophet, no lie; I am the son of 'Abd al-Muttalib.'"],[743,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded a man from the Ansar, when he went to his bed, to say: 'O Allah, I submit my soul to You, and I turn my face to You, and I entrust my affair to You, and I lean my back upon You, out of desire and fear of You. There is no refuge and no escape from You except to You. I believe in Your Book which You sent down and Your Messenger whom You sent.' He said: 'If he dies, he dies upon the natural disposition (fitrah).'"],[744,"When he went to his bed, he placed his hand under his cheek and said: O God, protect me from Your punishment on the Day You resurrect Your servants."],[745,"A silk robe was gifted to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and they began touching it and marveling at its softness. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: A handkerchief from the handkerchiefs of Sa'd b. Mu'adh in Paradise is softer than this."],[746,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came upon some people who sat in the road and said: If you must do so, then return the greeting, help the oppressed, and guide the way."],[747,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ on the Day of the Trench digging with us, until I saw the dust covering the whiteness of his belly—or he said: his hair—while he said: By God, were it not for God we would not have been guided, nor given charity, nor prayed. So send down tranquility upon us and make firm the feet when we meet. Shu'ba said in his hadith: My memory: the first ones have transgressed against us, and in the sheet: the chiefs have transgressed against us; when they desire a trial, we refuse. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ would say: \"We refuse, we refuse,\" raising his voice with it."],[748,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ made peace with the polytheists of Quraysh, he wrote between them a document: \"This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of God ﷺ, has made peace upon.\" They said: If we knew you were the Messenger of God, we would not have fought you! So he said to 'Ali: \"Erase it.\" He refused, so the Messenger of God ﷺ erased it with his hand and wrote: This is what Muhammad b. 'Abd Allah has made peace upon. They stipulated upon him that they should stay three days and not enter Makkah with weapons except the sheathed sword."],[749,"While a man was reciting Surat al-Kahf at night, he saw his riding beast bolting—or he said: his horse bolting. He looked and there was something like a mist—or he said: like a cloud. He mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, who said: That was the tranquility that descended for the Qur'an, or descended upon the Qur'an."],[750,"When the prohibition of wine was revealed, they said: What about those who drank it before it was forbidden? Then this verse was revealed: There is no blame upon those who believe and do righteous deeds for what they have eaten [in the past]—the verse."],[751,"When he returned from a journey, he would say: \"Returning, repenting, worshiping—to our Lord praising.\""],[752,"The Ansar, when they returned from a journey, a man would not enter through his door. Then this verse was revealed: It is not righteousness that you enter houses from their backs, but righteousness is [in] one who fears God. And enter houses from their doors."],[753,"When they prayed with the Messenger of God ﷺ and raised their heads from bowing, none of them would prostrate until they saw the Messenger of God ﷺ prostrating, then they would prostrate."],[754,"I and Ibn 'Umar were deemed too young on the Day of Badr."],[755,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ came to Madinah, he prayed toward Jerusalem for sixteen months. Then this verse was revealed to him: So turn your face toward the Sacred Mosque. It was revealed while some people were praying toward Jerusalem. When they heard it while in prayer, they turned their faces toward the Ka'bah while still in prayer."],[756,"\"I went on fifteen military expeditions with the Messenger of God ﷺ.\""],[757,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ was of medium stature, broad-shouldered, the greatest of people and the most handsome. His hair reached his earlobes. He wore a red hulla. I have never seen anything more beautiful than him.\""],[758,"\"Some people who used to pray toward Jerusalem died, and they said: 'What about our companions who died while they prayed toward Jerusalem?' Then God, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: 'God would never let your faith be lost' – meaning your prayer toward Jerusalem.\""],[759,"\"I saw the whiteness of the armpit of the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was prostrating.\""],[760,"\"He would fight the enemy. A man came veiled in iron armor, and the Messenger of God ﷺ offered him Islam, so he accepted. He said: 'Which deed is best for me to do?' He said: 'Fight the people you have just come from.' So he fought them until he was killed. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'He did little and was rewarded much.'\""],[761,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ appointed 'Abd Allah b. Jubayr over the archers on the day of Uhud, and they were fifty men. He said to them: 'Stay in your place and do not leave, even if you see birds snatching us.' Al-Bara' said: 'By God, I saw the women, their anklets showing, their garments loosened, climbing the mountain. When what happened happened and the people were raiding, they moved on. 'Abd Allah b. Jubayr, their commander, said: 'What will you do about the words of the Messenger of God ﷺ?' But they moved on, and what happened happened. When night came, Abu Sufyan b. Harb came and said: 'Is Muhammad among you?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Do not answer him.' Then he said: 'Is Muhammad among you?' They did not answer him. Then he said: 'Is Muhammad among you?' a third time, and they did not answer him. Then he said: 'Is Ibn Abi Quhafa among you?' They did not answer him—he said it three times. Then he said: 'Is Ibn al-Khattab among you?' He said it three times, and they did not answer him. He said: 'As for these, you have been spared them.' 'Umar could not control himself and said: 'You lie, O enemy of God! Here is the Messenger of God ﷺ, and Abu Bakr, and I, alive. And from us you will have an evil day.' He said: 'A day for the day of Badr, and war is a matter of give and take.' Then he said: 'Exalted be Hubal!' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Answer him.' They said: 'O Messenger of God, what should we say?' He said: 'Say: God is higher and more majestic.' He said: 'We have al-'Uzza, and you have no 'Uzza!' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Answer him.' They said: 'O Messenger of God, what should we say?' He said: 'Say: God is our Protector, and you have no protector.' Then Abu Sufyan said: 'You will see mutilation among the people that I did not order.' Then he said: 'And it did not displease me.'\""],[762,"\"Was the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ like a sword? He said: No, rather like the moon.\""],[763,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ performed 'umrah in Dhu al-Qa'dah.\""],[764,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ said about the Ansar: 'No one loves them except a believer, and no one hates them except a hypocrite. Whoever loves them, God loves him, and whoever hates them, God hates him.'\""],[765,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ said when his son Ibrahim died: 'He has a wet nurse in Paradise.'\""],[766,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ said to Hassan b. Thabit: 'Satirize them'—meaning the polytheists—or he said, 'attack them'—'and Gabriel is with you.'\""],[767,"\"He forbade the meat of domestic donkeys, and the pots were overturned.\""],[768,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ placing al-Hasan on his shoulder, and he said: Whoever loves me, let him love him."],[769,"I was with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on a journey, and he recited in the Maghrib prayer in the second rak'ah, 'By the fig and the olive.'"],[770,"The Prophet ﷺ was asked about performing ablution after eating camel meat, and he commanded it. And he was asked about praying in camel resting places, and he forbade it."],[771,"He was asked about performing ablution after eating sheep meat, and he gave a dispensation for performing ablution after it. And he was asked about praying in their resting places, and he gave a dispensation for it."],[772,"When Matar b. Najiyah took control of Kufah, he ordered Abu 'Ubaydah b. 'Abd Allah to lead the people in prayer, and he led the people. When he raised his head from bowing, he lengthened the standing. I narrated that to Ibn Abi Layla, and he narrated from al-Bara' b. 'Azib, who said: The prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, when he prayed and bowed, and when he raised his head from bowing, and when he prostrated, and when he raised his head from prostration, between the two prostrations, was nearly equal in length."],[773,"He used to perform qunut in the Fajr and Maghrib prayers."],[774,"Beautify the Qur'an with your voices."],[775,"A Bedouin came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me of a deed that will admit me into Paradise. He said: If you have been brief in the address, you have certainly framed the question broadly! Free the captive and release the neck. He said: O Messenger of Allah, are they not the same? He said: No, freeing the captive is to do it alone, and releasing the neck is to help with its price, and the productive gift, and the return to a wrongdoer who is a relative. He said: What if someone cannot do that? He said: Then feed the hungry and give water to the thirsty. He said: What if I cannot do that? He said: Enjoin good and forbid evil. He said: What if someone cannot do that? He said: Then restrain your tongue except from good."],[776,"Whoever gives a gift of silver, or guides a lost animal, or gives milk to drink, it will be for him like the reward of freeing a captive or a neck. And whoever says, 'There is no god but Allah alone, with no partner, His is the dominion and His is the praise, and He is over all things capable,' ten times, it will be for him like the reward of freeing a captive or a neck."],[777,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come to us when we stood for prayer and would wipe our shoulders and chests and say: Do not differ, lest your hearts differ. Indeed, Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and His angels send blessings upon the first row, or he said: the first rows."],[778,"When the Prophet's ﷺ son Ibrahim died, he said: He has a wet nurse who will suckle him in Paradise."],[779,"He delivered a sermon on the Day of Sacrifice and said: The first thing we begin with on this day of ours is to pray, then return and sacrifice. Whoever does that has followed our Sunnah, and whoever slaughters before the prayer, it is only meat that he has offered for his family and is not part of the sacrifice at all. My maternal uncle Abu Burdah b. Niyar stood up, and he had slaughtered before the prayer, and said: O Messenger of Allah, I have a jadha'ah that is dearer to me than a musinnah. He said: Sacrifice it, and it will not suffice, or be acceptable, for anyone after you."],[780,"The Prophet ﷺ commanded a man, when he took to his bed at night, to say: 'O Allah, I have submitted my soul to You, turned my face to You, entrusted my affair to You, and leaned my back upon You, in desire and fear of You. There is no refuge and no escape from You except to You. I have believed in Your Book which You sent down and Your Messenger whom You sent.' He said: 'If he dies, he dies upon the fitrah.'"],[781,"Regarding His saying, 'Allah keeps firm those who believe with the firm word,' he said: 'In the grave when he is questioned.'"],[782,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us with seven things and forbade us from seven. He commanded us to visit the sick, follow funerals, return the greeting, respond to the one who sneezes, fulfill the oath of the one who swears, help the oppressed, and accept the invitation of the one who invites. And he forbade us from gold rings—or he said gold signet rings—vessels of gold and silver, saddle cushions, silk brocade, heavy silk, and silk."],[783,"He said: 'Do you know which bond of faith is firmest?' We said: Prayer. He said: 'Prayer is good, but it is not that.' We said: Fasting. He said the like of that until we mentioned jihad, and he said the like of that. Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'The firmest bond of faith is love for the sake of Allah and hatred for the sake of Allah.'"],[784,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to me: 'When you prostrate, place your hand and raise your elbows.'"],[785,"I asked al-Bara' b. 'Azib what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ disliked or forbade regarding sacrificial animals. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ stood among us like this—and my hand is shorter than his hand—and said: 'Four will not suffice: the one-eyed whose defect is evident, the sick whose illness is evident, the lame whose lameness is evident, and the broken one that has no marrow.' I said: I dislike that there be a defect in the teeth or in the horn or in the ear. He said: 'Whatever you dislike of it, leave it, but do not forbid it to anyone.'"],[786,"I asked al-Bara' b. 'Azib and Zayd b. Arqam about exchanging money. I would ask one of them and he would say: Ask the other, for he is better than me and more knowledgeable. So I asked them both and they narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade selling silver for gold on credit."],[787,"When a Muslim meets his brother, shakes his hand, and they praise Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, and seek His forgiveness, Allah forgives them both."],[788,"Abu Burdah slaughtered before the prayer, so the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: 'Replace it.' He said: O Messenger of Allah, I have nothing but a jadha'ah that is better than a musinnah! He said: 'Put it in its place, and it will never suffice—or fulfill—for anyone after you.'"],[789,"When the believing servant is in the onset of the Hereafter and the severance from this world, an angel comes to him and sits at his head and says: 'Come out, O tranquil soul, to forgiveness from Allah and His good pleasure.' So his soul comes out and flows as a drop flows from a waterskin. 'Amr said in his narration, and Abu 'Awanah did not say it: 'Even if you see otherwise.' Angels descend from Paradise with white faces, as if their faces were the sun, bringing shrouds from the shrouds of Paradise and perfume from its perfume. They sit from him as far as the eye can see. When the angel seizes the soul, they do not leave it in his hand for the blink of an eye. That is His saying, the Mighty and Majestic: 'Our messengers take him, and they do not fail.' He said: His soul comes out with the most pleasant scent ever found. The angels ascend with it, and they do not pass by any host between heaven and earth but that they say: 'What is this spirit?' It is said: 'So-and-so'—with the best of his names—until they reach the gate of the lowest heaven, and it is opened for him, and the near ones of every heaven escort him until it is brought to the seventh heaven. Then it is said: 'Write his book in 'Illiyyin—and what will make you know what 'Illiyyin is? A written book witnessed by those brought near.' So his book is written in 'Illiyyin. Then it is said: 'Return him to the earth, for I promised them that from it I created them, and into it I shall return them, and from it I shall bring them out another time.' So he is returned to the earth, and his soul is restored to his body. Two angels with harsh rebuke come to him and rebuke him and sit him up. They say: 'Who is your Lord, and what is your religion?' He says: 'My Lord is Allah and my religion is Islam.' They say: 'What do you say about this man who was sent among you?' He says: 'He is the Messenger of Allah.' They say: 'And what makes you know that?' He says: 'He brought us clear proofs from our Lord, so I believed in him and affirmed him.' He said: That is His saying, the Mighty and Majestic: 'Allah keeps firm those who believe with the firm word in the life of this world and in the Hereafter.' He said: A caller calls from heaven: 'My servant has spoken truth, so clothe him from Paradise and spread for him from it, and show him his place in it.' So he is clothed from Paradise, spread for from it, and shown his place in it. Space is expanded for him as far as his eye can see, and his deeds are represented to him in the form of a man with a handsome face, pleasant scent, and fine clothes. He says: 'Rejoice in what Allah, the Mighty and Majestic, has prepared for you. Rejoice in the good pleasure of Allah and gardens in which there is lasting bliss.' He says: 'May Allah give you good tidings. Who are you? Your face is the face that brings good.' He says: 'This is your day which you were promised and the matter which you were promised. I am your righteous deed. By Allah, I never knew you but to be quick in obedience to Allah and slow to disobey Allah, so may Allah reward you with good.' He says: 'O Lord, establish the Hour so that I may return to my family and my wealth.' He said: And if he was a wicked person, and he was in the onset of the Hereafter and the severance from this world, an angel comes to him and sits at his head and says: 'Come out, O wicked soul, rejoice in the wrath of Allah and His anger.' Angels with black faces descend, bringing haircloth. When the angel seizes it, they stand and do not leave it in his hand for the blink of an eye. He said: It sinks into his body, and he extracts it, cutting with it the veins and nerves like a large multi-pronged skewer in wet wool. It is taken from the angel and comes out with the foulest scent ever found. It does not pass by any host between heaven and earth but that they say: 'What is this wicked spirit?' They say: 'This is so-and-so'—with the worst of his names—until they reach the lowest heaven, but it is not opened for him. Then it is said: 'Return him to the earth, for I promised them that from it I created them, and into it I shall return them, and from it I shall bring them out another time.' He said: He is thrown from heaven. He said: Then he recited this verse: 'And whoever associates others with Allah, it is as though he had fallen from the sky'—the verse. He said: He is returned to the earth, and his soul is restored to him. Two angels with harsh rebuke come to him and rebuke him and sit him up. They say: 'Who is your Lord, and what is your religion?' He says: 'I do not know.' They say: 'What do you say about this man who was sent among you?' He does not find guidance to his name. He says: 'I do not know. I heard the people saying that.' He said: It is said: 'You did not know.' His grave is constricted for him until his ribs interlace. His deeds are represented to him in the form of a man with an ugly face, foul smell, and ugly clothes. He says: 'Rejoice in punishment from Allah and His wrath.' He says: 'Who are you? Your face is the face that brings evil.' He says: 'I am your wicked deed. By Allah, I never knew you but to be slow in obedience to Allah and quick to disobey Allah.' 'Amr said in his narration from al-Minhal from Zadhan from al-Bara' from the Prophet ﷺ: An angel is assigned to him, deaf and mute, with a sledgehammer, which if a mountain were struck with it would become dust—or he said: crumbled remains. He strikes him with it a blow that all creatures hear except the two heavy ones. Then the soul is restored to him and he strikes him another blow. In the Dar al-Ma'rifah edition there is an addition: (al-Hasan). In the Dar al-Ma'rifah edition there is an addition: (min). In the Dar al-Ma'rifah edition there is an addition: ('ala)."],[790,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ turn away Ma'iz twice, then he ordered him to be stoned."],[791,"Before the Hour there will be liars. He said a word I did not understand, so I said to my father: 'What did he say?' He said: 'Beware of them.'"],[792,"\"This religion will continue to stand, a band of the Muslims fighting for it, until the Hour comes.\""],[793,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ delivering a sermon standing, then sitting, then standing and delivering a sermon."],[794,"What did the Messenger of God ﷺ used to do when he prayed the dawn prayer? He said: He would sit in his place until the sun rose."],[795,"\"I saw the seal on the shoulder of the Messenger of God ﷺ as if it were an egg.\""],[796,"\"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ at the funeral of Ibn al-Dahdahah, and he was on a horse that was prancing with him, while we were walking around him.\""],[797,"The Messenger of God ﷺ only mounted the horse after he had finished burying him."],[798,"They used to call Madinah Yathrib, \"and the Messenger of God ﷺ named it Taybah.\""],[799,"\"When he applied oil it was not visible, and when he did not apply oil it became apparent.\""],[800,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to recite in the noon and afternoon prayers: 'By the night when it covers' and similar surahs, and he would recite in the dawn prayer something longer than that.\""],[801,"I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ when Maiz b. Malik, a short man with muscles, was stoned. When he finished stoning him, he said: \"Whenever we go out as raiders in the path of God, one of them stays behind and bleats like a goat, giving one of them a small amount of milk. Indeed, God has not enabled me against any of them except that I would make an example of him and turn him into a warning.\""],[802,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ had eyes with a touch of redness, thin heels, and a wide mouth.\""],[803,"\"He was asked about ablution from the meat of sheep, and he allowed it. He was asked about praying in sheep folds—or he said: their resting places (Abu Dawud was uncertain)—and he allowed it. He was asked about ablution from the meat of camels, and he commanded it. He was asked about praying in camel resting places, and he forbade it and disliked it.\""],[804,"\"Islam will continue to be mighty until twelve caliphs,\" then he said a word I did not understand. I said to my father: \"What did the Messenger of God ﷺ say?\" He said: \"All of them will be from Quraysh.\""],[805,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stoned Ma'iz, and he did not mention flogging."],[806,"One of them said: \"Bilal used to give the call to prayer when the sun had begun to decline,\" and the other said: \"Bilal used to give the call to prayer when the sun had passed its zenith.\""],[807,"\"Bilal did not omit any part of the call to prayer, and he sometimes delayed the iqamah a little.\""],[808,"I said to Jabir b. Samurah: \"Did you sit with the Prophet ﷺ?\" He said: \"Yes. He was long-silent and rarely laughed, and his companions would sometimes recite poetry to one another in his presence and talk about some of their affairs, and they would laugh; and sometimes he would smile.\""],[809,"How did the Messenger of God ﷺ deliver the sermon? He said: \"Whoever tells you that the Messenger of God ﷺ delivered a sermon sitting down, disbelieve him. I witnessed him delivering the sermon standing.\" I said: \"How was his sermon?\" He said: \"It was moderate; he would recite verses from the Book of God and speak words of admonition to the people.\""],[810,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray Zuhr like your prayer, Asr like your prayer, and Maghrib like your prayer, and he would delay Isha a little.\""],[811,"\"He used to recite in Zuhr and Asr: 'By the sky and the night comer' and 'By the sky with constellations.'\""],[812,"The Messenger of God ﷺ stoned a Jewish man and a Jewish woman."],[813,"A man had a she-camel in the Harrah. He gave it to another man when it had become ill. When it was about to die, his wife said to him: \"If only you would slaughter it and we could eat from it!\" But he refused. He went to the Messenger of God ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: \"Do you have anything that would suffice you?\" He said: \"No.\" He said: \"Then eat it.\" It had already died. She said: \"We ate from its fat, meat, and suet for about twenty days. Then he met its owner and said to him: 'Why didn't you slaughter it?' He said: 'I was too shy before you.'\""],[814,"\"No call to prayer was given for him on the two Eids.\""],[815,"\"Seek the Night of Decree in the last ten nights.\""],[816,"That a man killed himself with a broad-headed arrow, and the Messenger of God ﷺ did not pray over him."],[817,"When we came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, we sat where we ended up."],[818,"In Makkah there is a rock that used to greet me during the nights I was sent. I recognize it whenever I pass by it."],[819,"The white treasures of Kisra will certainly be opened by a group of the Muslims."],[820,"Bilal used to give the call to prayer when the sun declined, and sometimes he delayed the iqama a little and sometimes he hurried it a little. As for the call to prayer, he did not miss the time."],[821,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to command us to fast on Ashura, urge us to do it, and check on us at that time. When Ramadan was made obligatory, he neither commanded us nor forbade us from it, and he did not check on us at that time."],[822,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ pointing with his finger in the prayer. When he said the salam, I heard him say: O God, I ask You for all good, what I know of it and what I do not know, and I seek refuge in You from all evil, what I know of it and what I do not know."],[823,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw people who had raised their hands, and he said: They have raised their hands as if they were the tails of restless horses. Be still in the prayer."],[824,"I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ delivering a sermon on Friday, reciting from the Quran and admonishing the people."],[825,"In the son of Adam there is a lump of flesh: if it is sound, the rest of his body is sound, and if it is corrupt, the rest of his body is corrupt. It is the heart."],[826,"His father gave him a gift and wanted to have the Prophet ﷺ witness it, so he said: Did you give all your children as you gave him? He said: No. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: It is obligatory on you to be just among your children just as it is obligatory on them to treat you kindly."],[827,"Indeed, the likeness of the believers in their mutual love, affection, and compassion is that of the body: when one part of it complains, the rest of the body responds with sleeplessness and fever."],[828,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to straighten the rows until he made them like an arrow shaft or a spear. Then, when he thought that we had learned that from him and understood it, he saw a man whose chest was protruding from the row, so the Messenger of God ﷺ said: “Servants of God, you shall straighten your rows or God, Mighty and Majestic, will certainly cause discord among your faces.”"],[829,"“I have warned you of the Fire,” until if a man were at such-and-such a place, he would hear his voice."],[830,"“The likeness of the believers is that of a body: when one part of it aches, the rest of it responds with wakefulness and fever.”"],[831,"“If a man were on a journey with his mount, upon which are his provisions and water-skin, and it strayed, so he climbed an elevation and looked but did not see anything. Then while he was thus, suddenly he saw it with its provisions and water-skin. God is more intensely joyful at the repentance of His servant than the owner of the mount at finding his mount.”"],[832,"“In Friday prayer and the two Eids he recited: ‘Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High’ and ‘Has there come to you the story of the Overwhelming?’”"],[833,"A woman came to al-Nuʿmān b. Bashīr and said: “My husband had intercourse with my slave-girl without my permission.” Al-Nuʿmān said: “I have a decisive judgment regarding this which I took from the Messenger of God ﷺ: If you had not given him permission, I would stone him; but if you had given him permission, I will flog him with a hundred lashes.” Then the people said to her: “Woe to you! The father of your child is to be stoned!” So she came back and said: “I had given him permission, but jealousy carried me to say what I said!” So he flogged him with a hundred lashes."],[834,"I am the most knowledgeable of people about the time of this prayer—meaning the late evening prayer. The Messenger of God ﷺ used to pray it at the setting of the moon on the third night."],[835,"“The one among the people of the Fire with the lightest punishment is a man on the soles of whose feet are two coals—or a coal—from which his brain boils.”"],[836,"“You shall straighten your rows or God, Mighty and Majestic, will certainly cause discord among your faces.”"],[837,"“He prayed during the eclipse, and he bowed and prostrated twice.”"],[838,"“Supplication is worship. Your Lord has said: ‘Call upon Me, I will respond to you.’”"],[839,"“There is no retaliation except with iron.”"],[840,"Indeed, before the Hour there will be trials like patches of a dark night. A man will wake up a believer and become a disbeliever by evening, and he will be a believer in the evening and become a disbeliever by morning. People will sell their religion for a small portion of this world."],[841,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the morning prayer. A bedouin said, 'Who will call out for the red camel?' — saying it in the mosque. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'May you not find it.' Then the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'These mosques were built only for what they were built for.'"],[842,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed all the prayers with a single ablution."],[843,"A man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said, 'Are there horses in Paradise? For they please me.' He said, 'If you desire that, you will be given a horse of red ruby that will fly with you in Paradise wherever you wish.' Another man said to him, 'Camels please me. Are there camels in Paradise?' He said, 'O servant of Allah, if you enter Paradise, you will have in it what your soul desires and what delights your eyes.'"],[844,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ permitted visiting graves."],[845,"He returned Ma'iz four times."],[846,"Buraydah al-Aslami entered upon a man in Khurasan while he was dying, and his forehead was sweating. Buraydah said, 'Allah is greater! I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say, \"Indeed, the believer dies with sweat on the forehead.\"'"],[847,"I went out one day walking and saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I thought he needed something, so I crossed his path until he saw me. He sent for me, and I came to him. He took my hand and we walked together. There was a man ahead of us praying, performing many bowings and prostrations. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Do you think he is showing off?' I said, 'Allah and His Messenger know best.' He released my hand and said, 'Keep to a moderate course, for whoever contends with this religion will be overcome by it.'"],[848,"We were with Buraydah al-Ansari on a military expedition on a cloudy day. He said, 'Pray early, for I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say' — or the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said — 'Whoever abandons the afternoon prayer, his deeds are nullified.'"],[849,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ would not go out on the day of Fitr until he ate, and he would not eat on the day of sacrifice until he slaughtered."],[850,"A man from Khuza'ah died during the time of the Prophet ﷺ, and his inheritance was brought to the Prophet ﷺ. He said, 'Look for any heir.' They searched but found no heir for him. The Prophet ﷺ was informed, and he said, 'Give it to the eldest of Khuza'ah.'"],[851,"A man came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, I do not recite the Qur'an well. Is there something that will suffice me from the Qur'an?' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'Glory be to Allah, praise be to Allah, there is no god but Allah, Allah is greater, and there is no power or strength except with Allah.' The man turned away, then returned and said, 'O Messenger of Allah, this is for Allah. What is for me?' He said, 'Say: O Allah, forgive me, have mercy on me, grant me well-being, guide me, and provide for me.' The man counted them on his hand as ten. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, 'As for this one, he has filled his hands with good.'"],[852,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade nabīdh of the red jar. I said: “And the white one?” He said: “I do not know.”"],[853,"Abū Burdah and ʿAbdullāh b. Shaddād disagreed about salam, so they sent me to Ibn Abī Awfā. I asked him, and he said: “We used to engage in salam at the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ in wheat, barley, raisins, and dates, with people who did not have them.” He said: Then we asked Ibn Abzā, and he said the same."],[854,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the meat of domesticated donkeys."],[855,"In his supplication, the Messenger of God ﷺ used to say: “O God, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will after that.” Abū Dāwūd said: Qays said in his ḥadīth: The Messenger of God ﷺ used to say this when he raised his head from bowing."],[856,"I took part in seven military expeditions with the Messenger of God ﷺ, during which we ate locusts with him."],[857,"When people of a household brought the Messenger of God ﷺ ṣadaqah, he would invoke blessing upon them. My father gave ṣadaqah, so he said: “O God, bless the family of Abū Awfā.”"],[858,"He heard Ibn Abī Awfā, the Companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ – and he had witnessed the Pledge of al-Riḍwān – say: “We were on that day one thousand three hundred, and Aslam was on that day one-eighth of the Muhājirūn.”"],[859,"I asked ʿAbdullāh b. Abī Awfā: “Did the Messenger of God ﷺ leave a will?” He said: “No.” I said: “Then why did he command us to make wills but did not make one himself?” He said: “He left a will of the Book of God, Mighty and Majestic.”"],[860,"I came to ʿAbdullāh b. Abī Awfā, the Companion of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said to me: “Who are you?” – and at that time he had lost his sight. I said: “I am Saʿīd b. Jumhān.” He said: “What happened to your father?” I said: “The Azāriqah killed him.” He said:"],[861,"“A slave does not commit fornication while he is a believer, and he does not steal while he is a believer, and he does not drink wine while he is a believer, and he does not seize plunder of great value while he is a believer.”"],[862,"Al-Ḥakam narrated to us, from a man, from Ibn Abī Awfā, from the Prophet ﷺ – something similar."],[863,"The Prophet ﷺ used to supplicate with this supplication: “O God, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth and filling whatever You will after that.”"],[864,"I saw Ibn Abi Awfa at the funeral of his daughter, riding a mule. He passed by women who were wailing, and he said: Beware of wailing, for the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade it. Let any of you shed her tears."],[865,"I and ʿImrān b. Ḥuṣayn prayed behind ʿAlī b. Abī Ṭālib. When he prostrated he said the takbīr, and when he raised his head he said the takbīr, and when he rose from the two prostrations he said the takbīr. When we finished the prayer, ʿImrān took my hand and said: This has reminded us of the prayer of Muḥammad ﷺ — or he said: He led us in the prayer of Muḥammad ﷺ."],[866,"The Messenger of God ﷺ combined ḥajj and ʿumrah, then he did not forbid it and no Qurʾān came down to prohibit it. And he used to greet me, but when I cauterized myself it was cut off from me. When I abandoned it, it returned to me — meaning the angels."],[867,"It was said to the Prophet ﷺ: Is it known who are the people of Paradise and who are the people of the Fire? He said: Yes. He said: Then why do the workers work? He said: Each works for what he was created for and for what was made easy for him."],[868,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent ʿAlī with an army. They saw something from him and disapproved of it. Four men agreed and pledged to inform the Prophet ﷺ of what ʿAlī had done. ʿImrān said: When we returned from a journey we would not go to our families until we came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, greeted him, and looked at him. The four men came; one of them stood and said: O Messenger of God, did you not see that ʿAlī did such and such? But he turned away from him. Then the second stood and said the same, and he turned away from him. Then the third stood and said the same, and he turned away from him. Then the fourth stood and said the same. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: What have they to do with ʿAlī? Indeed ʿAlī is from me and I am from him, and he is the guardian of every believer after me."],[869,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade cauterization, but we cauterized ourselves, and we neither succeeded nor prospered."],[870,"Fast the middle of the month."],[871,"He had two wives. He came to one of them and she said: Have you come from so-and-so? — meaning his other wife. He said: No, but from ʿImrān b. Ḥuṣayn. He related that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: The fewest of the people of Paradise are women."],[872,"I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its people are the poor, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its people are women."],[873,"An old man came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, my son has died, what do I inherit from him? He said: You get one-sixth. When he turned away, he called him and said: You get another sixth. When he left, he called him and said: The other sixth is a gift."],[874,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was on a journey when he raised his voice reciting the two verses: “O people, fear your Lord” up to His saying: “but the punishment of God is severe.” He said: So they urged their mounts and knew that he was about to say something. When they gathered around him, he said: Do you know what day that is? They said: God and His Messenger know best. He said: That is the day when God, Mighty and Exalted, says to Adam: O Adam, arise and send forth the delegation of the Fire. He says: O Lord, what is the delegation of the Fire? He says: From every thousand, nine hundred and ninety-nine to the Fire and one to Paradise. They were struck with despair until none of them showed his teeth. When the Messenger of God ﷺ saw that, he said: Work and rejoice, for by Him in whose hand is my soul, you are with two creations that never appear in anything but they multiply it: Gog and Magog, and those who perished from the children of Adam and the children of Iblīs. Work and rejoice, for by Him in whose hand is my soul, you are among people only like a mole on the side of a camel or a mark on the foreleg of a beast."],[875,"Rarely did the Messenger of God ﷺ stand among us without urging us to give charity and forbidding us from mutilation. He said: It is mutilation to vow to cut off one's nose, and it is mutilation to vow to perform ḥajj on foot. If one of you vows to perform ḥajj on foot, let him offer a sacrificial animal and ride."],[876,"He was on a journey, and they slept and did not wake until the sun had risen. So they prayed and said, 'O Messenger of God, should we add to our prayer?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'God forbids you from usury, yet He accepts it from you!'"],[877,"\"There is no jalab, no janab, and no shighar in Islam.\""],[878,"\"There is no vow in anger, and its expiation is the expiation for an oath.\""],[879,"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed two rak'ahs in Makkah, then gave the salutation and said, 'O people of Makkah, complete your prayer, for we are a traveling people.'"],[880,"\"The best of my community is my generation.\""],[881,"A man from Juhaynah or Muzaynah asked the Messenger of God ﷺ, saying, 'O Messenger of God, what do you think of the deeds that people do? Is it a matter that has been decreed upon them from destiny and a destiny that has already preceded them, or something that you have brought to them by which you establish proof against them?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Rather, it is what has been decreed upon them and destined for them from a destiny that has already preceded.' He said, 'O Messenger of God, then why do they work?' He said, 'Work, for everyone is facilitated toward what he was created for.' Then he recited this verse: 'By the soul and He who proportioned it, and inspired it with its wickedness and its righteousness.'"],[882,"\"He forbade nabidh made in earthen jars.\""],[883,"The Prophet ﷺ \"was brought the 'Uqayli in bonds.\""],[884,"A man manumitted six of his slaves during the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so the Messenger of God ﷺ cast lots among them and freed two, while four remained enslaved."],[885,"Wuhayb narrated to us, from Khalid, from Abu Qilabah, from Abu al-Muhallab, from 'Imran, from the Prophet ﷺ - the like of it."],[886,"The Messenger of God ﷺ \"ransomed two men of his companions who were in the hands of the polytheists with one male captive.\""],[887,"\"The Messenger of God ﷺ prayed the noon or afternoon prayer as three rak'ahs, then gave the salutation. A man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ called Ibn al-Khirbaq said, 'Has the prayer been shortened?' So the Prophet ﷺ asked, and it was as he had said. He then prayed one rak'ah, gave the salutation, then prostrated twice, then gave the salutation.\""],[888,"A woman from Juhaynah came to the Prophet ﷺ while she was pregnant from fornication. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered her guardian to treat her well, and when she had delivered her child, to bring her to him. He did so, and the Prophet ordered that her garments be fastened around her, then ordered that she be stoned. Then he prayed over her. Umar said to him: O Messenger of Allah, you pray over her and she had fornicated? He said: She has repented with such a repentance that if it were divided among the people of Madinah, it would suffice them. And have you found anything better than her giving herself for Allah?"],[889,"\"Your brother, the Negus, has died, so pray over him.\" He said: We lined up behind him as one lines up for a funeral, and we prayed over him as one prays over the dead."],[890,"\"There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah, Mighty and Majestic.\""],[891,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the noon prayer with his companions, then said: \"Which of you recited 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High'?\" A man said: I did. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"I knew that someone was contending with me in it.\""],[892,"\"The best of my community is the generation in which I was sent, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then there will come a people who make vows but do not fulfill them, who betray and are not trusted, who give testimony but are not asked to, and among whom obesity spreads.\""],[893,"\"Modesty brings nothing but good.\" Bushayr b. Ka'b said: In wisdom it is said: Indeed, from modesty comes dignity, and from modesty comes weakness. Imran said: I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and you narrate to me from the scriptures!"],[894,"\"Modesty is all good.\""],[895,"It was mentioned before Imran b. Husayn: weeping over the dead, that he is punished. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said it."],[896,"Do you know the day the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: There is no obedience in disobedience to Allah, Mighty and Majestic? He said: Yes. Imran said: Allah is greatest, Allah is greatest."],[897,"He was on a journey, so he stopped and slept, and said to Bilal: \"Wake us for our prayer.\" They did not wake up except by the heat of the sun on their backs or shoulders. He said: \"Depart from this place,\" so they departed. Then they stopped, and he said to Bilal: \"What prevented you from waking us?\" He said: The One who put you to sleep put me to sleep. He said: So they performed tayammum with the earth—and he ordered Bilal, so he gave the call to prayer, and they prayed two rak'ahs. Then he stood and they prayed the morning prayer."],[898,"A young man asked Imran b. Husayn about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while traveling. He said: This young man asked me about the prayer of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while traveling, so memorize from me: I never traveled with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ on any journey except that he prayed two rak'ahs until he returned. I witnessed with him Hunayn and al-Ta'if, and he prayed two rak'ahs. Then I performed Hajj and Umrah with him, and he prayed two rak'ahs. Then he said: O people of Makkah, complete the prayer, for we are a traveling people. Then I performed Hajj and Umrah with Abu Bakr, and he prayed two rak'ahs. Then he said: \"O people of Makkah, complete the prayer, for we are a traveling people.\" Then I performed Hajj and Umrah with Umar, and he prayed two rak'ahs. Then he said: Complete the prayer, for we are a traveling people. Then I performed Hajj and Umrah with Uthman, and he prayed two rak'ahs, two rak'ahs. Then indeed Uthman completed it."],[899,"\"Do not return after me as straying, striking one another's necks.\""],[900,"His father wrote to him while he was in Sijistan: Do not judge between two men while you are angry, for I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'No man should judge between two men, or between two adversaries, while he is angry.'"],[901,"He said: 'Do you think that if Muzayna, Juhayna, Aslam, and Ghifar were better than Banu Tamim, Asad, Ghatafan, and Banu Amir b. Sa'sa'a, they would be losers and failures? By Him in Whose hand is my soul, they are better than them.'"],[902,"'Muzayna, Juhayna, Aslam, and Ghifar are better than Banu Tamim, Asad, Ghatafan, and Banu Amir b. Sa'sa'a.'"],[903,"A man was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ and they praised him highly. He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said to the man: 'Woe to you, you have cut off your companion's neck' - he said it three times. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'If one of you must praise his brother, let him say: \"I consider So-and-so\" - if he knows that about him - \"and I do not declare anyone pure before God, Mighty and Majestic.\"'"],[904,"'The two months of the festivals are not deficient: Ramadan and Dhu al-Hijja.'"],[905,"It was said: 'O Messenger of God, which of the people is best?' He said: 'The one who lives long and whose deeds are good.' It was said: 'O Messenger of God, which of the people is worst?' He said: 'The one who lives long and whose deeds are evil.'"],[906,"'The parents of the Dajjal remain for thirty years without having a child, then a boy is born to them, one-eyed, the most harmful of things and the least beneficial. His eyes sleep but his heart does not sleep.' He said: And the Messenger of God ﷺ described his father: a tall man with flabby flesh, as if his nose were a beak. As for his mother, a tall woman with prominent breasts. Abu Bakra said: We heard of a newborn born in Madinah among the Jews, so I and al-Zubayr b. al-Awwam went and entered upon his parents, and found the description of the Messenger of God ﷺ in them. We said: 'Do you have any children?' They said: 'We remained thirty years without having a child, then a child was born to us, the most harmful of things and the least beneficial. His eyes sleep but his heart does not sleep.' We went out from them and found him lying wrapped in a velvet cloth in the sun, murmuring. He uncovered his head and said: 'What did you say?' We said: 'Did you hear?' He said: 'I sleep but my heart does not sleep.'"],[907,"We came as a delegation to Mu'awiya with Ziyad, and with us was Abu Bakra. We entered upon him, and Mu'awiya said to him: 'Narrate to us a hadith you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ, perhaps God will benefit us by it.' He said: 'Yes. The Prophet of God ﷺ used to like good dreams and ask about them.' A man said: 'O Messenger of God, I saw a dream. I saw as if a scale was suspended from heaven, and you and Abu Bakr were weighed, and you outweighed Abu Bakr. Then Abu Bakr was weighed against Umar, and Abu Bakr outweighed Umar. Then Umar was weighed against Uthman, and Umar outweighed Uthman. Then the scale was raised!' The Messenger of God ﷺ was upset by it, then said: 'A caliphate of prophethood, then God gives kingship to whomever He wills.' Mu'awiya became angry and shoved us by the napes of our necks, so we were expelled. Ziyad said to Abu Bakra: 'Could you not find any hadith of the Messenger of God ﷺ to narrate other than this?' He said: 'By God, I will not narrate anything but this until I part from him.' He said: Ziyad kept seeking permission until we were granted permission and admitted. Mu'awiya said: 'O Abu Bakra, narrate to us a hadith from the Messenger of God ﷺ, perhaps God will benefit us by it.' He said: I narrated to him again the like of his first hadith. Mu'awiya said to him: 'May your father perish! You tell us that we are kings! We are content to be kings.'"],[908,"While I was walking with the Messenger of God ﷺ and with me was a man, and the Messenger of God ﷺ was walking between us, he came upon two graves. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'The occupants of these two graves are being punished right now in their graves. Which of you will bring me a palm branch from this palm tree?' My companion and I raced, and I beat him and broke a palm branch from the tree and brought it to the Prophet ﷺ. He split it into two halves from its top and placed one half on one grave and the other half on the other, and said: 'It will be lightened for them as long as there is any moisture in them. They are being punished for backbiting and urine.'"],[909,"O father, I hear you supplicate every morning: 'O God, grant me well-being in my body; O God, grant me well-being in my hearing; O God, grant me well-being in my sight; there is no god but You,' repeating it three times in the evening and three times in the morning. And you say: 'O God, I seek refuge in You from disbelief and poverty; O God, I seek refuge in You from the punishment of the grave; there is no god but You,' repeating it three times in the evening and three times in the morning. He said: 'Yes, my son. I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ supplicate with these, so I like to follow his practice.'"],[910,"The supplication of the distressed: 'O God, Your mercy I hope for, so do not entrust me to myself for the blink of an eye, and set right all my affairs; there is no god but You.'"],[911,"'A group of my nation will certainly descend upon a land called al-Basra, and their number and palm trees will increase there. Then Banu Qantura' will come, broad-faced, small-eyed, until they descend upon a bridge of theirs called Dijla. The Muslims will split into three factions: as for one faction, they will take hold of the tails of camels and join the desert, and they will perish; as for another faction, they will take their own souls and disbelieve, so this one and that one are equal; as for another faction, they will place their families behind their backs and fight, and their slain are martyrs, and God, Mighty and Majestic, will grant victory to the rest of them.'"],[912,"Abu Bakrah entered upon them to give testimony, and a man stood up for him from his seat. Abu Bakrah said: The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'If a man stands up for you from his seat, do not sit in it'—or he said: 'You should not make a man stand up from his seat and then sit in it'—'and do not wipe your hand with the garment of one you do not own.'"],[913,"The Prophet ﷺ prayed the eclipse prayer as two rakʿahs."],[914,"Fast when you see it and break your fast when you see it; if it is obscured for you, then complete the number as thirty days."],[915,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was praying when al-Hasan came and climbed onto his back, so he placed him down gently. When he finished his prayer, he embraced him and kissed him. They said: 'O Messenger of God, you did with al-Hasan something you had not done before!' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'This son of mine is a chief; through him God, Mighty and Majestic, will reconcile two factions of the Muslims.'"],[916,"The Prophet ﷺ delayed the evening prayer for eight nights. Abu Bakrah said: 'If you were to hasten this prayer, it would be better for our standing in prayer at night!' And he did so."],[917,"He came to the Prophet ﷺ out of breath, and bowed before reaching the row. When the Prophet ﷺ finished his prayer, he said: 'Who did this?' Abu Bakrah said: 'I did.' He said: 'May God increase you in eagerness, but do not do it again.'"],[918,"The Prophet ﷺ led his companions in the fear prayer: he prayed two rakʿahs, then these went to the positions of those, and those came and he prayed two rakʿahs with them. Thus the Messenger of God ﷺ had four and the people had two rakʿahs each."],[919,"A people who entrust their affairs to a woman will never prosper."],[920,"Whoever kills a muʿāhad without just cause, God has forbidden Paradise to him."],[921,"There is no sin more deserving that its punishment be hastened for its doer in this world, along with what is stored up for him in the Hereafter, than injustice and severing ties of kinship."],[922,"The Night of Decree was mentioned in the presence of Abu Bakrah. Abu Bakrah said: As for me, I seek it only in the last ten, based on a hadith I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ. I heard him say: 'Seek it in the last ten: on the ninth remaining, or the seventh remaining, or the fifth remaining, or the third remaining, or the last night.' And Abu Bakrah used to pray during the first twenty days of Ramadan as he prayed the rest of the year, but when the last ten entered, he exerted himself."],[923,"Nabīdh was steeped for Abu Bakrah in a clay jar. Abu Barzah returned from an absence and stopped at Abu Bakrah's house before going to his own home. He did not find Abu Bakrah in his house, so he stood before a woman of his named Maysah and asked her about Abu Bakrah and his condition. He looked and saw the jar containing the nabīdh, and said: 'What is in this jar?' She said: 'Nabīdh for Abu Bakrah.' He said: 'I wish you had put it in a waterskin.' Then he left, and she ordered that the nabīdh be transferred to a waterskin and hung it up. Abu Bakrah came and she told him about Abu Barzah and his arrival. Then he noticed the waterskin and said: 'What is this waterskin?' She said: 'Abu Barzah said such and such, so I transferred your nabīdh to the waterskin.' He said: 'I will not drink any of it. By God, if you put honey in a jar it would be forbidden to me, and if you put wine in a waterskin it would be lawful for me. We have known what we were forbidden: we were forbidden from the dubbaʾ, the naqīr, the ḥantam, and the muzaffat. As for the dubbaʾ, we, the tribe of Thaqīf in al-Ṭāʾif, used to take gourds, hollow them out, and place bunches of grapes in them, then bury them and leave them until they fermented and then died down. As for the naqīr, the people of al-Yamāmah used to hollow out the trunk of a palm tree and crush ripe and unripe dates in it, then leave it until it fermented and then died down. As for the ḥantam, they were jars in which wine used to be brought to us. As for the muzaffat, they are these vessels that have this pitch in them.'"],[924,"I was at the funeral of ʿAbd al-Raḥmān b. Samura, and Ziyād and men from his clients were walking on their heels in front of the bier, saying: \"Gently, gently, may Allah bless you!\" He said: Abū Bakra caught up with them in one of the alleys of al-Mirbad, and he charged at them on the mule and struck at them with the whip, and said: \"Let go, by the One who honored the face of Abū al-Qāsim ﷺ, I have seen us in the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ almost trotting with it.\""],[925,"\"If a man points a weapon at his brother, they are both on the edge of Hell, and if he kills him, they both fall into it together.\""],[926,"\"Whoever claims descent from someone other than his father, while knowing that he is not his father, Paradise is forbidden to him.\""],[927,"On the authority of Abū Bakra regarding His saying: 'A throng from the former generations, and a throng from the latter generations' (Q 56:39–40), he said: \"Both of them are from this community.\""],[928,"Ibn ʿĀmir went out and ascended the minbar wearing thin clothes, and Abū Bilāl said: \"Look at your amir wearing the clothing of the wicked!\" Abū Bakra said from beneath the minbar: \"I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: 'Whoever humiliates the authority of Allah, Allah will humiliate him.'\""],[929,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited in the Friday prayer: 'Glorify the name of your Lord Most High' (Q 87) and 'Has there come to you the account of the Overwhelming?' (Q 88)."],[930,"\"Begging is a scratch with which a man scratches his face, so whoever wishes may keep it on his face and whoever wishes may leave it, except that a man asks in a matter he cannot do without, or asks one in authority.\" Zayd b. ʿUqba said: I narrated this to al-Ḥajjāj b. Yūsuf, and he said: \"Ask me, for I am one in authority.\""],[931,"\"The best treatment you use is cupping.\""],[932,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed the morning prayer and then said: \"Is there anyone here from Banū so-and-so? Your companion is detained at the gate of Paradise by a debt he owes.\""],[933,"The Prophet ﷺ called out twice: \"Who is here from Banū so-and-so?\" No one answered him, then on the third time a man stood up and said: \"I am.\" He said: \"What prevented you from answering me the first two times? I did not mention your name except for good. Your companion is detained at the gate of Paradise by a debt he owes.\" He said: So he paid it off on his behalf until no one demanded anything from him."],[934,"\"If you wish, hand him over to the punishment of Allah, and if you wish, ransom him.\""],[935,"\"Do not name your boy Aflaḥ (most successful), nor Rabāḥ (profit), nor Yasār (ease), nor Najīḥ (prosperous), for it may be said: 'Is he here?' and it will be said: 'No.'\""],[936,"\"Wear these white garments, for they are purer and more pleasant, and shroud your dead in them.\""],[937,"\"Whoever narrates from me a hadith that he thinks is a lie is one of the liars.\""],[938,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade prayer before sunrise, for it rises between the two horns of the devil or upon the two horns of a devil.\""],[939,"\"Do not be deceived by the call of Bilal or this whiteness until the dawn breaks like this.\""],[940,"\"Do not let the adhan of Bilal prevent you from suhur, nor the elongated dawn, but the dawn that spreads across the horizon.\""],[941,"\"When I narrate a hadith to you, do not add to it upon me. Four are among the best of speech, and it is from the Quran, and it does not harm you with whichever of them you begin: 'Subhan Allah', 'Al-hamdu lillah', 'La ilaha illa Allah', and 'Allahu akbar'.\""],[942,"\"Do not name your boy Aflah, or Najih, or Rabah, or Yasar.\""],[943,"\"Whoever misses Jumu'ah without an excuse should give a dinar in charity; if he cannot find it, then half a dinar.\""],[944,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ prayed over a woman and stood at her middle."],[945,"\"If two guardians marry off a woman, the marriage belongs to the first of them, and if a man sells goods to two men, it belongs to the first of them.\""],[946,"\"The neighbor of a house has more right to the house.\""],[947,"\"Whoever kills his slave, we kill him, and whoever mutilates him, we mutilate him, and whoever castrates him, we castrate him.\""],[948,"Whoever encloses a wall around land, it belongs to him."],[949,"The Prophet ﷺ ordered a caller, and he called out on a rainy day: 'Pray at your dwellings.'"],[950,"The warranty for a slave is four days."],[951,"Every boy is held in pledge for his 'aqiqah."],[952,"Whoever owns a closely related mahram, he is free."],[953,"Do not curse with the curse of Allah, nor with the wrath of Allah, nor with the Fire."],[954,"A man should not outbid his brother in a sale, nor propose to a woman when his brother has proposed to her."],[955,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ commanded us to pray in sheep pens, and not to pray in camel resting places, for they were created from devils."],[956,"He forbade throwing pebbles and said: 'It neither catches game nor injures an enemy, and pebble-throwing breaks the tooth and puts out the eye.'"],[957,"The Prophet ﷺ recited Surah al-Fath on the day of the conquest and made a trilling sound. Were it not that people would gather around me, I would have imitated that tone for you."],[958,"The first person I saw wearing khuffs in Islam was al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah. He came to us while we were with the Messenger of Allah ﷺ wearing two black khuffs, and we began looking at them and marveling at them. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed, khuffs will become plentiful among you.' They said: 'O Messenger of Allah, what should we do?' He said: 'Wipe over them and pray.'"],[959,"A bag of fat was let down on the day of Khaybar, and I took it and clutched it, saying: 'This is mine; I will not give anyone any of it!' Then I turned and saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, and I felt ashamed before him."],[960,"What was forbidden to us of this drink? He said: Wine. He said: I said: Is this in the Quran? He said: I only narrate to you what I heard from Muhammad the Messenger — or the Messenger Muhammad ﷺ, either he began with the messengership or with the name — He said: I said: It is my law; meaning I have enough — meaning he said: He forbade al-hantam. He said: I said: What is al-hantam? He said: Green and white earthenware jars, and al-naqir and al-muzaffat. He said: I said: What is al-muzaffat? He said: That which has pitch put in it, from a vessel or otherwise, and al-dubba. He said: So I bought a small hide and soaked [the drink] in it and hung it."],[961,"He forbade al-khadhfa (throwing pebbles with the fingers)."],[962,"How was your prayer with the Messenger of God ﷺ? He said: He used to lead us in the mid-day prayer, which you call al-zuhr, when the sun declined. And he used to lead us in al-asr while the sun was still alive — and I forgot what he said about al-maghrib — and he used to lead us in al-isha not caring to delay it to a third of the night, and he disliked sleeping before it and talking after it. And he used to lead us in al-fajr and one of us would leave while he could recognize his companion. And he used to recite in it from sixty to one hundred [verses]."],[963,"Bilal used to give the call to prayer when the sun had declined, and the other said: When the sun had passed its zenith."],[964,"We went out on an expedition of ours and encamped at a place. A man bought a slave for a horse, and we remained the rest of our day and night. When it was time to depart, the man went to his horse to saddle it, but the other man seized him over the sale. They brought their dispute to Abu Barzah al-Aslami, and he said: Would you both accept that I judge between you with the judgment of the Messenger of God ﷺ? The Messenger of God ﷺ ruled that the two parties to a sale have the option as long as they have not separated."],[965,"I used to wish to meet a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ to ask him about the Khawarij. I met Abu Barzah al-Aslami on a day of Eid among people from his companions, and I said to him: Have you heard the Messenger of God ﷺ speak about the Khawarij? Abu Barzah said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ with my ears and saw him with my eyes. Some wealth was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ and he divided it. A black man with trimmed hair, wearing two white garments, came and he gave to those on his right and those on his left but gave him nothing. He came from behind him and said: By God, O Muhammad, you have not been just! The Messenger of God ﷺ said: By God, you will not find anyone after me more just to you than me. He said it three times. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'A people will emerge in the last days as if this man is from them. They recite the Quran but it does not go beyond their collarbones. They pass through Islam as an arrow passes through the game. Their mark is shaving. They will emerge until the last of them comes out with the Messiah. So when you meet them, kill them. They are the worst of creation and creatures.'"],[966,"He was on an expedition of his, and when he finished fighting, he said: 'Do you miss anyone?' They said: By God, we miss so-and-so and so-and-so and so-and-so. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Look, do you miss anyone?' They said: We miss so-and-so and so-and-so. He said: But I miss Julaybib, so search for him. They found him beside seven [men] whom he had killed, and then they killed him. The Prophet ﷺ was informed and he came to him and said: 'He killed seven, then they killed him! This one is from me and I am from him. He killed seven, then they killed him! This one is from me and I am from him.' He said it twice or three times. Then he gestured with his arms like this — and spread them out — and he was placed on the arms of the Prophet ﷺ until a grave was dug for him. He had no bier except the arms of the Prophet ﷺ until he was buried. He (the narrator) said: He did not mention washing."],[967,"Ghifar, may God forgive them, and Aslam, may God grant them peace."],[968,"The leaders are from Quraysh as long as they act by three things."],[969,"I was sitting on a riverbank in al-Ahwaz, and there was an old man praying who had taken hold of his mount's rein and placed it in his hand. The mount backed up, so he backed up with it. With us was a man from the Khawarij who began to insult him. When he finished his prayer, he said: I have heard your words. I fought with the Messenger of God ﷺ in such-and-such an expedition and such-and-such an expedition, and I witnessed his command and his facilitation. Holding my mount is easier for me than leaving it to go to its accustomed place, which would be hard for me."],[970,"Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad entered upon Maqil b. Yasar, and Maqil b. Yasar said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever enters into any of the prices of the Muslims to make it more expensive for them, it is incumbent upon God to throw him into the great fire on the Day of Resurrection."],[971,"Ubayd Allah b. Ziyad entered upon Maqil b. Yasar and said: Narrate to me a hadith you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ, perhaps God will benefit me! He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever is entrusted with a flock and dies while he deceives it, God has forbidden Paradise to him."],[972,"\"I had a sister who was sought in marriage from me, and I kept people away from her, until a paternal cousin of mine came to me and proposed to her, so I married her to him. They stayed together as long as Allah willed they stay together, then he divorced her with a divorce that gave him the right to take her back. Then he left her until her waiting period ended. Then he came to me proposing to her along with other suitors. I said, 'You fool! My sister was proposed to me and I kept people away from her, and you proposed to me and I favored you with her and married her to you, then you divorced her. Then you did not propose to her until her waiting period ended.' When the suitors came to me proposing to her, you came to propose to her! No, by Allah, besides whom there is no god, I will never marry her to you.'\" He said: Ma'qil said: \"About me this verse was revealed: 'And when you divorce women and they reach their term, do not prevent them from marrying their husbands when they agree among themselves on reasonable terms.'\" He said: \"And Allah, Mighty and Majestic, knew her need for him and his need for her, so this verse was revealed.\" So I said: \"I hear and obey!\" And I married her to him and expiated my oath."],[973,"\"Recite Ya-Sin over your dying ones.\""],[974,"\"Worship during turmoil is like emigration to me.\""],[975,"That two men brought a dispute to him concerning a piece of land. He said: I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever swears an oath to seize thereby the property of his brother will meet Allah, Mighty and Majestic, while He is angry with him.\""],[976,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade fadikh.\""],[977,"\"Jibril ﷺ was slow in coming to the Prophet ﷺ. A woman said: 'I think his companion has been slow in coming to him!' So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: 'By the morning brightness and by the night when it grows still, your Lord has not forsaken you, nor is He displeased.'\""],[978,"I witnessed the Prophet ﷺ giving a sermon on the day of sacrifice. He said: \"Whoever among you has slaughtered before the prayer, let him repeat another in place of his slaughtered animal. And whoever has not slaughtered, let him slaughter in the name of Allah.\""],[979,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ went out to prayer and his toe stubbed and bled. He said: \"Are you anything but a toe that has bled, and in the path of Allah what you have suffered.\""],[980,"\"Whoever prays the morning prayer is under the protection of Allah, Mighty and Majestic. And whoever violates Allah's protection, Allah will cast him on his face into the Fire.\""],[981,"That the Messenger of Allah ﷺ lodged them in a tent in the mosque so that it would be softer for their hearts. When they accepted Islam, they stipulated upon him that they would not be mustered, nor tithed, nor conscripted. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: \"You shall not be mustered, nor tithed, nor conscripted, and there is no good in a religion that has no bowing.\""],[982,"The last instruction the Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave me was: \"When you lead people in prayer, make the prayer light for them.\""],[983,"\"When one of you feels pain, let him place his hand where he feels the pain and then say: 'I seek refuge in the might of Allah and His power over all things from the evil of what I find,' saying that seven times.\""],[984,"I am Muhammad, and Ahmad, and al-Hashir, and the Prophet of repentance, and the Prophet of the malhama."],[985,"I came to Madinah for the ransom of Badr—he said he was then a polytheist—and entered the mosque while the Messenger of God ﷺ was praying the Maghrib prayer and recited in it al-Tur, and it was as if my heart was split by the recitation of the Quran."],[986,"A woman came to the Prophet ﷺ about something she mentioned to him, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to her, \"Come back to me.\" She said, \"O Messenger of God, what do you think if I come and do not find you—to whom should I go?\" He said, \"To Abu Bakr.\""],[987,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a road between Makkah and Madinah, and he said, \"The people of Yemen are about to come upon you like pieces of clouds—or a piece of cloud—they are the best of those on earth.\" A man from the Ansar said, \"And not us, O Messenger of God?\" He was silent. Then he said, \"And not us, O Messenger of God?\" He was silent. Then he said, \"And not us, O Messenger of God?\" He was silent. Then he said, \"Except you,\" a weak word."],[988,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ recite in the Maghrib prayer al-Tur."],[989,"When the Prophet ﷺ entered the prayer, he said the takbir: \"God is most great, greatly\"—he said it three times—\"and praise be to God, abundantly\"—he said it three times—\"and glory be to God morning and evening\"—he said it three times—\"I seek refuge in God from the accursed Satan, from his blowing, his spitting, and his prodding.\""],[990,"The washing from major impurity was mentioned before the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"As for me, I pour water over my head three times.\""],[991,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, your companions claim that there are no rewards for us in our stay in Makkah!\" He said, \"Your rewards will surely come to you even if you were in a hole.\" He leaned his head toward me and said, \"Among my companions there are hypocrites.\""],[992,"A prayer in this mosque of mine is better than a thousand prayers—or he said a hundred—in any other except the Sacred Mosque."],[993,"A Qurayshi has the strength of two men from others."],[994,"If the slave woman of one of you commits adultery, let him flog her; if she returns, let him flog her; if she returns, let him flog her; and if she returns a fourth time, let him sell her even for a rope of hair."],[995,"Two disputants came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, we adjure you by God to judge between us according to the Book of God, Mighty and Majestic!\" His opponent stood up—and he was more knowledgeable than him—and said, \"Yes, O Messenger of God, judge between us according to the Book of God and permit me to speak!\" He permitted him, and he said, \"O Messenger of God, my son was a servant for this man, and he committed adultery with his wife. I was told that my son was subject to stoning, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a servant. Then I asked the people of knowledge, and they told me that my son is subject to a hundred lashes and exile for a year, and that this man's wife is subject to stoning!\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"By Him in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, I will surely judge between you according to the Book of God: the hundred sheep and the servant are returned to you, and upon your son is a hundred lashes and exile for a year. And go, O Unays, to this man's wife; if she confesses, then stone her.\" He went to her and asked her, and she confessed, so he stoned her."],[996,"\"We prayed Maghrib with the Messenger of God ﷺ, then we went to the market, and if we shot arrows, we could see where they fell.\""],[997,"\"Whoever performs wudu' well, then prays two rak'ahs without being heedless in them, will be forgiven.\""],[998,"\"Whoever equips a warrior in the path of God, Mighty and Majestic, has indeed fought, and whoever looks after his family with good has indeed fought.\""],[999,"\"Do not curse the rooster, for it calls to prayer.\""],[1000,"\"There is no amputation for fruit or palm pith.\""],[1001,"\"Let the morning prayer be performed when it is light, for that is greater in reward.\""],[1002,"\"Whoever sows in the land of a people without their permission, he has no right to any of the crop, but he is entitled to his expenses.\""],[1003,"The Prophet ﷺ said to Bilal: \"Make the morning prayer light so that the people can see where their arrows fall.\""],[1004,"He was struck by an arrow while with the Messenger of God ﷺ in one of his expeditions. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: \"O Rafi', if you wish, I will remove the arrow and leave the head, and I will testify for you on the Day of Resurrection that you are a martyr.\" And he did so."],[1005,"We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ at Dhu al-Hulayfah in Tihamah, and the people became hungry and captured camels and sheep. The Messenger of God ﷺ came upon them after the pots had been set up, and he ordered the pots to be overturned. Then he divided among them, equating ten sheep to one camel. He said: Then a camel from the people's camels bolted, and the people had only a few horses. A man shot it with an arrow and stopped it. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"These camels have wild tendencies like those of wild animals. Whatever of them eludes you, do to it like this.\""],[1006,"We said: \"O Messenger of God, we will meet the enemy tomorrow and we have no knives. Can we slaughter with reeds?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Whatever lets the blood flow and the name of God is mentioned, then eat, except for the tooth and the nail. I will tell you about that: as for the tooth, it is bone, and as for the nail, it is the knife of the Abyssinians.\""],[1007,"\"We used to see no harm in sharecropping until Ibn Khadij claimed that the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade it.\""],[1008,"He forbade al-ḥaql (sharecropping for a fixed share of the produce)."],[1009,"The earnings of a cupper are vile, the dowry of a prostitute is vile, and the price of a dog is vile."],[1010,"When this verse was revealed: “When the victory of Allah and the conquest come” (Qur’an 110:1), the Messenger of Allah ﷺ recited it until he completed it, then said: “I and my companions are one group and the people are another group. There is no emigration after the conquest.”"],[1011,"Whoever has land, let him grant it to his brother and not lease it out."],[1012,"He narrated that his grandfather died and left a slave boy who was a cupper, a water-carrying camel, land, and a slave woman. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ ordered that the earnings of the cupper be spent on the fodder of the water-carrying camel, and he forbade [taking] the earnings of the slave woman. Regarding the land, he said: “Cultivate it or leave it.”"],[1013,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ call the adhan for prayer in the ear of al-Ḥasan when his mother Fāṭimah gave birth to him."],[1014,"The Prophet ﷺ borrowed a young camel from a man. The man came to him demanding repayment, so he ordered Abū Rāfiʿ to repay him. Abū Rāfiʿ said: “I find only a choice camel.” He said: “Give it to him, for the best of you—or he said: the best of people—are those who are best in repayment.”"],[1015,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent a man from Banū Makhzūm to collect zakah. He said to Abū Rāfiʿ: “Accompany me so that you may get something of it.” Abū Rāfiʿ said: “No, not until I go to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and ask him.” So he went to the Prophet ﷺ and asked him, and he said: “Zakah is not lawful for us, and the client of a people is one of them.”"],[1016,"The neighbor has more right to his adjacent property."],[1017,"The Prophet ﷺ gave Abū Rāfiʿ a short spear and ordered him to kill the dogs of Madinah. He killed them except for one dog. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and told him, so he ordered him to kill it."],[1018,"The Prophet of Allah ﷺ passed by me while I was prostrating and had tied back my hair, so he loosened it."],[1019,"He forbade branding on the face. Al-ʿAbbās said: “I will brand only on the farthest part of the bone,” so he branded on the farthest part of the two protruding hip bones."],[1020,"Al-Abbas built an upper room, and the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Demolish it.' He said: 'Should I give its price in charity?' He said: 'Demolish it,' three times."],[1021,"'Whoever intends the Hajj, let him hasten, for the sick may fall ill, the stray may be lost, and the need may arise.'"],[1022,"The Prophet ﷺ continued to recite the talbiyah until he threw the pebble at Jamrat al-Aqabah."],[1023,"A woman from Khath'am came to the Prophet ﷺ in the year of the Farewell Hajj and said: 'O Messenger of God, God's obligation upon His servants regarding the Hajj has overtaken my father, an old man who cannot keep himself steady on the mount. May I perform the Hajj on his behalf?' He said: 'Yes.'"],[1024,"He rode behind the Prophet ﷺ, and his mount did not raise a foreleg in the morning until he threw the pebble."],[1025,"'I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ eating cucumber with fresh dates.'"],[1026,"When the news of Ja'far's death reached the Prophet ﷺ, he said: 'Prepare food for Ja'far's family, for there has come to them what preoccupies them.'"],[1027,"'When the Messenger of God ﷺ returned from a journey, he would be met by me and al-Hasan. He would place one of us in front of him and the other behind him on the mount.'"],[1028,"One who witnessed 'Abd Allah b. Ja'far and 'Abd Allah b. al-Zubayr, with Ibn al-Zubayr cutting meat for 'Abd Allah b. Ja'far and feeding him, and Ibn Ja'far said: 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: The best meat is the back.'"],[1029,"When the news of the killing of Ja'far and his companions reached the Messenger of God ﷺ, he gave Ja'far's family three days' respite, then came to them and said: 'Bring out to me the children of my brother.' He said: Three were brought out, as if they were chicks: 'Abd Allah, 'Awn, and Muhammad were brought out. He called the barber and had their heads shaved, and said: 'As for 'Awn, he resembles me in appearance and character; as for Muhammad, he resembles our uncle Abu Talib.' He took 'Abd Allah by the hand, raised it, and said: 'O God, succeed Ja'far in his family, and bless 'Abd Allah in the transaction of his right hand.' He said: Their mother began to be anxious about them, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Do you fear poverty while I am their guardian in this world and the next?'"],[1030,"The Messenger of God ﷺ had cupping done on his head after he was poisoned."],[1031,"'The soul of the believer is a bird that clings to the trees of Paradise until God, Mighty and Majestic, returns it to his body.'"],[1032,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade killing women and children."],[1033,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ went on a raid, he would make it appear he was going elsewhere."],[1034,"\"As for this one, he has told me the truth. Stand until God decides your case.\" He said: So I stood, and some men of my people from Banu Salimah came back to me and said: \"By God, we do not know that you committed any sin in Islam before this. It would have been enough for your sin that the Messenger of God ﷺ ask forgiveness for you. Why did you not excuse yourself to the Messenger of God as those who stayed behind excused themselves to him?\" He said: By God, they kept reproaching me until I almost started to disbelieve myself. He said: So I said: \"Did anyone experience this along with me?\" He said: \"Two men experienced it with you; they were told what you were told.\" I said: \"Who are they?\" They said: \"Hilal b. Umayyah al-Waqifi and Murarah b. al-Rabi' al-'Amiri.\" They mentioned two righteous men who had been present at Badr, and in them I had an example. He said: And the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade speaking to us, the three men, among those who stayed behind from him. He said: So the people avoided us and did not speak to us. By God, I felt estranged from myself, and the earth seemed estranged to me in my own mind; it was not the earth I used to know. As for my two companions, they submitted and sat in their houses. As for me, I was the youngest and most vigorous of the people, so I would attend the prayer with the Muslims and walk in the markets, but no one would speak to me. I would come to the Messenger of God ﷺ and pray with him, then greet him and say to myself: \"Did he move his lips in reply to me?\" I would steal glances at him. When I turned to my prayer, he would turn toward me, but when I turned toward him, he would turn away from me. When the harshness of the Muslims toward us had gone on for a long time, I went to Abu Qatadah, who was my cousin and the dearest of people to me, and I spoke to him. By God, he did not speak to me. I said: \"O Abu Qatadah, I adjure you by God: do you know that I love God and His Messenger?\" He said: \"God and His Messenger know best.\" He said: So my eyes overflowed, and I climbed over the wall and went on. One day while I was in the market, a Nabatean from the Nabateans of Syria came to me with a letter from the king of Ghassan, and he was saying: \"Who will direct me to Ka'b b. Malik?\" The people began pointing to me. I took the letter, for I could read, and there it was from the king of Ghassan, and in it: \"To proceed: It has reached us that your companion has banished you. God would not place you in a house of humiliation or loss, so join us and we will console you!\" He said: I said: \"This too is part of the evil.\" I took the letter and headed to the oven with it and kindled it. When forty nights had passed since the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade speaking to us, the messenger of the Messenger of God ﷺ came to me and said: \"The Messenger of God commands you to keep away from your wife.\" I said: \"Should I divorce her, or what should I do with her?\" He said: \"Do not go near her.\" So I said to my wife: \"O woman, go to your family until God decides in this matter.\" And he sent the same to my two companions. He said: Then the wife of Hilal b. Umayyah came and said: \"O Messenger of God, Hilal is a helpless man and has no servant. Would you dislike me serving him?\" He said: \"No, but he must not come near you.\" She said: \"O Messenger of God, by God, he has made no movement toward anything of that since his affair began; he only weeps.\" Then some of my family said to me: \"Why don't you ask the Messenger of God permission regarding your wife, since he gave permission to the wife of Hilal?\" I said: \"By God, I will not do it. I am a young man and I do not know what the Messenger of God will say.\" He said: While I was in that state, on the morning of the fiftieth night since the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade speaking to us, I prayed the dawn prayer on the roof of a house of ours, then I sat in the state that God mentioned: \"the earth became straitened for them despite its vastness, and their own selves became straitened for them, and they thought there was no refuge from God except to Him,\" when I heard the voice of a caller raised on Mount Sal', and a man galloped a horse to me. The voice reached me faster than the horse: \"Rejoice, O Ka'b b. Malik!\" I fell down in prostration, and I knew that relief had come. The one whose voice I had heard came, and I took off two garments that were on me—by God, I owned no others—and gave them to him as a reward for good news. Then I borrowed two garments and put them on, and went to the Prophet ﷺ. Ka'b said: Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who was kind to me in my affair, told me that the Messenger of God ﷺ was with her that night. When a third of the night remained, our repentance descended upon him, and he said to her: \"O Umm Salamah, repentance has been accepted for Ka'b b. Malik and his two companions.\" She said: I said: \"O Messenger of God, shall I not send to him and give him the good news?\" He said: \"Then the people would crowd you and prevent you from sleeping the rest of the night.\" And the Messenger of God ﷺ announced God's acceptance of our repentance after he had prayed the dawn prayer. He said: So bearers of good news went to my two companions, and bearers of good news went to me. Ka'b said: I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ with the Muhajirun and Ansar around him, and his face was shining as if it were a piece of the moon. Whenever he was pleased with something, his face would shine. Talhah b. 'Ubayd Allah ؓ stood up for me, hurrying until he congratulated me and shook my hand. By God, no man among the Muhajirun stood up other than him, so Ka'b never forgot it for Talhah. He said: The Muslims began congratulating me on God's acceptance of my repentance, saying: \"May God's acceptance of repentance bring you joy, may God's acceptance of repentance bring you joy,\" until I reached the Messenger of God ﷺ. When he saw me, he said: \"Come, O Ka'b, and rejoice in the best day that has come upon you since the day your mother gave birth to you.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, is it from you or from God?\" He said: \"Rather, it is from God.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, part of my repentance is that I divest myself of all my wealth as charity to God and His Messenger.\" He said: \"O Ka'b, keep some of your wealth, for it is better for you.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, I will keep my share at Khaybar.\" And I said: \"O Messenger of God, God, Mighty and Majestic, saved me only by truthfulness, and part of my repentance is that I will never speak anything but truth as long as I live.\" Ka'b said: By God, I do not know anyone whom God has tested in truthful speech as He has tested me. By God, I have never deliberately told a lie since I said that to the Messenger of God ﷺ until this day of mine, and I hope God will protect me in what remains. He said: Then God, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: \"God has turned in mercy to the Prophet, and to the Muhajirun and the Ansar\"—the two verses together."],[1035,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said on the pulpit: \"I set out intending to inform you of the Night of Decree, but I was made to forget it. So seek it in the last ten nights, in the odd ones.\""],[1036,"He used to travel on Thursday."],[1037,"Whoever draws a sword against us is not one of us."],[1038,"The Messenger of God ﷺ used to lead us in the Friday prayer, and we would leave while we could not find shade from the walls to sit in."],[1039,"We raided with Abu Bakr ؓ against Hawazin, and I beat the people to the mountain, so I drove back a group of people and captured a woman from Fazarah who had a daughter among the most beautiful of the Arabs. Abu Bakr gave me the daughter of the Fazari woman as a prize. When we arrived, the Messenger of God ﷺ said to me: \"O Salamah, give me the woman, may your father be ransomed for God.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, I have not uncovered her!\" He said: \"Give her to me, may your father be ransomed for God.\" I said: \"She is yours, O Messenger of God.\" He said: Then he sent her to the people of Makkah and ransomed with her a captive who was in their hands."],[1040,"Ghifar—may God forgive them, and Aslam—may God, Mighty and Majestic, keep them safe."],[1041,"The best of our infantry is Salamah, and the best of our cavalry is Abu Qatadah."],[1042,"A man looked into the room of the Prophet ﷺ while the Prophet ﷺ had a comb with which he was scratching his head. He said: \"If I knew that you were looking, I would stand up and poke it into your eyes. Permission was only made because of seeing.\""],[1043,"We used to rejoice on Friday, and that was because we would go to an old woman who would make chard and barley for us, and we would eat it and then return, in the time of the Messenger of God ﷺ."],[1044,"The majority of those who prayed behind the Messenger of God ﷺ were people of knotted garments."],[1045,"The Messenger of God ﷺ died while he had a woolen cloak in the weaving."],[1046,"The Prophet ﷺ passed away when he was sixty-three, Abu Bakr ؓ when he was sixty-three, and Umar ؓ when he was sixty-three."],[1047,"Mu'awiyah seldom narrated from the Messenger of God ﷺ, but he had a speech on Fridays that he would deliver, reporting it from the Prophet ﷺ. He said: 'Whomever God intends good for, He gives him understanding in religion. This wealth is green and sweet, so whoever takes it with its due right is blessed in it. Beware of mutual praise, for mutual praise is slaughter.'"],[1048,"A life grant is permissible to its recipients."],[1049,"We were at Mu'awiyah's door, and he came out to us and said: 'What were you discussing?' We said: 'We were discussing the Ansar and their hadiths.' Mu'awiyah said: 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever loves the Ansar, God loves him, and whoever hates the Ansar, God hates him.'"],[1050,"Mu'awiyah gave a sermon and said: 'Why do some people pray a prayer that I accompanied the Messenger of God ﷺ and never saw him pray, and I heard him prohibit it?'"],[1051,"Talhah is among those who fulfilled their vow."],[1052,"We were with Mu'awiyah when the muezzin called to prayer, and he said the same as the muezzin, then said: 'Thus I heard your Prophet ﷺ.'"],[1053,"Mu'awiyah came out, and Ibn Amir stood up for him while Ibn al-Zubayr remained seated, and he was the more balanced of the two. Mu'awiyah said to Ibn Amir: 'Sit down, for I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: Whoever loves for men to stand up for him, let him take his seat in the Fire.'"],[1054,"The Night of Decree is the night of the twenty-seventh."],[1055,"Mu'awiyah said to a group of the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ: 'Do you know that the Messenger of God ﷺ prohibited tiger skins?' They said: 'O God, yes.' He said: 'And I bear witness.' He said: 'Do you know that the Prophet ﷺ prohibited wearing gold except in small pieces?' They said: 'O God, yes.' He said: 'Do you know that the Prophet ﷺ prohibited combining Hajj and Umrah?' They said: 'O God, no.' He said: 'By God, it is indeed with them.'"],[1056,"Mu'awiyah came to Madinah and addressed us. He took out a lock of hair and said: 'I did not think that anyone would do this except the Jews. The Messenger of God ﷺ called it falsehood.'"],[1057,"Mu'awiyah delivered a sermon and said: 'You have introduced an evil fashion. Surely the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade falsehood.'"],[1058,"Do not ride on silk brocade or leopard skins."],[1059,"Whomever God wills good for, He grants him understanding in religion."],[1060,"There was a fright in Madinah, and the people began to go this way and that. I entered the mosque, and there was Salim, the freedman of Abu Hudhayfah, sitting with his sword straps wrapped around him near the minbar—the minbar of the Prophet ﷺ. He said: I sat with Salim, and the Prophet ﷺ came and ascended the minbar and said: 'O people, should not your place of refuge have been to God and His Messenger? Should you not have done what these two believing men did?'"],[1061,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sent for me, saying: 'Put on your weapon and come to me.' I did so, and I entered upon him. He lowered his gaze at me and then raised it, and said to me: 'O 'Amr, I want to send you out on an expedition, and God will give you booty, and I will grant you a good share of wealth.' I said: 'O Messenger of God, by God, I did not become Muslim for the sake of wealth.' He said: 'O 'Amr, excellent is righteous wealth for a righteous man.'"],[1062,"'Amr b. al-'As said: 'O Messenger of God, who is the most beloved of people to you?' He said: ''A'ishah.' He said: 'I mean among men.' He said: 'Her father.'"],[1063,"I witnessed 'Amr b. al-'As when Muhammad b. Abi Bakr was brought to him—he had been governor over Egypt—and he was bound. 'Amr said to him: 'Do you have a guarantee of safety? Has anyone given you protection?' He did not mention that he had any guarantee. 'Amr said: 'I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: The humblest of the Muslims may grant protection on behalf of the Muslims.' He said: Then his neck was struck."],[1064,"'Amr b. al-'As grieved intensely at the time of death. His son 'Abd Allah said to him: 'Why this grief, when the Messenger of God ﷺ used to appoint you and keep you close?' He said: 'O my son, I will tell you about that. He used to do that, and by God, I do not know whether it was out of love or a conciliation he was using toward me. But I testify concerning two men that he departed this world loving them: the son of Umm 'Abd and the son of Sumayyah.'"],[1065,"He sent him to 'Ali to seek permission on behalf of Asma' bt. 'Umays, and he granted him permission. When he had finished his errand, the freedman asked 'Amr about that. He said: 'The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us—or he forbade—entering upon women without the permission of their husbands.'"],[1066,"I came to Syria and entered the mosque and said: 'O God, grant me a righteous companion to sit with.' He said: I sat down next to a man, and it was Abu al-Darda'. He said to me: 'Where are you from?' I said: 'From the people of Kufah.' He said: 'Is not among you the man of the cushion and the toothstick?'—meaning Ibn Mas'ud. Then he said: 'Is not among you the keeper of the secret that no one else knew?'—meaning Hudhayfah. Then he said: 'Is not among you the one whom God protected through the tongue of His Prophet ﷺ from Satan?'—meaning 'Ammar. Then he said: 'Do you know how 'Abd Allah used to recite: By the night when it covers, and the male and the female?' I said: 'He used to recite it: By the night when it covers and the day when it shines.' Abu al-Darda' said: 'By God, these people kept at me until they almost made me doubt.' Then Abu al-Darda' said: 'This is how we recite it, and this is how I heard it recited by the Messenger of God ﷺ.'"],[1067,"'Would any of you be unable to recite one third of the Qur'an in a night?' It was said: 'O Messenger of God, who can do that?' He said: 'Recite: Say, He is God, the One.'"],[1068,"“The thing I fear most for you is the misleading leaders.”"],[1069,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about His saying: “Those who believe and were mindful—for them is good news in the life of this world.” The Messenger of God ﷺ said: “It is the righteous dream that the Muslim sees or is seen for him.”"],[1070,"The Messenger of God ﷺ saw a woman far advanced in pregnancy at the door of a tent—or he said: a pavilion—and said: “Perhaps the owner of this tent has intercourse with her! I have considered cursing him with a curse that would enter the grave with him. How can he make him his heir while he is not lawful for him, and how can he enslave him while he is not lawful for him?”"],[1071,"“Nothing will be placed in the balance on the Day of Resurrection heavier than good character.”"],[1072,"“The sun has never risen but that God, Mighty and Majestic, sends two angels by its sides who call out, making all creation hear except the two heavy ones (humans and jinn): ‘O God, hasten for the spender a replacement, and give the withholder ruin.’ And the sun has never set but that God, Mighty and Majestic, sends two angels by its sides who call out, making all creation hear except the two heavy ones: ‘What is little and suffices is better than what is much and distracts.’”"],[1073,"“The one who gives charity or manumits a slave at the time of death is like the one who gives a gift after he is full.”"],[1074,"“The parent is the middle gate of Paradise, so if you wish, guard that gate, or waste it.”"],[1075,"When a guest would stay with Abu al-Darda’, he would say: “Are you staying, so we may pasture (the animals), or leaving, so we may feed (them)?” If he said, “Leaving,” he said: “I will tell you what the Messenger of God ﷺ told me. I said: ‘O Messenger of God, the wealthy have taken the world and the Hereafter; they pray as we pray, strive as we strive, remember as we remember, and give charity, while we have nothing to give.’ He said to me: ‘Shall I not tell you something that if you do it, no one who comes after you will catch you, and you will catch up with those who preceded you? Say God is greatest after every prayer thirty-four times, glorify Him thirty-three times, and praise Him thirty-three times. If you do that, you will catch up with those who preceded you, and no one who comes after you will catch you except one who says the like of what you said.’”"],[1076,"Two men brought a dispute over a span of land to Abu al-Darda’. Abu al-Darda’ said: “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘If you are in a land and hear two men disputing over a span of land, leave it.’ So Abu al-Darda’ left and went to Syria.”"],[1077,"“God, Mighty and Majestic, has finished with His creation regarding five things: his term, his action, his trace, his resting place, and his provision.”"],[1078,"“Whoever prays over a funeral has a qirat, and whoever follows it until its matter is concluded has two qirats.”"],[1079,"It was said to Thawban, the freedman of the Messenger of God ﷺ: “Narrate to us.” He said: “You have lied against me and said about me what I did not say.” They said: “Narrate to us.” He said: “I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: ‘No servant prostrates to God a prostration but that God, Mighty and Majestic, raises him a degree by it or removes from him a sin by it.’”"],[1080,"The best dinar is a dinar a man spends on his dependents, a dinar he spends on his riding beast in the way of God, and a dinar he spends on his companions in the way of God."],[1081,"The one who visits a sick person is in the orchards of Paradise until he returns."],[1082,"The cupper and the one cupped have broken the fast."],[1083,"The daughter of Hubayra came to the Prophet ﷺ with thick gold rings on her hand, and the Prophet ﷺ began striking her hand. She then went to Fatima complaining to her. Thawban said: The Prophet ﷺ entered upon Fatima while I was with him, and she had taken a gold necklace from her neck and said: This was gifted to me by Abu Hasan—and the necklace was in her hand. The Prophet ﷺ said: \"O Fatima, would it please you that people say Fatima bt. Muhammad has a necklace of fire in her hand?\" Then he left without sitting. Fatima took the necklace, sold it, bought a slave with it, and set the slave free. This reached the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: \"Praise be to God who saved Fatima from the Fire through me.\""],[1084,"The Hour will not come until tribes of my community join the polytheists and worship idols, and when the sword is placed among my community it will not be lifted from them until the Day of Resurrection."],[1085,"The nations are about to call one another against you just as people call one another to their food bowl. It was said: Is it because of our small number? He said: \"No, but you will be like the scum of a flood. Weakness will be placed in your hearts, and fear of you will be removed from the hearts of your enemy because of your love of this world and your hatred of death.\""],[1086,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ vomit, and he broke his fast."],[1087,"Who will guarantee me one thing, and I will guarantee—or I will take responsibility—for him Paradise? Thawban said: I said: I will, O Messenger of God. He said: \"Do not ask anyone for anything.\" He said: Thawban would sometimes drop his whip and dismount to pick it up himself."],[1088,"Umar b. Abd al-Aziz sent for Abu Sallam al-Habashi, and he was brought on the postal mount until he came to him. Umar said: I sent for you to hear from you directly the hadith of Thawban about the Hawd. Abu Sallam said: I heard Thawban say: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: \"My Pool extends from Adan Abyan to Amman al-Balqa; its cups are like the number of stars in the sky; its water is sweeter than honey—or he said: whiter than milk. Whoever drinks a drink from it will never thirst after it. The first to come to me at it are the poor of my community.\" Umar stood up and said: O Messenger of God, who are they? He said: \"They are the disheveled-haired, dusty-clothed, who do not marry women accustomed to luxury and for whom doors of rulers are not opened.\""],[1089,"Remain upright, though you will not be able to fully do so. Know that the best part of your religion is prayer, and no one maintains ablution except a believer."],[1090,"For every instance of forgetfulness, there are two prostrations after the salutation."],[1091,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey, and we halted for rest, each of us spreading his camel's foreleg as a pillow. Then I woke during the night and found no one before the camel of the Messenger of God ﷺ, so I set out and came upon Muadh b. Jabal and Abdullah b. Qays standing. I said to them: Have you seen the Messenger of God ﷺ? They said: No. I heard a sound like the whirring of a millstone. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ came to us and said: \"A messenger from my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, came to me and gave me the choice between admitting half of my community to Paradise and intercession, and I chose intercession.\" We said: We adjure you by God and by companionship to make us among the people of your intercession. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"You are among the people of my intercession.\" A man would come and say: O Messenger of God, make me among the people of your intercession, and he would say: \"You are among the people of my intercession.\" When they crowded around him, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O God, I call you as witnesses that my intercession is for those of my community who die not associating anything with God.\""],[1092,"I witnessed the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray over the funeral of a man from the Ansar, and I heard him say: 'O Allah, send blessings upon him, forgive him, have mercy on him, grant him well-being, pardon him, wash him with water, snow, and hail, purify him from sins and transgressions as a white garment is purified from dirt, give him in exchange for his abode a better abode and a family better than his family, and protect him from the trial of the grave and the punishment of the Fire.' 'Awf said: I saw myself in that place wishing I were in the place of the Ansari man because of what I heard of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ supplicating for him."],[1093,"When 'So glorify the name of your Lord, the Most Great' was revealed, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Place it in your bowing.' When 'Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High' was revealed, the Prophet ﷺ said: 'Place it in your prostration.'"],[1094,"Three times the Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to forbid us to pray in or to bury our dead: when the sun rises brightly until it ascends, when the sun stands still at midday until it declines, and when it turns yellow for setting until it sets."],[1095,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ distributed sacrificial animals among his Companions, and I got a jadha'ah. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Sacrifice it.'"],[1096,"Verses were revealed to me, none greater than them were ever seen."],[1097,"They were on a journey and we wanted him to lead us in prayer, but he refused and said: 'Let one of you go forward until I tell you why I will not lead you. I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever leads a people in prayer and completes the prayer for them, then it is for him and for them; but if he does not, then for them is the completeness and for him is the deficiency.'"],[1098,"It was said to 'Uqbah b. 'Amir: 'We have neighbors who drink wine and do such and such.' He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: Whoever sees a private matter and conceals it is like one who revives a buried infant from its grave.'"],[1099,"Allah, Mighty and Majestic, will enter into Paradise three people because of a single arrow: the one who made it, seeking reward for his craft; the one who shoots it; and the one who hands it to him."],[1100,"Shoot and ride, but that you shoot is more beloved to me than that you ride. Everything a man amuses himself with is false except his shooting with his bow, training his horse, or playing with his wife, for these are from truth. Whoever abandons archery after having learned it has disbelieved in what he learned."],[1101,"I performed ablution and entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was delivering a sermon. I heard him say: 'Whoever performs ablution and does it well, then prays the prescribed prayer, guarding it and understanding it until he completes it, will be like the day his mother gave birth to him.'"],[1102,"Whoever frees a slave, it will be his ransom from the Fire, limb for limb."],[1103,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ gave a sermon and recited: 'And prepare against them whatever you are able of power.' Then he said: 'Verily, power is archery. Verily, power is archery.'"],[1104,"The Prophet ﷺ was brought a necklace containing a bead mounted in gold. A man bought it for seven — or nine — dinars, and mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, who said: 'No, not until it is separated, the one from the other.'"],[1105,"I was given the seven long surahs in place of the Torah, the ones of a hundred verses in place of the Psalms, the oft-repeated ones in place of the Gospel, and I was favored with the detailed surahs."],[1106,"I saw Wathilah b. al-Asqaʿ — and he was a Companion — praying in the mosque of Damascus wearing two sandals. He spat beneath his left foot, then rubbed it into the ground. When he finished praying, I said: 'You do this while you are among the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ?' He said: 'Thus I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do.'"],[1107,"O Messenger of God, I live in a land whose people are People of the Book: they eat pork and drink wine. What about their vessels and cooking pots? He said: 'Leave them as long as you can do without them. If you cannot do without them, rinse them with water — or he said: wash them — then cook in them and eat.' He said: And I think he said: 'And drink.'"],[1108,"I said: O Messenger of God, I send out my dog and it catches game? He said: 'If you send out your trained dog and mention God's name, and it catches, then eat. If you send out your dog that is not trained and it catches, then if you reach it while it is still alive and slaughter it, eat; if you do not reach it alive, do not eat.'"],[1109,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade every beast of prey with fangs and the meat of domestic donkeys — or he said: 'tame ones.'"],[1110,"The Prophet ﷺ allotted him a piece of land — I do not think but that he said: 'in Hadramawt.'"],[1111,"Suwayd b. Tariq asked the Prophet ﷺ, saying: 'O Messenger of God, we have grapes that we press' — and he mentioned wine, so he forbade him. He said: 'It is a remedy!' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Rather, it is a disease.'"],[1112,"Salama b. Yazid stood up to the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was giving a sermon after the afternoon prayer, and said: 'What do you think if there are rulers over us after you who demand our rights and deny us ours?' He remained silent. Then he repeated the question, and it was as if he became angry, and remained silent. Al-Ashʿath pulled him and said: 'By God, I will keep asking him until the sun sets or he answers me!' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Upon them is what they are charged with, and upon you is what you are charged with. Hear and obey them.'"],[1113,"I prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'I will memorize his prayer!' He began the prayer, said the takbir, and raised his hands until they reached his ears. He took his left hand with his right. When he wanted to bow, he said the takbir and raised his hands as he had raised them when beginning the prayer, and placed his palms on his knees when bowing. When he raised his head from bowing, he raised his hands as he had raised them when beginning the prayer. Then he prostrated, spread his left foot, and sat on it. He said: Then he placed his right palm on his right thigh and his left hand on his left thigh, and began supplicating like this."],[1114,"He prayed with the Prophet ﷺ: he would say the takbir when going down and when rising, raise his hands upon the takbir, and turn in salutation to his right and to his left."],[1115,"He prayed with the Prophet ﷺ, and he turned in salutation to his right and to his left."],[1116,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was praying when a man entered and said: Allahu akbar kabiran, wal-hamdu lillahi kathiran, wa subhana Allahi wa bi-hamdihi bukratan wa asilan. When he finished praying, he said: 'Who said those words?' The man said: 'I did, O Messenger of Allah, and I intended by them nothing but good.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'I saw the gates of heaven opened, and they did not stop until they reached the Throne.'"],[1117,"He prayed with the Prophet ﷺ, and when he recited 'not of those who earned anger nor of those who went astray,' he said: 'Amin,' lowering his voice, and he placed his right hand over his left hand, and he said the salam to his right and to his left."],[1118,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ when two disputants came quarreling over land. One of them was Imru' al-Qays b. 'Abis al-Kindi and the other was Rabi'a b. 'Aydan. Imru' al-Qays said: 'O Messenger of Allah, this man seized my land!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Your proof.' He said: 'I have no proof!' He said: 'Then he takes an oath.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah, then he will take it!' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'You have no right except that.' When he stood up to swear, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Indeed, if he swears falsely to take his land, he will meet Allah while He is angry with him.'"],[1119,"A man delivered a speech in the presence of the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'Whoever obeys Allah and His Messenger has been guided, and whoever disobeys them has gone astray.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'Be quiet! What a bad speaker you are.'"],[1120,"Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better than it, let him do what is better and let him expiate his oath."],[1121,"A man asked 'Adi b. Hatim for two hundred dirhams, and he became angry at the smallness of the amount and swore not to give it to him. Then he said: 'Were it not that I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better than it, let him do what is better and let him expiate his oath,\" I would not give you anything. But it is yours, to be deducted from my allowance.'"],[1122,"He narrated that 'Adi b. Hatim was asked for something and he swore not to give it, then he gave it. He said: 'I heard the Messenger of Allah ﷺ say: \"Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better than it, let him do what is better and let him expiate his oath.\"'"],[1123,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the mi'rad (a blunt arrow). He said: 'If it strikes with its edge and kills, then eat; but if it strikes with its side and kills, then it is a waqidh (beaten to death), so do not eat.' I said: 'I send my dog.' He said: 'If you send your dog upon game and mention Allah's name, and it catches it, then eat. But if it eats from it, then do not eat, for it has caught it for itself.' I said: 'I send my dog and find with my dog another dog that has caught it, and I do not know which of them caught it!' He said: 'Then do not eat, for you mentioned Allah's name only over your dog and not over the other.'"],[1124,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I send my dog upon game.'"],[1125,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, I throw the mi'rad at game.' He said: 'If you throw the mi'rad at game and it pierces it, then eat; but if it does not pierce it, then do not eat.' Or he said: 'If it strikes with its side, then do not eat.'"],[1126,"I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, we have trained dogs. We send them upon game and they catch it for us.' The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'If they are trained and they catch it for you and kill it, then eat as long as no other dog has shared in it.'"],[1127,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ: 'O Messenger of Allah, I catch game but I find nothing to slaughter it with except a sharp stone or a stick!' He said: 'Cause the blood to flow with whatever you wish, and mention the name of Allah.'"],[1128,"I said: O Messenger of God, my father used to maintain kinship ties. He said: And he mentioned noble character traits, then said: Your father desired a matter and attained it."],[1129,"I said: O Messenger of God, food that I do not leave except out of religious scrupulousness. He said: Then do not leave any food in which you have imitated Christianity."],[1130,"The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned the Fire, sought refuge from it and turned his face away. Then he mentioned the Fire, sought refuge from it and turned his face away. Then he mentioned the Fire, sought refuge from it and turned his face away. Then he said: Guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date. If you cannot find that, then with a good word."],[1131,"Guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date. If you cannot find that, then with a good word."],[1132,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when highway robbery was mentioned. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Only a short time will pass before a woman travels between Makkah and Madinah with no one holding her camel's halter. By God, only a little time will pass before a man takes a handful of gold and finds no one to accept it from him. And there is none of you but will meet God, Mighty and Majestic, with no interpreter between him and Him. He will look to his right and left and see nothing but the Fire. So whoever among you can protect his face from the Fire, even with half a date, let him do so."],[1133,"There is none of you but will meet God, Mighty and Majestic, on the Day of Resurrection with no interpreter between him and Him. He will look to his right and left and see nothing but what he has sent forth. Then he will look and behold, it is the Fire. So let each of you guard against the Fire, even with half a date."],[1134,"Guard yourselves against the Fire, even with half a date. If you cannot find that, then with a good word."],[1135,"When I arrived in Madinah, it had reached me that the Messenger of God ﷺ was saying: I hope that God will place His hand in my hand. He said: He took me to his saddle and a slave girl threw us a cushion - or he said: a rug - and we sat. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Do you deny that it should be said: There is no god but God? Is there any god other than God? He said: I said: No. He said: Do you deny that it should be said: God is greater? Is there anything greater than God? He said: I said: No. He said: The Jews are those upon whom is wrath, and the Christians are astray. He said: I said: Then I am a Muslim. He said: I saw the face of the Messenger of God ﷺ brighten with joy at that, or light up at that."],[1136,"I said: O Messenger of God, I shoot game and find it the next day with my arrow in it. He said: If you find your arrow in it and you know that it killed it, and you do not see any trace of a wild animal on it, then eat."],[1137,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ -"],[1138,"A short spear was set up for the Messenger of God ﷺ and he prayed facing it, while a donkey and a woman passed behind it."],[1139,"I bought a slave who was a cupper, and my father took his cupping instruments and broke them. I said to him: Are you breaking them? He said: The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade the price of blood, the price of a dog, the earnings of a prostitute, and the stud fee of a stallion."],[1140,"The Prophet ﷺ went out in the midday heat—in the midday heat—in the midday heat—to al-Batha', performed ablution, and prayed Zuhr as two rak'ahs and 'Asr as two rak'ahs, with a spear planted in front of him."],[1141,"The Prophet ﷺ cursed the image-maker."],[1142,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, and I saw this white spot from him,\" and he pointed to the tuft of hair under his lower lip. It was said, \"What were you doing at that time, O Abu Juhaifah?\" He said, \"I was trimming arrows and fletching them.\""],[1143,"\"I do not eat reclining.\""],[1144,"\"The most grateful of people to God are the most grateful of them to people.\""],[1145,"I said, \"O Messenger of God, we claim that we are from you or that you are from us\"—Abu Bishr was uncertain—so the Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"We are the Banu al-Nadr b. Kinanah. We do not disown our father, nor do we follow our mother's line.\" Al-Ash'ath then said, \"I will find no one—or no one will be brought to me—who denies that Quraysh are from Kinanah except that I will flog him with the prescribed punishment.\""],[1146,"Whoever swears a false oath in order to thereby seize his brother's property will meet God while He is angry with him. Then al-Ash'ath b. Qais came to us and said, \"What did Abu 'Abd al-Rahman narrate to you?\" We told him, and he said, \"He spoke the truth. This verse was revealed concerning me: 'Indeed, those who purchase with the covenant of God and their oaths a small price—those will have no share in the Hereafter' to the end of the verse. I disputed with a man over a well before the Prophet ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Your evidence or his oath.' I said, 'Then he will swear, and he is sinful.'\""],[1147,"Whoever swears a binding oath in order to thereby seize property while he is lying in it will meet God, the Mighty and Majestic, while He is angry with him. Then al-Ash'ath b. Qais al-Kindi came out to us and said, \"What did Abu 'Abd al-Rahman narrate to you?\" We said, \"Such and such.\" He said, \"He spoke the truth. It was revealed concerning me. I disputed with a man over a well before the Messenger of God ﷺ, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said to me, 'Your evidence or his oath.' I said, 'Then he will swear, and he is sinful.' So the Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'Whoever swears a binding oath in which he is lying in order to thereby seize property will meet God, the Mighty and Majestic, while He is angry with him.' And it was revealed: 'Indeed, those who purchase with the covenant of God and their oaths a small price' to the end of the verse.\""],[1148,"\"We complained to the Messenger of God ﷺ about the intense heat of the sun-baked ground, but he did not respond to our complaint.\""],[1149,"We entered upon Khabbab after he had been cauterized. He said, \"I do not know anyone who met with as much affliction as I did. I remained during the time of the Prophet ﷺ without finding a single dirham, while in the corner of this house of mine there are forty thousand. Were it not that the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade us—or forbade anyone—from wishing for death, I would have wished for it.\""],[1150,"\"I was a blacksmith in the pre-Islamic era. Al-'As b. Wa'il owed me some dirhams, so I went to him to demand payment. He said, 'I will not pay you until you disbelieve in Muhammad!' I said, 'I will not disbelieve in Muhammad ﷺ until God causes you to die and then resurrects you.' He said, 'Leave me until I die and then am resurrected, so that I will have wealth and children, and then I will pay you!' So this verse was revealed: 'Have you seen the one who disbelieved in Our verses and said, \"I will surely be given wealth and children\"?'\""],[1151,"\"I prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ, and he recited 'When the sun is wrapped up.' When he reached this verse, 'And by the night when it darkens, and by the dawn when it breathes,' I said to myself: What is 'the night when it darkens and the dawn when it breathes'?\""],[1152,"\"Horses have goodness tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection.\" It was said, \"O Messenger of God, what is the goodness?\" He said, \"Reward and booty.\""],[1153,"\"Horses have goodness tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection.\" It was said, \"O Messenger of God, what is the goodness?\" He said, \"Reward and booty.\""],[1154,"\"Horses have goodness tied to their forelocks.\" It was said, \"And what is the goodness?\" He said, \"Reward and spoils.\""],[1155,"The Prophet ﷺ was seen wiping the cheek of a horse, and he was asked about that. The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"Gabriel rebuked me concerning the horse.\""],[1156,"There are phrases that follow the prayers, whose utterer—or he said doer—will not be disappointed: to magnify God thirty-four times, glorify Him thirty-three times, and praise Him thirty-three times after every prayer. Al-Hakam said, \"I have not abandoned them since.\""],[1157,"Ka'b b. 'Ujrah met me and said, \"Shall I give you a gift? The Prophet ﷺ came out and we said, 'We know how to greet you, but how should we invoke blessings upon you?' He said, 'Say: O God, bless Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You blessed the family of Abraham; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious. O God, grant grace to Muhammad and the family of Muhammad as You granted grace to the family of Abraham; indeed You are Praiseworthy, Glorious.'\""],[1158,"I sat with Ka'b b. 'Ujrah in this mosque and asked him about God's saying, Mighty and Majestic: \"Then a ransom of fasting or charity or sacrifice.\" He said, \"It was revealed concerning me. I was carried to the Messenger of God ﷺ while lice were falling on my face. He said, 'I did not think the hardship had reached you to what I see! Slaughter a sheep.' I said, 'I cannot find one.' So it was revealed: 'Then a ransom of fasting'—three days—'or feeding six poor people half a saa'. It was revealed specifically about me, but it is general for you.\""],[1159,"\"When one of you performs ablution and then goes out for prayer, he is in prayer. So let none of you interlace his fingers after he performs ablution or after he enters prayer.\""],[1160,"The Messenger of God ﷺ entered the mosque upon us and said, \"Who is here? Do you hear? After me there will be rulers who act contrary to obedience to God. Whoever shares in their deeds and helps them in their wrongdoing is not of me and I am not of him. And whoever does not share in their deeds and does not help them in their wrongdoing is of me and I am of him.\""],[1161,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ at the time of al-Hudaybiyyah, in a state of ihram, while the polytheists had blocked us from the House. I had long hair, and lice were falling on me—or he said on my face. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to me, \"Do your parasites bother you?\" I said, \"Yes.\" He said, \"Shave your head and fast three days, or feed six poor people, or offer a sacrifice.\""],[1162,"I went out with Ka'b b. 'Ujrah on the day of Eid, and he did not pray before it. When we had prayed, he saw the people all as one going to the mosque. He said, \"What are these doing?\" I said, \"They are going to the mosque.\" He said, \"This is an innovation and an abandonment of the Sunnah.\""],[1163,"The Messenger of God ﷺ looked upon us while we were discussing the Hour. He said, \"The Hour will not come until there are ten signs: the smoke, the Dajjal, the Beast, the rising of the sun from the west, three sinkings—a sinking in the east, a sinking in the west, and a sinking in the Arabian Peninsula—and the descent of Jesus son of Mary, the opening of Gog and Magog, and a fire that comes out from the depths of Aden that drives the people to the gathering place.\""],[1164,"When the death of the Negus was reported to the Prophet ﷺ, he said: \"Your brother has died in a land other than yours, so stand and pray over him.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ arranged them in rows behind him and prayed over him."],[1165,"The Messenger of God ﷺ mentioned the Beast and said: \"It has three emergences in the course of time. It will emerge in the farthest part of the desert, and its mention will not enter the town—meaning Makkah. Then it will stay hidden for a long time, then it will emerge a second time, lesser than that, and its mention will rise among the desert dwellers and enter the town—meaning Makkah.\" The Messenger of God ﷺ then said: \"Then while the people are in the greatest mosque, the most sacred, the best, and the most noble—the Sacred Mosque—nothing will startle them except that it is bellowing between the Corner and the Station, shaking dust from its head. The people will scatter from it in all directions and together, but a band of believers will remain firm, knowing they cannot thwart God. It will begin with them and polish their faces until they become like a brilliant star. Then it will turn away through the land; no seeker can catch it, and no fugitive can escape it. Even a man will seek refuge from it in prayer, and it will come to him from behind and say: 'O so-and-so, only now are you praying!' He will turn to face it, and it will brand his face, then go on. And people will share in wealth and accompany one another in the towns, the believer being known from the disbeliever, until the believer says: 'O disbeliever, pay me my due!' and until the disbeliever says: 'O believer, pay me my due!'\""],[1166,"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade plunder and mutilation."],[1167,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: 'O Messenger of God, show me the seal!' He said: 'Put your hand in.' So I put my hand into the opening of his garment and began to feel, looking at the seal, and there it was on the cartilage of his shoulder, like an egg. That did not prevent him from praying for me while my hand was still in the opening of his garment."],[1168,"I came to the Prophet ﷺ and found his buttons undone, and you would never see Mu'awiya and his son except with their buttons undone."],[1169,"In the time of the Prophet ﷺ we were strongly forbidden from standing between the pillars in prayer."],[1170,"Fasting three days of the month is equivalent to fasting for a lifetime and its breaking."],[1171,"A man from the Ansar used to frequent the Prophet ﷺ with a son of his. One day the Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: 'O so-and-so, do you love him?' He said: 'Yes, O Messenger of God, may God love you as I love him!' The Prophet ﷺ later missed him and asked about him. They said: 'O Messenger of God, his son has died.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Is he not pleased—or: are you not pleased—that on the Day of Resurrection he will not come to any gate of Paradise except that he will come running until he opens it for you?' A man said: 'O Messenger of God, is that for him alone or for all of us?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Rather for all of you.'"],[1172,"When the people of Syria become corrupt, there is no good in you. A group of my community will remain victorious, unharmed by those who forsake them, until the Hour comes."],[1173,"My father came to the Prophet ﷺ after he had milked and tied the udder."],[1174,"Ibn Mas'ud went to bring the Prophet ﷺ a tooth-stick, and people began to look at the thinness of his legs, or they marveled at the thinness of his legs. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'They are heavier in the balance than Mount Uhud.'"],[1175,"The Prophet of God ﷺ said one day in his sermon: \"Indeed my Lord—or: indeed my Lord—commanded me to teach you what you do not know of what He taught me this day. Every wealth I have bestowed upon My servant is lawful. I created all My servants as upright, and the devils came to them and lured them away from their religion, forbidding them what I had made lawful for them and commanding them to associate with Me that for which I sent down no authority. And God, Mighty and Majestic, looked upon the people of the earth and despised them, Arab and non-Arab, except for remnants of the People of the Book. He said: 'O Muhammad, I sent you only to test you and to test through you. I have sent down to you a Book that water does not wash away; you read it asleep and awake.' And God, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me to burn Quraysh. I said: 'My Lord, then they would split my head and leave it like a loaf of bread!' He said: 'Extract them as they extracted you, and raid them; you will be raided against. Spend, and it will be spent on you. Send an army, and We will send five times its like. Fight with those who obey you against those who disobey you.'\" And he said: \"The people of Paradise are three: a ruler who is moderate, charitable, and guided; a man who is merciful and tender-hearted toward every Muslim relative; and a poor person who is chaste and charitable. The people of the Fire are five: the weak one with no restraint, those among you who are mere followers seeking neither family nor wealth; the treacherous one whose greed never remains hidden, however small, without betraying it; a man who does not rise in the morning or fall in the evening without trying to deceive you about your family and wealth—and he mentioned miserliness or lying—and the foul-mouthed miser.\""],[1176,"I said: O Messenger of God, a man from my people insults me while he is beneath me? The Messenger of God ﷺ said: The two who insult each other are two devils who exchange accusations and lies, so whatever they say falls on the one who began it until the wronged one transgresses."],[1177,"\"Whoever picks up a lost item should have two just witnesses - or one just witness - and should not conceal it or hide it. If its owner comes, he is more entitled to it; otherwise it is God's property which He gives to whom He wills.\""],[1178,"I gave the Messenger of God ﷺ a gift - or he said: a she-camel - and he said to me: \"Have you become Muslim?\" I said: No. He refused to accept it and said: \"We do not accept the leftover of the polytheists.\""],[1179,"I gave the Messenger of God ﷺ a she-camel - or he said: a gift - and he said: \"Have you become Muslim?\" I said: No. He said: \"I have been forbidden from the leftover of the polytheists.\""],[1180,"He asked the Prophet ﷺ about alliances in Islam, and he said: There is no alliance in Islam, but hold fast to the alliance of the Jahiliyyah."],[1181,"His father instructed his sons at his death, saying: When I die, do not wail over me, for the Messenger of God ﷺ was not wailed over."],[1182,"And he mentioned charity, and said: Let none of you bring a sheep that has a defect."],[1183,"\"He prayed with the Prophet ﷺ and he would turn away from both his sides.\""],[1184,"\"The dream of a believer is one of forty parts of prophethood, and it is suspended on the leg of a bird as long as it is not related. When it is related, it falls.\" He said: And I think he said: \"Do not relate it except to a beloved or a wise person.\""],[1185,"I said: O Messenger of God, how does God bring the dead to life? He said: Have you not passed by a barren valley, then passed by it green? He said: Yes. He said: \"Thus is the resurrection,\" or he said: \"Thus does God bring the dead to life.\""],[1186,"I said: O Messenger of God, my mother maintained family ties and did such and such, but she died a polytheist! Where is she? He said: \"She is in the Fire.\" He said: I said: O Messenger of God, where is your mother? He said: \"Are you not content that your mother be with my mother?\""],[1187,"I said: O Messenger of God, my father is an old man who cannot perform Hajj or Umrah or travel! He said: Perform Hajj on behalf of your father or Umrah."],[1188,"Our Lord, Mighty and Majestic, laughs at the despair of His servants and the nearness of His relief. I said: 'O Messenger of God, does the Lord, Blessed and Exalted, laugh?' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Yes.' He said: 'We will never be deprived of good from a Lord who laughs.'"],[1189,"The Prophet ﷺ disliked being asked, but when Abu Razin asked him, he was pleased. He said: I said: 'O Messenger of God, where was our Lord, Mighty and Majestic, before He created the heavens and the earth?' He said: 'He was in a cloud, above which was no air and below which was no air. Then He created the Throne upon the water.'"],[1190,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, will each of us see his Lord on the Day of Resurrection?' He said: 'Yes.' I said: 'What is the sign of that in His creation?' He said: 'Do you not each see the moon when it is alone with it?' I said: 'Yes.' He said: 'God, Mighty and Majestic, is greater.'"],[1191,"There are no two witrs in one night."],[1192,"I said: 'O Messenger of God, one of us may be in prayer and touch his private part; should he repeat the ablution?' He said: 'No, it is only a part of you.'"],[1193,"It is not lawful for a woman to refuse her husband, even on the back of a saddle."],[1194,"The Messenger of God ﷺ was asked: 'May a man pray in a single garment?' He remained silent until the prayer time arrived, then he prayed in a single garment, wrapping its two ends together."],[1195,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform ablution and rub his forearms."],[1196,"The Messenger of God ﷺ went out to pray for rain. He turned his back to the people, faced the qibla, turned his cloak inside out, and prayed two rak'ahs with the people, reciting aloud."],[1197,"I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ lying on his back in the mosque, with one of his legs placed over the other."],[1198,"Shall I not perform ablution for you as the Messenger of God ﷺ did? We said: 'Yes.' So he rinsed his mouth and sniffed water with a single handful three times, then washed his face three times, then washed his forearms twice each, then wiped his head, bringing his hands forward and back, and washed his feet three times each. Then he said: 'This is how the ablution of the Messenger of God ﷺ was.'"],[1199,"He saw the call to prayer in a dream, so he came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. He said: 'Then Bilal called the adhan.' He said: 'My uncle came to the Prophet ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I see the dream, yet Bilal gives the adhan!' He said: 'Then you give the iqama.' He said: 'So my uncle gave the iqama.'"],[1200,"I asked the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about bird omens, and he said: “It is something you find in your hearts, so let it not hinder you.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, there are people who go to soothsayers.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not go to them.”"],[1201,"I prayed with the Prophet ﷺ, and a man next to me sneezed, so I said: “May Allah have mercy on you.” The people stared at me, and I said: “Woe to my mother! Why are you looking at me while I am praying?” They began striking their hands on their thighs to silence me. When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ finished his prayer, by my father and mother, I had never seen before or after him anyone better at teaching than him. By Allah, he did not scowl at me, insult me, or strike me, but he said to me: “In this prayer of ours, nothing of people's speech is fitting; it is only prayer, glorification, praise, and recitation of the Qur'an” – or something like what the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said. I had sheep grazing between Uhud and al-Jawwaniyyah, with a slave girl of mine among them. One day I checked on them and saw that a wolf had taken one of the sheep. I am a human being and felt regret as people do, so I raised my hand and slapped her hard. I came to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he made it seem grave to me. I said: “O Messenger of Allah, should I not free her?” He said: “Call her.” So I called her. He said to her: “Where is Allah?” She said: “In the sky.” He said: “Who am I?” She said: “You are the Messenger of Allah.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ then said: “Free her, for she is a believer.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, among us are people who draw lines (for divination).” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A prophet among the prophets used to draw lines; whoever matches his line, that is it.” I said: “Among us are people who practice bird omens.” He said: “It is something they find in their hearts, but it should not hinder them.” I said: “O Messenger of Allah, among us are people who go to soothsayers.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Do not go to them.”"],[1202,"There has been no prophet who did not warn his nation about the Dajjal. Indeed he is blind in the left eye, and on the right eye there is a thick white film. Between his eyes is written “kafir” – meaning the letters k, f, r. With him will come two valleys, one of them a garden and the other a fire. His fire is a garden and his garden is a fire. The Dajjal will say to the people: “Am I not your Lord? I give life and cause death.” With him will be two prophets, and I know their names and the names of their fathers. If I wished I could name them. One of them will be on his right and the other on his left. He will say: “Am I not your Lord? I give life and cause death.” One of them will say: “You lie,” but no one will hear him except his companion. The other will say: “You speak truth,” and the people will hear him. That is a trial. Then he will travel until he comes to Madinah and say: “This is the town of that man,” but he will not be permitted to enter it. Then he will travel until he comes to Syria, and Allah will destroy him at the pass of Afiq."],[1203,"The caliphate in my nation is thirty years, then there will be kingship.” Then Safinah said: “Hold on: the caliphate of Abu Bakr, and the caliphate of Umar – twelve years and six months, the caliphate of Uthman – twelve years, then the caliphate of Ali completes the thirty. I said: What about Mu'awiyah? He said: He was the first of the kings."],[1204,"We came as the delegation of Thaqif to the Prophet ﷺ, and the Ahlafis stayed with al-Mughirah b. Shu'bah, and he lodged the Malikis in his tent. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to come to us and talk to us after the late evening prayer until he would shift from one foot to the other from the length of standing. Most of what he talked to us about was the complaint against Quraysh. He would say: “We were in Makkah oppressed and weak. When we came to Madinah, we took our due from the people, and the turns of war were against us and for us.” One night he was late in coming to us at the time he used to come, then he came to us. We said: “O Messenger of Allah, you were late tonight at the time you used to come to us.” The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “A portion of the Qur'an came to me, and I wanted not to go out until I had recited it” – or he said: “completed it.” When morning came, we asked the companions of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about the portions of the Qur'an: how do you divide it into portions? They said: “Three, five, seven, nine, eleven, thirteen, and the portion of the Mufassal.”"],[1205,"My grandfather gestured to me to hand him his sandals while he was praying. I handed them to him, and he put them on while praying. When he finished praying, he said: “I saw the Messenger of Allah ﷺ praying in his sandals.”"],[1206,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ in a tent, and there was no one among the people awake except me. A man came and whispered to him, and he said: “Go and kill him.” Then he called him back and said: “Does he not bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah?” He said: “Yes.” He said: “I have been commanded to fight people until they bear witness that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah. If they bear witness to it, they have protected their blood and property from me” – or he said: “they are protected” – “except by its right.”"],[1207,"I saw the Prophet ﷺ perform istawkafa three times.” I said: “What is ‘istawkafa three times’?” He said: “He poured water on his hand three times.”"],[1208,"We came to the Prophet ﷺ in the delegation of Thaqif and stayed with him for half a month. I saw him turn to his right and to his left (after prayer)."],[1209,"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ performed ablution and wiped over his sandals."],[1210,"Whoever washes on Friday, performs the major ablution, comes early, walks and does not ride, for every step he has the reward of fasting and praying for a year."],[1211,"On the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the Ka'bah and locked the door behind him. Al-Fadl b. Abbas, Uthman b. Talhah, Usamah b. Zayd, and Bilal entered with him. When they came out, I raced the people and beat them. I said to Bilal: “Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray?” He said: “Between the two front pillars, opposite the entrance.”"],[1212,"\"The Prophet ﷺ used to wipe over the leather socks and the turban.\""],[1213,"\"We were only forbidden from praying before sunrise, for it rises between the two horns of a devil,\" or he said: \"upon the two horns of a devil.\""],[1214,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ when he passed by a man being cupped. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"The cupper and the one cupped have broken their fast.\""],[1215,"Two traits I memorized from the Prophet ﷺ. He said: \"God, Mighty and Majestic, loves excellence in all things. So when you slaughter, slaughter well, and when you kill, kill well. Let each of you sharpen his blade and give ease to his animal.\""],[1216,"\"Whoever prays to be seen has associated partners with God; whoever fasts to be seen has associated partners with God; whoever gives charity to be seen has associated partners with God.\" Awf b. Malik said: \"Will God not intend what was for Him from that and accept it and leave aside what is other than that?\" He said: Shaddad said: \"I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: 'God, Mighty and Majestic, said: I am the best of partners, or the best of dividers. Whoever associates partners with Me, his deed, whether small or great, is for My partner, and I am free of it.'\""],[1217,"\"The worst of this community will surely follow those who came before them, just as one arrow feather matches another.\""],[1218,"\"The shrewd one is he who calls himself to account and works for what comes after death, while the helpless one is he who lets his soul follow its desires and yet hopes in God.\""],[1219,"The Messenger of God ﷺ named him Bashir, and his name before that was Zahm."],[1220,"While I was walking alongside the Messenger of God ﷺ holding his hand—or he said: holding my hand—he said to me: \"O son of al-Khasasiyah, why have you come to resent God? You are walking alongside the Messenger of God ﷺ.\" I said: \"I do not resent God in anything, may my father and mother be your ransom. Every good God has done for me, every good God has done for me.\" He said: Then the Messenger of God ﷺ came upon the graves of the polytheists and said: \"These have gone ahead with much good, these have gone ahead with much good.\" Then he came upon the graves of the Muslims and said: \"These have attained much good, these have attained much good.\" Then the Messenger of God ﷺ glanced and saw a man walking among the graves wearing two sandals. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"O owner of the two sandals, throw off your two sandals.\" When the man saw the Messenger of God ﷺ, he threw them away."],[1221,"I wanted to fast two days consecutively, so I mentioned that to Bashir. He said: \"The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade it and said: 'The Jews do that. But fast, and when night comes, break your fast.'\""],[1222,"We were sitting with the Messenger of God ﷺ when a woman came to him with a child or two children of hers, carrying them, and another young son. He said: I think she was pregnant. He said: I think she did not ask the Messenger of God ﷺ for anything that day except that he gave it to her. When she turned away, the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"Carriers, bearers, merciful ones. Were it not for what they do to their husbands, those among them who pray would enter Paradise.\""],[1223,"I witnessed the Messenger of God ﷺ during the Farewell Pilgrimage and heard him say: \"God, Mighty and Majestic, has given every possessor of a right his right, so there is no bequest to an heir. The child belongs to the bed, and the stone to the adulterer. Their reckoning is with God. Whoever claims descent from other than his father or affiliates himself with other than his patrons, upon him is the curse of God, continuous until the Day of Resurrection. Indeed, it is not lawful for a woman to give anything from her husband's wealth except with his permission.\" A man said: \"O Messenger of God, not even food?\" He said: \"That is the best of our wealth.\""],[1224,"Debt is to be repaid, and borrowed property is to be returned, and the gift given for temporary use is to be given back, and the guarantor is liable."],[1225,"Ablution expiates what came before it, and prayer becomes supererogatory.” It was said, “Did you hear it from the Messenger of God ﷺ?” He said, “Not once, not twice, not three, not four, not five.”"],[1226,"God, Mighty and Majestic, created the creation and decreed the decree and took the covenant of the prophets while His Throne was upon the water. So the people of Paradise are its people, and the people of the Fire are its people."],[1227,"One who is disobedient to parents will not enter Paradise, nor one who reminds others of his favors, nor one who denies the divine decree."],[1228,"Blessed is the one who saw me and believed in me, and blessed seven times is the one who did not see me and believed in me."],[1229,"Among the people I most envy is a servant who has a share of prayer, who obeys his Lord and increases his worship in secret, who is not pointed at with fingers, who is obscure among people, whose livelihood is just enough, whose death comes quickly, whose inheritance is little, and whose weepers are few."],[1230,"God, Mighty and Majestic, sent me as guidance and mercy for the worlds, and commanded me to eradicate stringed instruments, wind instruments, idols, crosses, and the affairs of the pre-Islamic era. And my Lord swore by His might and majesty—or by His oath: No servant of My servants drinks a gulp of wine deliberately in this world but that I will give him to drink in its place from the pus on the Day of Resurrection, whether forgiven or punished. And no one gives it to drink to a weak Muslim child but that I will give him to drink in its place from the pus on the Day of Resurrection, whether forgiven or punished. And no one leaves it out of fear of Me but that I will give him to drink it in the enclosure of holiness. Their selling is not lawful, nor their buying, nor trading in them, and their price is forbidden."],[1231,"When a Muslim performs ablution and does it well, then if he sits, he sits forgiven, and if he prays, it is a merit for him.” It was said to him, “Or a supererogatory prayer?” He said, “Supererogatory prayers were only for the Prophet ﷺ.”"],[1232,"I was with Abu Umamah when heads of the Kharijites were brought and set up on the steps of Damascus. He said, “Dogs of the Fire”—he said it three times—“the worst of those slain under the shade of the sky. The best of those slain are those whom they killed and who killed them.” He said it three times. I said, “Something you heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ or something you say by your own opinion?” He said, “Then I would be bold, then I would be bold. Rather, it is something I heard from the Messenger of God ﷺ.”"],[1233,"A people of this community will spend the night on food, drink, amusement, and play, and will wake up transformed into apes and pigs. And they will be struck by sinking and pelting until people wake up and say, ‘The tribe of so-and-so was swallowed up last night,’ and ‘The house of so-and-so was swallowed up last night,’ specifically. And He will send upon them a storm of stones from the sky as it was sent upon the people of Lot upon tribes among them and upon houses. And He will send upon them the barren wind that destroyed ‘Ad upon tribes among them and upon houses because of their drinking wine, their wearing silk, their taking female singers, their consuming usury, and their severing ties of kinship.” And one trait Ja‘far forgot."],[1234,"The Messenger of God ﷺ left off the two leather socks on his feet during the expedition of Tabuk for three days."],[1235,"Excellent, excellent! Five things, how heavy they are: ‘Glory be to God,’ ‘Praise be to God,’ ‘There is no god but God,’ ‘God is greatest,’ and a righteous child who dies and his parent seeks reward for him."],[1236,"It was said: 'O Messenger of God, what was the beginning of your affair?' He said: 'The supplication of my forefather Ibrahim and the good tidings of 'Isa son of Maryam (God's blessings be upon them both), and my mother saw that a light came forth from her by which the palaces of Syria were illuminated.'"],[1237,"\"A man was taken to the gate of Paradise, and he raised his head and saw written on the gate of Paradise: 'Charity is [rewarded] tenfold, and a loan is [rewarded] eighteenfold, because the one who takes a loan does not come to you except when he is in need, whereas charity may be given to one who is wealthy.'\""],[1238,"\"There is no servant who sends blessings upon me but the angels send blessings upon him as long as he sends blessings upon me, so let the servant do little of that or much.\""],[1239,"A woman from Fazara was brought to the Prophet ﷺ, and she had married a man for [a dower of] two sandals. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to her: 'Are you content with yourself and your property for two sandals?' She said: 'Yes.' So he approved it."],[1240,"I cannot count—or he said: how numerous—how many times I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ using the tooth-stick while he was fasting."],[1241,"It became dark once while we were on a journey, and the qiblah was unclear to us, so each man among us prayed in the direction he faced. When it cleared, some of us had prayed away from the qiblah and some had prayed toward it. We mentioned that to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: 'Your prayer has been accepted,' and the verse was revealed: 'Wherever you turn, there is the face of God.'"],[1242,"I was with the Prophet ﷺ during the tawaf, and his sandal strap broke. I said: 'O Messenger of God, hand it to me and I will fix it!' He said: 'This is a privilege, and I do not like privilege.'"],[1243,"About perpetual fasting he said: \"He has neither fasted nor broken his fast.\""],[1244,"I came upon the Prophet of God ﷺ while he was reciting 'The mutual rivalry for piling up diverts you,' and he was saying: 'The son of Adam says, \"My wealth, my wealth,\" but what do you have of your wealth, son of Adam, except what you eat and consume, or wear and wear out, or give in charity and send forth?'"],[1245,"\"There is no man who seeks hospitality from a people and the guest wakes up deprived, except that every Muslim is obliged to help him until he takes the hospitality of his night from their crops and wealth.\""],[1246,"\"Whoever leaves behind wealth, it is for his heirs, and whoever leaves behind dependents, they are our responsibility\"—he said: and sometimes he said: \"then to God and His Messenger\"—\"and I am the heir of the one who has no heir; I pay his blood-money and inherit from him, and the maternal uncle is the heir of the one who has no heir; he pays his blood-money and inherits from him.\""],[1247,"\"The guest's night is a right upon every Muslim. Whoever wakes up with the guest at his courtyard, it is a right upon him\"—or he said: \"a debt\"—\"if he wishes he may claim it, and if he wishes he may leave it.\""],[1248,"\"Whoever grows a gray hair in Islam—or he said: in the path of God—it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection, as long as he does not dye it or pluck it.\""],[1249,"I saw myself when I was a quarter of Islam. I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, who has followed you upon this matter? He said: A free man and a slave."],[1250,"We besieged with the Prophet ﷺ the fortress of al-Ta'if, and I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever shoots an arrow in the path of God, it is for him equal to freeing a slave. That day I shot sixteen arrows. Then I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever shoots an arrow in the path of God, Mighty and Majestic, it is for him a degree in Paradise. Whoever grows a gray hair in Islam, it will be light for him on the Day of Resurrection. Any Muslim man who frees a Muslim man, God, Mighty and Majestic, will make for him, as a shield, every bone of his bones a freed slave from the Fire. And any Muslim woman who frees a Muslim woman, God, Mighty and Majestic, will make for her, as a shield, every bone of her bones a freed slave from the Fire."],[1251,"There was a treaty between Mu'awiya and the Byzantines. He was traveling in their lands, and when the treaty expired, he raided them. There was a man on a mount—or on a horse—saying: God is greatest. Loyalty, not treachery—twice—and it was 'Amr b. 'Abasa al-Sulami. Mu'awiya said to him: What are you saying? 'Amr said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: Whoever has a treaty between him and a people, let him not loosen a knot nor tighten it until its term has elapsed or he gives them notice on equal terms. So Mu'awiya returned with the people."],[1252,"There was some exchange between 'Ammar and Khalid b. al-Walid, so 'Ammar complained to the Messenger of God ﷺ. The Messenger of God ﷺ said to him: O Khalid, whoever is hostile to 'Ammar, God is hostile to him; whoever hates him, God hates him; and whoever reviles 'Ammar, God reviles him."],[1253,"\"The people with the severest punishment on the Day of Resurrection are those who inflict the severest punishment on people in this world.\""],[1254,"We were sitting in the mosque of the Messenger of God ﷺ when some people came praising 'Uthman and extolling him, while al-Miqdad was in a corner of the mosque. When he heard them praising him, he stood up, took some pebbles, and began throwing them at their faces. 'Uthman said: What is this? He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: When you see the flatterers, throw dust in their faces—or he said: in their mouths—or he said: pebbles."],[1255,"A man began praising a servant of 'Uthman, so al-Miqdad went and began throwing dust in his face. 'Uthman said to him: What is this? He said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say: When you see the flatterers, throw dust in their faces."],[1256,"It was only a mercy from God. If you had awakened your two companions, they would have gotten some of it. I said: By Him who sent you with the truth, I do not care, when you get it and I get your leftover, who among the people misses it."],[1257,"\"God, Mighty and Majestic, revealed to Yahya b. Zakariyya five words to act upon and to command the Children of Israel to act upon. It was as if he was slow about them, so God, Mighty and Majestic, revealed to 'Isa: Either you convey them or they will be conveyed. 'Isa came to him and said: God has commanded you with five words to act upon and to command the Children of Israel to act upon. Either you inform them or I inform them. He said: O Spirit of God, do not do that; I fear that if you precede me with them, the earth may swallow me or I may be punished. He said: So he gathered the Children of Israel in the Holy House until the mosque was full and they sat on the balconies. Then he addressed them saying: God, Mighty and Majestic, has revealed to me five words and commanded the Children of Israel to act upon them. The first of them: Do not associate anything with God, for the likeness of one who associates partners with God is like a man who bought a slave with his pure wealth of gold or silver, then lodged him in a house and said: Work and bring to me. But the slave began bringing to someone other than his master. Which of you would be pleased for his slave to be like that? God, Mighty and Majestic, created you and provided for you, so do not associate anything with Him. When you stand for prayer, do not turn aside, for God, Mighty and Majestic, turns His face toward the face of His servant as long as he does not turn aside. He commanded you to fast, and the likeness of that is like a man in a group with a pouch of musk; all of them love to find its scent. The breath of the fasting person is sweeter to God than the scent of musk. He commanded you to give charity, and the likeness of that is like a man whom the enemy captured and bound him to his neck or brought him near to strike his neck. He began saying to them: Would you let me ransom myself from you? He began giving a little and a lot until he ransomed himself. He commanded you to remember God frequently, and the likeness of that is like a man whom the enemy pursued swiftly in his tracks until he reached a fortified fortress and secured himself in it. Likewise, the servant does not escape from Satan except by remembrance of God.\""],[1258,"\"And I command you with five things God, Mighty and Majestic, commanded me with: the congregation, hearing and obedience, emigration, and jihad in the path of God. Whoever separates from the congregation by a handspan has thrown off the yoke of Islam or faith from his neck—or faith from his head—unless he returns. Whoever calls with the call of Jahiliyya is among the crouching ones of Hell.\" It was said: O Messenger of God, even if he fasts and prays? He said: \"Even if he fasts and prays. Call one another by the call of God with which He named you: Muslims, believers, servants of God.\""],[1259,"The Messenger of God ﷺ sought forgiveness for the first row three times and for the second once."],[1260,"Two men from the People of the Book, one said to his companion: 'Let us go to this prophet.' He replied: 'He must not hear this, or he will have four eyes.' So they came to him and asked him about nine clear signs. The Prophet ﷺ said: 'Do not associate anything with God, do not kill, do not steal, do not commit adultery, do not practice sorcery, do not consume usury, do not falsely accuse a chaste woman, do not flee from battle, and do not take an innocent person to a ruler to have him killed or destroyed. And upon you Jews in particular, do not transgress on the Sabbath.' They kissed his hands and feet and said: 'We bear witness that you are a prophet.' He said: 'What prevents you from following me?' They said: 'David prayed that there would never cease to be a prophet among his descendants, and we fear that if we follow you, the Jews will kill us!' Abu Dawud once said: 'And do not falsely accuse a chaste woman, or do not flee from battle.'"],[1261,"I went early to Safwan b. 'Assal al-Muradi and he said: 'What brings you, O Zirr?' I said: 'Seeking knowledge.' He said: 'Shall I give you good news?' Abu Dawud said: Hammad b. Salama said: 'None of them said it, and he raised the hadith: The angels lower their wings for the seeker of knowledge, pleased with what he seeks.'"],[1262,"I went early to Safwan b. 'Assal and said: 'Something has stirred in my mind about wiping over the leather socks. Have you heard anything from the Messenger of God ﷺ about that?' He said: 'We were with the Prophet ﷺ on a journey'—or 'traveling'—'and he commanded us to wipe over them for three days and their nights, from defecation, urination, and sleep, but not from major impurity.'"],[1263,"Have you heard anything from the Messenger of God ﷺ about passionate love?' He said: 'Yes. We were with the Messenger of God ﷺ on a march or a raid, and a bedouin called him with a loud voice: \"O Muhammad, O Muhammad, O Muhammad.\" It was said to him: \"Woe to you, lower your voice, for you have been forbidden from raising the voice!\" But he kept calling him like that, and the Prophet ﷺ answered him accordingly, saying: \"Here I am.\" He said: \"What do you think of a man who loves a people but has not yet caught up with them?\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"A man is with the one he loves.\"'"],[1264,"Safwan did not cease telling me until he mentioned the gate of repentance on the western side, its width forty years or a journey of forty years. It will not cease to be open until the sun rises from its direction. That is His saying: On the day when some of the signs of your Lord come, no soul will benefit from its faith if it had not believed before or earned good through its faith."],[1265,"I came to Madinah and was stricken with severe hunger. I entered an orchard, took an ear of grain, ate from it, and put some in my garment. The owner of the orchard came, beat me, and took what was in my garment. He said: We went to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'You did not teach him when he was ignorant, nor feed him when he was hungry.' Then he ordered for me half a wasq of barley."],[1266,"The Messenger of God ﷺ said a word to me that I would not love to have red camels in exchange for it. The Messenger of God ﷺ was brought captives, and he gave to some people and withheld from others. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'We give to people whose alarm and anxiety we fear, and we entrust others to what God has placed in their hearts of faith; among them is Amr b. Taghlib.'"],[1267,"Among the signs of the Hour is that you will fight a people whose sandals are hair, and among the signs of the Hour is that you will fight a people whose faces are like hammered shields, and among the signs of the Hour is that merchants will increase and the pen will appear."],[1268,"I spent the night with the Prophet ﷺ and used to hand him the water for ablution at night. I would hear him for a long portion of the night saying: 'God hears the one who praises Him,' and I would hear him for a long portion of the night saying: 'Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds.'"],[1269,"O Burayda al-Aslami, collect for me the weight of a date pit of gold. He collected it for me, and he said: 'Go with this to them.' I brought it to them and they accepted it from me and rejoiced. Then I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and he saw me saddened. He said: 'What is the matter with you, O Rabi'a?' I said: 'O Messenger of God, I came to a noble people and they accepted it from me and rejoiced, but I have nothing with which to hold a wedding feast.' He said: 'O Burayda, collect for him the price of a ram.' They collected for me the price of a great ram. Then he said: 'Go to A'isha and tell her: The Messenger of God says to you: Hand over to him that food.' I came to her and she said: 'Take the basket; by God, we have nothing else.' He said: I took it and came to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he said: 'Go with this to them, and let this be prepared as bread among them, and let this be cooked as meat among them.' I brought it to them and they said: 'As for the bread, we will take care of it for you; you take care of the meat.' So I went with the ram to some of my companions and we cooperated on it. When we finished it, I went with it and held the wedding feast, and I invited the Messenger of God ﷺ and he accepted my invitation."],[1270,"The Messenger of God ﷺ gave me a piece of land and gave Abu Bakr a piece of land. He said: We disputed about a cluster—meaning a palm tree. I said: 'It is from my land!' Abu Bakr said: 'It is from my land!' He said: 'O Abu Bakr, do you not see? Look, do you not see? It is from my land.' He refused and said to me a word that he regretted. He said: 'O Rabi'a, say to me the like of what I said to you so that it may be retribution.' I said: 'No.' He said: 'By God, then I will surely seek help against you!' I said: 'You? Yes.' He went intending to go to the Prophet ﷺ and I followed him. Some people from my tribe came and said: 'May God have mercy on Abu Bakr; he is the one who said to you what he said and he seeks help against you!' They went with me, and I said to them: 'Do you know who this is? This is Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, the second of two when they were in the cave. He is coming to the Messenger of God while angry, and the Messenger of God ﷺ will become angry because of his anger, and God, Mighty and Majestic, will become angry because of the anger of His Messenger, and Rabi'a will perish. Go back!' So I sent them back and went on. He had preceded me to the Prophet ﷺ and told him the story. When I came, he said to me: 'O Rabi'a, what is between you and al-Siddiq?' I said: 'O Messenger of God, he said something to me and told me: Say the like of what I said to you so that it may be retribution. I said: I will not say to you the like of what you said to me.' The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Indeed, do not say to him the like of what he said to you, but say: May God forgive you, O Abu Bakr.' So I said: 'May God forgive you, Abu Bakr. May God forgive you, Abu Bakr.' He said: Abu Bakr ؓ turned away weeping."],[1271,"I asked the Messenger of God ﷺ about fasting while traveling. He said: 'If you wish, fast; and if you wish, break the fast.'"],[1272,"The Prophet ﷺ passed by him while he had uncovered his thigh. He said: \"O Jarhad, cover your thigh, for it is part of the 'awrah.\""],[1273,"I said to al-Hasan b. Ali: \"What do you remember of the Prophet ﷺ?\" He said: \"I took a date from the dates of the sadaqah and threw it into my mouth. The Prophet ﷺ pulled it out with its saliva and threw it back among the dates. They said: 'O Messenger of God, a date from a boy!' He said: 'We, the family of Muhammad, do not find sadaqah lawful for us.'\""],[1274,"I said to al-Hasan b. Ali ؓ: \"What do you remember of the Prophet ﷺ?\" He said: \"He used to say: 'Leave what makes you doubt for what does not make you doubt. Indeed truthfulness is tranquility and lying is doubt.'\""],[1275,"I said to al-Hasan b. Ali: \"What do you remember of the Prophet ﷺ?\" He said: \"He would teach us this supplication: 'O God, guide me among those You have guided, and grant me well-being among those You have granted well-being, and take me as a friend among those You have taken as friends, and protect me from the evil of what You have decreed. Indeed You decree and none decrees against You. Indeed the one You befriend is never humiliated. Blessed are You, our Lord, and Exalted.'\""],[1276,"When the Prophet ﷺ intended to travel, he would say: \"I seek refuge in God from the hardship of travel, the gloom of return, change after constancy, the supplication of the oppressed, and an evil sight in wealth and family.\""],[1277,"He hunted a rabbit and slaughtered it with a sharp white stone. He came to the Prophet ﷺ and mentioned that to him, and he commanded him to eat it."],[1278,"\"When one of you fasts, let him break his fast with dates. If he does not find any, then with water, for it is purifying.\""],[1279,"A physician asked the Prophet ﷺ about a frog he wanted to put in a medicine. The Prophet ﷺ forbade him from killing it."],[1280,"\"No one hoards except a sinner.\""],[1281,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and heard him say: \"Look at Quraysh; hear their words but abandon their deeds.\""],[1282,"I saw Muhammad b. Maslama observing a woman from above a wall, looking at her. I said to him: \"Do you do this while you are one of the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ?\" He said: \"I heard the Prophet ﷺ say: 'When God, Mighty and Majestic, casts into the heart of one of you the proposal of a woman, there is no harm in looking at her.'\""],[1283,"I asked the Prophet ﷺ about wiping the pebble. He said to me: \"Once, or leave it.\""],[1284,"I had a wife called Suhayya, and I divorced her with an irrevocable divorce. I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said: O Messenger of God, I divorced Suhayya with an irrevocable divorce, and by God I only intended one [divorce]. He said: By God, did you only intend one? I said: By God, I only intended one. He said: By God, did you only intend one? I said: By God, I only intended one. So he returned her to me as [revocable with] one [divorce]."],[1285,"I heard the Prophet ﷺ urging [the people to equip] the army of hardship. Uthman b. Affan stood and said: One hundred camels with their saddles and packs in the path of God. Then he urged a second time, and Uthman stood and said: Two hundred camels with their saddles and packs in the path of God. Then he urged a third time, and Uthman stood and said: Three hundred camels with their saddles and packs in the path of God. He said: I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ descending from the pulpit saying: No blame upon Uthman for what he does after this—twice or thrice."],[1286,"I was walking wearing a cloak of mine that I was dragging, and a man said: Raise your garment, for it is more God-fearing and more durable. I looked, and behold it was the Prophet ﷺ. I said: O Messenger of God, it is only a striped cloak! He said: Do you not have in me an example to follow? Then I looked, and his lower garment reached to the middle of his shin."],[1287,"The Messenger of God ﷺ established brotherhood between two men. One of them was killed, and the other remained. Then he died, and they prayed over him. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: What did you say? They said: We supplicated God to forgive him, have mercy on him, and join him to his companion. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: Then where is his prayer after his prayer? And where is his deeds after his deeds? And I think he said: And where is his fasting after his fasting? By Him in whose hand is my soul, the [distance] between them is farther than what is between heaven and earth."],[1288,"Makhrafa and I brought cloth from Hajar, and I sold a pair of trousers to the Messenger of God ﷺ. There was a weigher weighing for a fee, and the Messenger of God ﷺ said: Weigh and give ample weight."],[1289,"I sold the Prophet ﷺ a trouser leg before the emigration for three dirhams, and he weighed for me and gave ample weight."],[1290,"The cooking pot fell on my hand and it got burned. My mother took me to the Messenger of God ﷺ, and he began to spit on it and say: Remove the affliction, O Lord of mankind. And I think he said: And heal, for You are the Healer."],[1291,"We were with the Prophet ﷺ, and some sheep were plundered. The Messenger of God ﷺ forbade that, so the cooking pots were overturned."],[1292,"This is the time of the departure of knowledge, or: This is the time of the severing of knowledge. Ibn Labid said: O Messenger of God, how [can that be] when the Book of God is among us, we teach it to our children and our children teach it to their children? The Prophet ﷺ said: May your mother be bereaved of you, O Ibn Labid! I certainly considered you the most intelligent man in Madinah. Have not the Jews and Christians been given the Torah and the Gospel, and yet they have not benefited from them in anything?"],[1293,"A believer is not bound by a vow concerning what he does not own. Cursing a believer is like killing him. Whoever kills himself with something will be punished with it on the Day of Resurrection. Whoever swears falsely by a religion other than Islam, he is as he has said."],[1294,"Any Muslim man who frees a Muslim man, it will be his ransom from the Fire, and he will be recompensed for every bone of his [the freed man's] bones with a bone of his own. Any Muslim man who frees two Muslim women, they will be his ransom from the Fire, and he will be recompensed for every two bones of their bones with a bone of his own. Any Muslim woman who frees a Muslim woman, she will be her ransom from the Fire, and she will be recompensed for every bone of her [the freed woman's] bones with a bone of her own."],[1295,"The Messenger of God ﷺ supplicated against Mudar. I came to him and said: O Messenger of God, God has given you victory, granted you, and answered you. Your people have perished, so supplicate God for them! He said: O God, give us a helping rain, wholesome and abundant, widespread and copious, swift and not delayed, beneficial and not harmful. He said: It was not until the next Friday or about that time that we were rained upon."],[1296,"\"O Messenger of God, I have come to you from a people among whom no camel strays and no shepherd is given provisions.\""],[1297,"The Prophet ﷺ saw a man praying alone in the row, so he ordered him to repeat the prayer."],[1298,"\"O people, repent to your Lord, for I repent to Him one hundred times a day.\""],[1299,"They were traveling with Salim b. 'Ubayd al-Ashja'i when a man sneezed and said, \"Peace be upon you!\" Salim said, \"And upon you and upon your mother!\" Then he traveled for a while, and said to the man, \"Perhaps you disliked what I said to you?\" He said, \"I wish you had not mentioned my mother either with good or with evil!\" He said, \"I only tell you what I witnessed from the Messenger of God ﷺ: A man sneezed in his presence and said, 'Peace be upon you!' The Messenger of God ﷺ said, 'And upon you and upon your mother. When one of you sneezes, let him say: Praise be to God, Lord of the worlds, or Praise be to God in every situation, and let his brother say to him: May God have mercy on you, and let him say: May God forgive me and you.'\""],[1300,"The Messenger of God ﷺ came out to us in the market while we were selling the loads, and we were called the brokers, so he named us with a name better than what we called ourselves."],[1301,"\"O assembly of merchants, indeed this market of yours is mixed with vain talk and oaths, so mix it with charity or with a portion of charity.\""],[1302,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with a group of riders from the tribe, and he led us in the dawn prayer. I kept looking at the one beside me, and I could hardly recognize him—meaning, due to the darkness before dawn."],[1303,"I came to the Messenger of God ﷺ with a group of riders from the tribe. When I wanted to return, I said, \"O Messenger of God, advise me!\" He said, \"Fear God, and when you are in a gathering and then leave them, if you hear them saying what pleases you, then go to it, and if you hear them saying what you dislike, then do not go to it.\""],[1306,"\"I prayed behind the Prophet ﷺ, and he recited 'When the sun is wrapped up.' When he reached this verse, 'And by the night when it darkens, and by the dawn when it breathes,' I said to myself: What is 'the night when it darkens and the dawn when it breathes'?\""],[1341,"\"Horses have goodness tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection.\" It was said, \"O Messenger of God, what is the goodness?\" He said, \"Reward and booty.\""],[1356,"His father instructed his sons at his death, saying: When I die, do not wail over me, for the Messenger of God ﷺ was not wailed over."],[1357,"\"When one of you fasts, let him break his fast with dates. If he does not find any, then with water, for it is purifying.\""],[1367,"The neighbor has more right to his adjacent property."],[1368,"The neighbor has more right to his adjacent property."],[1373,"Before the Hour there will be liars. He said a word I did not understand, so I said to my father: 'What did he say?' He said: 'Beware of them.'"],[1374,"\"Islam will continue to be mighty until twelve caliphs,\" then he said a word I did not understand. I said to my father: \"What did the Messenger of God ﷺ say?\" He said: \"All of them will be from Quraysh.\""],[1427,"\"Whoever equips a warrior in the path of God, Mighty and Majestic, has indeed fought, and whoever looks after his family with good has indeed fought.\""],[1428,"\"Whoever performs wudu' well, then prays two rak'ahs without being heedless in them, will be forgiven.\""],[1430,"Two disputants came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, we adjure you by God to judge between us according to the Book of God, Mighty and Majestic!\" His opponent stood up—and he was more knowledgeable than him—and said, \"Yes, O Messenger of God, judge between us according to the Book of God and permit me to speak!\" He permitted him, and he said, \"O Messenger of God, my son was a servant for this man, and he committed adultery with his wife. I was told that my son was subject to stoning, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a servant. Then I asked the people of knowledge, and they told me that my son is subject to a hundred lashes and exile for a year, and that this man's wife is subject to stoning!\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"By Him in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, I will surely judge between you according to the Book of God: the hundred sheep and the servant are returned to you, and upon your son is a hundred lashes and exile for a year. And go, O Unays, to this man's wife; if she confesses, then stone her.\" He went to her and asked her, and she confessed, so he stoned her."],[1431,"If the slave woman of one of you commits adultery, let him flog her; if she returns, let him flog her; if she returns, let him flog her; and if she returns a fourth time, let him sell her even for a rope of hair."],[1432,"\"We prayed Maghrib with the Messenger of God ﷺ, then we went to the market, and if we shot arrows, we could see where they fell.\""],[1448,"Whoever swears an oath and then sees something better than it, let him do what is better and let him expiate his oath."],[1454,"I saw Wathilah b. al-Asqaʿ — and he was a Companion — praying in the mosque of Damascus wearing two sandals. He spat beneath his left foot, then rubbed it into the ground. When he finished praying, I said: 'You do this while you are among the Companions of the Messenger of God ﷺ?' He said: 'Thus I saw the Messenger of God ﷺ do.'"],[1462,"Uthman b. 'Affan ؓ was brought water for wudu for the 'Asr prayer while he was at al-Maqa'id. Uthman said: I have decided to tell you a hadith that I did not think I would tell you. Al-Hakam b. Abi al-'As said: O Commander of the Faithful, it is only good that we should follow, or evil that we should avoid. He said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ was brought water for wudu while he was at al-Maqa'id. He said: Whoever performs wudu and perfects his wudu, then prays and completes its bowing and prostration, will have expiated for him what is between it and the next prayer as long as he does not commit a mortal sin, meaning as long as he does not commit a major sin."],[1465,"\"I saw the Prophet ﷺ, and I saw this white spot from him,\" and he pointed to the tuft of hair under his lower lip. It was said, \"What were you doing at that time, O Abu Juhaifah?\" He said, \"I was trimming arrows and fletching them.\""],[1485,"\"The pen is lifted from three: from the afflicted—or he said: the insane—until he recovers, from the child until he reaches puberty or understands, and from the sleeper until he wakes.\""],[1495,"I entered upon the Messenger of Allah ﷺ while he was suffering from a fever, so I touched him and said: O Messenger of Allah, you are suffering from a severe fever. He said: Yes, I suffer a fever as severe as two men among you. I said: That is because you have a double reward? He said: Yes, and by the One in whose hand is my soul, no Muslim is afflicted with any harm—illness or anything else—except that Allah, Mighty and Majestic, sheds his sins from him as a tree sheds its leaves."],[1539,"A necklace of ‘A’ishah made of Yemeni agate was lost during one of the journeys of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and ‘A’ishah was with the Messenger of God ﷺ on that journey. ‘A’ishah searched for her necklace until the night was well advanced. Abu Bakr came and became angry with her and said: 'You have detained the people in a place where there is no water.' He said: Then the verse of tayammum was revealed. Abu Bakr came and said: 'You, by God, my little daughter, as far as I know, are blessed!' ‘Ubayd Allah said: ‘Ammar used to relate that the people began that day wiping the ground with their palms and wiping their faces with them, then they would return and strike another blow and wipe their hands up to the shoulders and armpits, then they prayed."],[1554,"\"The Prophet ﷺ commanded me to raid Ubna in the morning and to burn.\""],[1579,"A necklace of ‘A’ishah made of Yemeni agate was lost during one of the journeys of the Messenger of God ﷺ, and ‘A’ishah was with the Messenger of God ﷺ on that journey. ‘A’ishah searched for her necklace until the night was well advanced. Abu Bakr came and became angry with her and said: 'You have detained the people in a place where there is no water.' He said: Then the verse of tayammum was revealed. Abu Bakr came and said: 'You, by God, my little daughter, as far as I know, are blessed!' ‘Ubayd Allah said: ‘Ammar used to relate that the people began that day wiping the ground with their palms and wiping their faces with them, then they would return and strike another blow and wipe their hands up to the shoulders and armpits, then they prayed."],[1584,"\"Whoever equips a warrior in the path of God, Mighty and Majestic, has indeed fought, and whoever looks after his family with good has indeed fought.\""],[1662,"When he pronounced the taslim, he would say: O Allah, You are Peace, and from You is peace. Blessed are You, O Possessor of Majesty and Honor."],[1794,"\"As for this one, he has told me the truth. Stand until God decides your case.\" He said: So I stood, and some men of my people from Banu Salimah came back to me and said: \"By God, we do not know that you committed any sin in Islam before this. It would have been enough for your sin that the Messenger of God ﷺ ask forgiveness for you. Why did you not excuse yourself to the Messenger of God as those who stayed behind excused themselves to him?\" He said: By God, they kept reproaching me until I almost started to disbelieve myself. He said: So I said: \"Did anyone experience this along with me?\" He said: \"Two men experienced it with you; they were told what you were told.\" I said: \"Who are they?\" They said: \"Hilal b. Umayyah al-Waqifi and Murarah b. al-Rabi' al-'Amiri.\" They mentioned two righteous men who had been present at Badr, and in them I had an example. He said: And the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade speaking to us, the three men, among those who stayed behind from him. He said: So the people avoided us and did not speak to us. By God, I felt estranged from myself, and the earth seemed estranged to me in my own mind; it was not the earth I used to know. As for my two companions, they submitted and sat in their houses. As for me, I was the youngest and most vigorous of the people, so I would attend the prayer with the Muslims and walk in the markets, but no one would speak to me. I would come to the Messenger of God ﷺ and pray with him, then greet him and say to myself: \"Did he move his lips in reply to me?\" I would steal glances at him. When I turned to my prayer, he would turn toward me, but when I turned toward him, he would turn away from me. When the harshness of the Muslims toward us had gone on for a long time, I went to Abu Qatadah, who was my cousin and the dearest of people to me, and I spoke to him. By God, he did not speak to me. I said: \"O Abu Qatadah, I adjure you by God: do you know that I love God and His Messenger?\" He said: \"God and His Messenger know best.\" He said: So my eyes overflowed, and I climbed over the wall and went on. One day while I was in the market, a Nabatean from the Nabateans of Syria came to me with a letter from the king of Ghassan, and he was saying: \"Who will direct me to Ka'b b. Malik?\" The people began pointing to me. I took the letter, for I could read, and there it was from the king of Ghassan, and in it: \"To proceed: It has reached us that your companion has banished you. God would not place you in a house of humiliation or loss, so join us and we will console you!\" He said: I said: \"This too is part of the evil.\" I took the letter and headed to the oven with it and kindled it. When forty nights had passed since the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade speaking to us, the messenger of the Messenger of God ﷺ came to me and said: \"The Messenger of God commands you to keep away from your wife.\" I said: \"Should I divorce her, or what should I do with her?\" He said: \"Do not go near her.\" So I said to my wife: \"O woman, go to your family until God decides in this matter.\" And he sent the same to my two companions. He said: Then the wife of Hilal b. Umayyah came and said: \"O Messenger of God, Hilal is a helpless man and has no servant. Would you dislike me serving him?\" He said: \"No, but he must not come near you.\" She said: \"O Messenger of God, by God, he has made no movement toward anything of that since his affair began; he only weeps.\" Then some of my family said to me: \"Why don't you ask the Messenger of God permission regarding your wife, since he gave permission to the wife of Hilal?\" I said: \"By God, I will not do it. I am a young man and I do not know what the Messenger of God will say.\" He said: While I was in that state, on the morning of the fiftieth night since the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade speaking to us, I prayed the dawn prayer on the roof of a house of ours, then I sat in the state that God mentioned: \"the earth became straitened for them despite its vastness, and their own selves became straitened for them, and they thought there was no refuge from God except to Him,\" when I heard the voice of a caller raised on Mount Sal', and a man galloped a horse to me. The voice reached me faster than the horse: \"Rejoice, O Ka'b b. Malik!\" I fell down in prostration, and I knew that relief had come. The one whose voice I had heard came, and I took off two garments that were on me—by God, I owned no others—and gave them to him as a reward for good news. Then I borrowed two garments and put them on, and went to the Prophet ﷺ. Ka'b said: Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who was kind to me in my affair, told me that the Messenger of God ﷺ was with her that night. When a third of the night remained, our repentance descended upon him, and he said to her: \"O Umm Salamah, repentance has been accepted for Ka'b b. Malik and his two companions.\" She said: I said: \"O Messenger of God, shall I not send to him and give him the good news?\" He said: \"Then the people would crowd you and prevent you from sleeping the rest of the night.\" And the Messenger of God ﷺ announced God's acceptance of our repentance after he had prayed the dawn prayer. He said: So bearers of good news went to my two companions, and bearers of good news went to me. Ka'b said: I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ with the Muhajirun and Ansar around him, and his face was shining as if it were a piece of the moon. Whenever he was pleased with something, his face would shine. Talhah b. 'Ubayd Allah ؓ stood up for me, hurrying until he congratulated me and shook my hand. By God, no man among the Muhajirun stood up other than him, so Ka'b never forgot it for Talhah. He said: The Muslims began congratulating me on God's acceptance of my repentance, saying: \"May God's acceptance of repentance bring you joy, may God's acceptance of repentance bring you joy,\" until I reached the Messenger of God ﷺ. When he saw me, he said: \"Come, O Ka'b, and rejoice in the best day that has come upon you since the day your mother gave birth to you.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, is it from you or from God?\" He said: \"Rather, it is from God.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, part of my repentance is that I divest myself of all my wealth as charity to God and His Messenger.\" He said: \"O Ka'b, keep some of your wealth, for it is better for you.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, I will keep my share at Khaybar.\" And I said: \"O Messenger of God, God, Mighty and Majestic, saved me only by truthfulness, and part of my repentance is that I will never speak anything but truth as long as I live.\" Ka'b said: By God, I do not know anyone whom God has tested in truthful speech as He has tested me. By God, I have never deliberately told a lie since I said that to the Messenger of God ﷺ until this day of mine, and I hope God will protect me in what remains. He said: Then God, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: \"God has turned in mercy to the Prophet, and to the Muhajirun and the Ansar\"—the two verses together."],[1796,"\"As for this one, he has told me the truth. Stand until God decides your case.\" He said: So I stood, and some men of my people from Banu Salimah came back to me and said: \"By God, we do not know that you committed any sin in Islam before this. It would have been enough for your sin that the Messenger of God ﷺ ask forgiveness for you. Why did you not excuse yourself to the Messenger of God as those who stayed behind excused themselves to him?\" He said: By God, they kept reproaching me until I almost started to disbelieve myself. He said: So I said: \"Did anyone experience this along with me?\" He said: \"Two men experienced it with you; they were told what you were told.\" I said: \"Who are they?\" They said: \"Hilal b. Umayyah al-Waqifi and Murarah b. al-Rabi' al-'Amiri.\" They mentioned two righteous men who had been present at Badr, and in them I had an example. He said: And the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade speaking to us, the three men, among those who stayed behind from him. He said: So the people avoided us and did not speak to us. By God, I felt estranged from myself, and the earth seemed estranged to me in my own mind; it was not the earth I used to know. As for my two companions, they submitted and sat in their houses. As for me, I was the youngest and most vigorous of the people, so I would attend the prayer with the Muslims and walk in the markets, but no one would speak to me. I would come to the Messenger of God ﷺ and pray with him, then greet him and say to myself: \"Did he move his lips in reply to me?\" I would steal glances at him. When I turned to my prayer, he would turn toward me, but when I turned toward him, he would turn away from me. When the harshness of the Muslims toward us had gone on for a long time, I went to Abu Qatadah, who was my cousin and the dearest of people to me, and I spoke to him. By God, he did not speak to me. I said: \"O Abu Qatadah, I adjure you by God: do you know that I love God and His Messenger?\" He said: \"God and His Messenger know best.\" He said: So my eyes overflowed, and I climbed over the wall and went on. One day while I was in the market, a Nabatean from the Nabateans of Syria came to me with a letter from the king of Ghassan, and he was saying: \"Who will direct me to Ka'b b. Malik?\" The people began pointing to me. I took the letter, for I could read, and there it was from the king of Ghassan, and in it: \"To proceed: It has reached us that your companion has banished you. God would not place you in a house of humiliation or loss, so join us and we will console you!\" He said: I said: \"This too is part of the evil.\" I took the letter and headed to the oven with it and kindled it. When forty nights had passed since the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade speaking to us, the messenger of the Messenger of God ﷺ came to me and said: \"The Messenger of God commands you to keep away from your wife.\" I said: \"Should I divorce her, or what should I do with her?\" He said: \"Do not go near her.\" So I said to my wife: \"O woman, go to your family until God decides in this matter.\" And he sent the same to my two companions. He said: Then the wife of Hilal b. Umayyah came and said: \"O Messenger of God, Hilal is a helpless man and has no servant. Would you dislike me serving him?\" He said: \"No, but he must not come near you.\" She said: \"O Messenger of God, by God, he has made no movement toward anything of that since his affair began; he only weeps.\" Then some of my family said to me: \"Why don't you ask the Messenger of God permission regarding your wife, since he gave permission to the wife of Hilal?\" I said: \"By God, I will not do it. I am a young man and I do not know what the Messenger of God will say.\" He said: While I was in that state, on the morning of the fiftieth night since the Messenger of God ﷺ forbade speaking to us, I prayed the dawn prayer on the roof of a house of ours, then I sat in the state that God mentioned: \"the earth became straitened for them despite its vastness, and their own selves became straitened for them, and they thought there was no refuge from God except to Him,\" when I heard the voice of a caller raised on Mount Sal', and a man galloped a horse to me. The voice reached me faster than the horse: \"Rejoice, O Ka'b b. Malik!\" I fell down in prostration, and I knew that relief had come. The one whose voice I had heard came, and I took off two garments that were on me—by God, I owned no others—and gave them to him as a reward for good news. Then I borrowed two garments and put them on, and went to the Prophet ﷺ. Ka'b said: Umm Salamah, the wife of the Prophet ﷺ, who was kind to me in my affair, told me that the Messenger of God ﷺ was with her that night. When a third of the night remained, our repentance descended upon him, and he said to her: \"O Umm Salamah, repentance has been accepted for Ka'b b. Malik and his two companions.\" She said: I said: \"O Messenger of God, shall I not send to him and give him the good news?\" He said: \"Then the people would crowd you and prevent you from sleeping the rest of the night.\" And the Messenger of God ﷺ announced God's acceptance of our repentance after he had prayed the dawn prayer. He said: So bearers of good news went to my two companions, and bearers of good news went to me. Ka'b said: I went to the Messenger of God ﷺ with the Muhajirun and Ansar around him, and his face was shining as if it were a piece of the moon. Whenever he was pleased with something, his face would shine. Talhah b. 'Ubayd Allah ؓ stood up for me, hurrying until he congratulated me and shook my hand. By God, no man among the Muhajirun stood up other than him, so Ka'b never forgot it for Talhah. He said: The Muslims began congratulating me on God's acceptance of my repentance, saying: \"May God's acceptance of repentance bring you joy, may God's acceptance of repentance bring you joy,\" until I reached the Messenger of God ﷺ. When he saw me, he said: \"Come, O Ka'b, and rejoice in the best day that has come upon you since the day your mother gave birth to you.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, is it from you or from God?\" He said: \"Rather, it is from God.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, part of my repentance is that I divest myself of all my wealth as charity to God and His Messenger.\" He said: \"O Ka'b, keep some of your wealth, for it is better for you.\" I said: \"O Messenger of God, I will keep my share at Khaybar.\" And I said: \"O Messenger of God, God, Mighty and Majestic, saved me only by truthfulness, and part of my repentance is that I will never speak anything but truth as long as I live.\" Ka'b said: By God, I do not know anyone whom God has tested in truthful speech as He has tested me. By God, I have never deliberately told a lie since I said that to the Messenger of God ﷺ until this day of mine, and I hope God will protect me in what remains. He said: Then God, Mighty and Majestic, sent down: \"God has turned in mercy to the Prophet, and to the Muhajirun and the Ansar\"—the two verses together."],[1847,"Ibn Mas'ud took his hand, and Ibn Mas'ud mentioned that the Prophet ﷺ took his hand and taught him the tashahhud: Greetings are for God, and prayers and good things. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of God and His blessings. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of God. I bear witness that there is no god but God, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. When you have said that, your prayer is complete; if you wish, stand, and if you wish, remain seated."],[1880,"\"We prayed Maghrib with the Messenger of God ﷺ, then we went to the market, and if we shot arrows, we could see where they fell.\""],[1951,"\"Whoever plays with dice has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger.\""],[1955,"On the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the Ka'bah and locked the door behind him. Al-Fadl b. Abbas, Uthman b. Talhah, Usamah b. Zayd, and Bilal entered with him. When they came out, I raced the people and beat them. I said to Bilal: “Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray?” He said: “Between the two front pillars, opposite the entrance.”"],[1960,"On the day of the conquest of Makkah, the Messenger of Allah ﷺ entered the Ka'bah and locked the door behind him. Al-Fadl b. Abbas, Uthman b. Talhah, Usamah b. Zayd, and Bilal entered with him. When they came out, I raced the people and beat them. I said to Bilal: “Where did the Messenger of Allah ﷺ pray?” He said: “Between the two front pillars, opposite the entrance.”"],[1965,"Ghifar, may God forgive them, and Aslam, may God grant them peace."],[1974,"\"I agreed with my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, in four matters. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, if only you prayed behind the Maqam,' and this verse was revealed: 'And take the Maqam of Ibrahim as a place of prayer.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, if only you ordered your wives to veil, for both the righteous and the wicked enter upon you.' So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: 'And when you ask them for something, ask them from behind a screen.' And this verse was revealed: 'We certainly created man from an extract of clay' until the end of the verse. When it was revealed, I said: 'Blessed is Allah, the best of creators.' Then it was revealed: 'So blessed is Allah, the best of creators.' And I entered upon the wives of the Prophet ﷺ and said to them: 'Either you desist, or Allah will replace you with better wives than you.' So this verse was revealed: 'Perhaps his Lord, if he divorces you...'\""],[2000,"The Night of Decree is the night of the twenty-seventh."],[2002,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ began the prayer, he would say the takbir, then say: \"I have turned my face to Him who created the heavens and the earth, as a hanif, and I am not of the polytheists. Indeed, my prayer, my sacrifice, my living, and my dying are for God, Lord of the worlds. No partner has He. With this I have been commanded, and I am the first of those who submit. O God, You are the King, there is no god but You. You are my Lord and I am Your servant. I have wronged myself and confessed my sin, so forgive me all my sins. None forgives sins but You. Guide me to the best of character; none guides to its best but You. Turn away from me its evil; none turns away its evil but You. Here I am at Your service, all good is in Your hands, and evil is not attributed to You. I am through You and to You. Blessed and exalted are You. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance.\" When he bowed, he said: \"O God, to You I have bowed, in You I have believed, and to You I have submitted. My hearing, my sight, my bones, my marrow, and my nerves humble themselves to You.\" When he raised his head, he said: \"God hears the one who praises Him. O God, our Lord, to You is praise, filling the heavens, filling the earth, filling what is between them, and filling whatever You will after that.\" When he prostrated, he said: \"O God, to You I have prostrated, in You I have believed, and to You I have submitted. My face has prostrated to the One who created it, shaped it, and perfected its form, and split its hearing and sight. Blessed is God, the best of creators.\" When he said the taslim, he said: \"O God, forgive me what I have sent ahead and what I have delayed, what I have made public and what I have concealed, and what You know better than I. You are the One who brings forward and the One who delays; there is no god but You.\""],[2009,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined—meaning at Muzdalifah—Maghrib and 'Isha'.\""],[2047,"\"Seek the Night of Decree in the last ten nights.\""],[2054,"I asked Ibn 'Umar about a man who divorced his wife while she was menstruating. He said: \"Do you know Ibn 'Umar? He divorced his wife while she was menstruating, so 'Umar mentioned that to the Prophet ﷺ, and he said: 'He should take her back.'\""],[2084,"I heard from a man a hadith that pleased me, so I said: write it down. He brought it to me written down, inscribed. He said: 'Ali and al-'Abbas entered upon 'Umar, and with him were 'Abd al-Rahman b. 'Awf, al-Zubayr b. al-'Awwam, and Sa'd b. Abi Waqqas. He said: I adjure you by God—did you not hear, or did you not know, that the Messenger of God ﷺ said: \"All the wealth of the Prophet is charity except what he feeds his family and clothes them with. We are not inherited from.\"? They said: Yes indeed."],[2135,"The likeness of my community is that of rain; it is not known whether its beginning is better or its end."],[2156,"\"I agreed with my Lord, Mighty and Majestic, in four matters. I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, if only you prayed behind the Maqam,' and this verse was revealed: 'And take the Maqam of Ibrahim as a place of prayer.' I said: 'O Messenger of Allah, if only you ordered your wives to veil, for both the righteous and the wicked enter upon you.' So Allah, Mighty and Majestic, revealed: 'And when you ask them for something, ask them from behind a screen.' And this verse was revealed: 'We certainly created man from an extract of clay' until the end of the verse. When it was revealed, I said: 'Blessed is Allah, the best of creators.' Then it was revealed: 'So blessed is Allah, the best of creators.' And I entered upon the wives of the Prophet ﷺ and said to them: 'Either you desist, or Allah will replace you with better wives than you.' So this verse was revealed: 'Perhaps his Lord, if he divorces you...'\""],[2167,"He was on an expedition of his, and when he finished fighting, he said: 'Do you miss anyone?' They said: By God, we miss so-and-so and so-and-so and so-and-so. The Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'Look, do you miss anyone?' They said: We miss so-and-so and so-and-so. He said: But I miss Julaybib, so search for him. They found him beside seven [men] whom he had killed, and then they killed him. The Prophet ﷺ was informed and he came to him and said: 'He killed seven, then they killed him! This one is from me and I am from him. He killed seven, then they killed him! This one is from me and I am from him.' He said it twice or three times. Then he gestured with his arms like this — and spread them out — and he was placed on the arms of the Prophet ﷺ until a grave was dug for him. He had no bier except the arms of the Prophet ﷺ until he was buried. He (the narrator) said: He did not mention washing."],[2197,"\"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[2206,"\"It is not lawful for a Muslim to abandon his brother for more than three days; they meet and this one turns away and this one turns away, and the best of them is the one who initiates the greeting.\""],[2229,"The best dinar is a dinar a man spends on his dependents, a dinar he spends on his riding beast in the way of God, and a dinar he spends on his companions in the way of God."],[2257,"\"Silver for silver, gold for gold, dates for dates, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, salt for salt, equal for equal,\" or he said: \"weight for weight.\" Thus al-Rabī' narrated it."],[2277,"\"God, Mighty and Majestic, revealed to Yahya b. Zakariyya five words to act upon and to command the Children of Israel to act upon. It was as if he was slow about them, so God, Mighty and Majestic, revealed to 'Isa: Either you convey them or they will be conveyed. 'Isa came to him and said: God has commanded you with five words to act upon and to command the Children of Israel to act upon. Either you inform them or I inform them. He said: O Spirit of God, do not do that; I fear that if you precede me with them, the earth may swallow me or I may be punished. He said: So he gathered the Children of Israel in the Holy House until the mosque was full and they sat on the balconies. Then he addressed them saying: God, Mighty and Majestic, has revealed to me five words and commanded the Children of Israel to act upon them. The first of them: Do not associate anything with God, for the likeness of one who associates partners with God is like a man who bought a slave with his pure wealth of gold or silver, then lodged him in a house and said: Work and bring to me. But the slave began bringing to someone other than his master. Which of you would be pleased for his slave to be like that? God, Mighty and Majestic, created you and provided for you, so do not associate anything with Him. When you stand for prayer, do not turn aside, for God, Mighty and Majestic, turns His face toward the face of His servant as long as he does not turn aside. He commanded you to fast, and the likeness of that is like a man in a group with a pouch of musk; all of them love to find its scent. The breath of the fasting person is sweeter to God than the scent of musk. He commanded you to give charity, and the likeness of that is like a man whom the enemy captured and bound him to his neck or brought him near to strike his neck. He began saying to them: Would you let me ransom myself from you? He began giving a little and a lot until he ransomed himself. He commanded you to remember God frequently, and the likeness of that is like a man whom the enemy pursued swiftly in his tracks until he reached a fortified fortress and secured himself in it. Likewise, the servant does not escape from Satan except by remembrance of God.\""],[2278,"Al-Ashʿarī sought permission to enter upon ʿUmar three times, but he did not grant him permission, so he turned back. ʿUmar sent to him, \"What made you go back?\" He said, \"I sought permission three times and was not granted permission, and I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ say, 'If one seeking permission asks three times and is not granted permission, let him go back.'\" ʿUmar said, \"You must bring me someone who knows this, or I will do such-and-such to you.\" Abū Saʿīd said, \"Al-Ashʿarī came to me trembling, his face turned yellow. He stood at a circle of the Prophet's ﷺ companions and said, 'I adjure by God, any man who knows anything about this must stand up for it, for I fear this man for myself.' I said, 'I am with you.' Another said, 'And I am with you.' So he was relieved.\""],[2282,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ dug the trench, the people were carrying one brick at a time, while ʿAmmār was recovering from an illness he had. He began carrying two bricks at a time. Abū Saʿīd said: My companions told me that the Messenger of God ﷺ was brushing the dust from his head and saying: “Woe to you, O son of Sumayyah! The transgressing party will kill you.”"],[2284,"\"Silver for silver, gold for gold, dates for dates, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, salt for salt, equal for equal,\" or he said: \"weight for weight.\" Thus al-Rabī' narrated it."],[2319,"When this verse was revealed, \"When the help of God comes, and the victory,\" the Messenger of God ﷺ recited it to its end, then said, \"I and my companions are one side, and the people are another side. There is no emigration after the victory.\" Abu Said said: I narrated this hadith to Marwan b. al-Hakam—who was governor over Madinah—and he said, \"You have lied,\" while Zayd b. Thabit and Zayd b. Arqam were with him. I said, \"If these two wished, they would tell you, but this one fears that you would remove him from the charity, and this one fears that you would remove him from the leadership of his people.\" He raised the whip against me, and when they saw that, they said, \"He has spoken the truth.\""],[2343,"I asked Ibn 'Umar ؓ about nabidh, and he narrated from 'Umar that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ forbade jars, gourds, and pitch-covered vessels."],[2369,"Fasting three days of the month is equivalent to fasting for a lifetime and its breaking."],[2370,"He prayed with the Prophet ﷺ—Abu Dawud said: meaning the night prayer. When he said the takbir, he said: God is the greatest, possessor of dominion, might, pride, and greatness. Then he recited al-Baqarah. Then he bowed, and his bowing was like his standing. In his bowing he kept saying: 'Glory be to my Lord, the Mighty, glory be to my Lord, the Mighty.' Then he raised his head from bowing and stood like his bowing, and he said: 'Praise belongs to my Lord.' Then he prostrated, and his prostration was like his standing. In his prostration he would say: 'Glory be to my Lord, the Most High.' Then he raised his head from prostration, and between the two prostrations he would say: 'Lord, forgive me; Lord, forgive me,' and he sat for as long as his prostration. Hudhayfah said: He prayed four rak'ahs, reciting in them al-Baqarah, Al Imran, al-Nisa, and al-Ma'idah or al-An'am."],[2394,"Fasting three days of the month is equivalent to fasting for a lifetime and its breaking."],[2409,"One who is disobedient to parents will not enter Paradise, nor one who reminds others of his favors, nor one who denies the divine decree."],[2499,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ began the prayer, he would say the takbir, then say: \"I have turned my face to Him who created the heavens and the earth, as a hanif, and I am not of the polytheists. Indeed, my prayer, my sacrifice, my living, and my dying are for God, Lord of the worlds. No partner has He. With this I have been commanded, and I am the first of those who submit. O God, You are the King, there is no god but You. You are my Lord and I am Your servant. I have wronged myself and confessed my sin, so forgive me all my sins. None forgives sins but You. Guide me to the best of character; none guides to its best but You. Turn away from me its evil; none turns away its evil but You. Here I am at Your service, all good is in Your hands, and evil is not attributed to You. I am through You and to You. Blessed and exalted are You. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance.\" When he bowed, he said: \"O God, to You I have bowed, in You I have believed, and to You I have submitted. My hearing, my sight, my bones, my marrow, and my nerves humble themselves to You.\" When he raised his head, he said: \"God hears the one who praises Him. O God, our Lord, to You is praise, filling the heavens, filling the earth, filling what is between them, and filling whatever You will after that.\" When he prostrated, he said: \"O God, to You I have prostrated, in You I have believed, and to You I have submitted. My face has prostrated to the One who created it, shaped it, and perfected its form, and split its hearing and sight. Blessed is God, the best of creators.\" When he said the taslim, he said: \"O God, forgive me what I have sent ahead and what I have delayed, what I have made public and what I have concealed, and what You know better than I. You are the One who brings forward and the One who delays; there is no god but You.\""],[2516,"When the Messenger of God ﷺ began the prayer, he would say the takbir, then say: \"I have turned my face to Him who created the heavens and the earth, as a hanif, and I am not of the polytheists. Indeed, my prayer, my sacrifice, my living, and my dying are for God, Lord of the worlds. No partner has He. With this I have been commanded, and I am the first of those who submit. O God, You are the King, there is no god but You. You are my Lord and I am Your servant. I have wronged myself and confessed my sin, so forgive me all my sins. None forgives sins but You. Guide me to the best of character; none guides to its best but You. Turn away from me its evil; none turns away its evil but You. Here I am at Your service, all good is in Your hands, and evil is not attributed to You. I am through You and to You. Blessed and exalted are You. I seek Your forgiveness and turn to You in repentance.\" When he bowed, he said: \"O God, to You I have bowed, in You I have believed, and to You I have submitted. My hearing, my sight, my bones, my marrow, and my nerves humble themselves to You.\" When he raised his head, he said: \"God hears the one who praises Him. O God, our Lord, to You is praise, filling the heavens, filling the earth, filling what is between them, and filling whatever You will after that.\" When he prostrated, he said: \"O God, to You I have prostrated, in You I have believed, and to You I have submitted. My face has prostrated to the One who created it, shaped it, and perfected its form, and split its hearing and sight. Blessed is God, the best of creators.\" When he said the taslim, he said: \"O God, forgive me what I have sent ahead and what I have delayed, what I have made public and what I have concealed, and what You know better than I. You are the One who brings forward and the One who delays; there is no god but You.\""],[2543,"\"Whoever deliberately lies about me, let him take his seat in the Fire.\""],[2559,"\"Horses have goodness tied to their forelocks until the Day of Resurrection.\" It was said, \"O Messenger of God, what is the goodness?\" He said, \"Reward and booty.\""],[2605,"Ghifar, may God forgive them, and Aslam, may God grant them peace."],[2635,"If the slave woman of one of you commits adultery, let him flog her; if she returns, let him flog her; if she returns, let him flog her; and if she returns a fourth time, let him sell her even for a rope of hair."],[2636,"Two disputants came to the Messenger of God ﷺ and said, \"O Messenger of God, we adjure you by God to judge between us according to the Book of God, Mighty and Majestic!\" His opponent stood up—and he was more knowledgeable than him—and said, \"Yes, O Messenger of God, judge between us according to the Book of God and permit me to speak!\" He permitted him, and he said, \"O Messenger of God, my son was a servant for this man, and he committed adultery with his wife. I was told that my son was subject to stoning, so I ransomed him with a hundred sheep and a servant. Then I asked the people of knowledge, and they told me that my son is subject to a hundred lashes and exile for a year, and that this man's wife is subject to stoning!\" The Messenger of God ﷺ said, \"By Him in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, I will surely judge between you according to the Book of God: the hundred sheep and the servant are returned to you, and upon your son is a hundred lashes and exile for a year. And go, O Unays, to this man's wife; if she confesses, then stone her.\" He went to her and asked her, and she confessed, so he stoned her."],[2705,"O Messenger of Allah, command me with something I can say in the morning and the evening. He said: 'Say: O Allah, Knower of the unseen and the seen, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Lord and Owner of everything, I bear witness that there is no god but You. I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul and from the evil of Satan and his trap. Say it in the morning, in the evening, and when you go to bed.'"],[2739,"\"Whoever builds a mosque for Allah, Mighty and Majestic, even like a sandgrouse's nest, Allah builds for him a house in Paradise.\""],[2751,"\"The Messenger of Allah ﷺ combined in an expedition he undertook—and that was in the expedition of Tabuk—between Zuhr and 'Asr, and between Maghrib and 'Isha'.\" He said: I said: What did he intend by that? He said: He intended not to cause hardship for his community."],[2764,"He forbade al-ḥaql (sharecropping for a fixed share of the produce)."],[2785,"A woman from Khath'am came to the Prophet ﷺ in the year of the Farewell Hajj and said: 'O Messenger of God, God's obligation upon His servants regarding the Hajj has overtaken my father, an old man who cannot keep himself steady on the mount. May I perform the Hajj on his behalf?' He said: 'Yes.'"],[2811,"I used to wish to meet a man from the companions of the Prophet ﷺ to ask him about the Khawarij. I met Abu Barzah al-Aslami on a day of Eid among people from his companions, and I said to him: Have you heard the Messenger of God ﷺ speak about the Khawarij? Abu Barzah said: I heard the Messenger of God ﷺ with my ears and saw him with my eyes. Some wealth was brought to the Messenger of God ﷺ and he divided it. A black man with trimmed hair, wearing two white garments, came and he gave to those on his right and those on his left but gave him nothing. He came from behind him and said: By God, O Muhammad, you have not been just! The Messenger of God ﷺ said: By God, you will not find anyone after me more just to you than me. He said it three times. Then the Messenger of God ﷺ said: 'A people will emerge in the last days as if this man is from them. They recite the Quran but it does not go beyond their collarbones. They pass through Islam as an arrow passes through the game. Their mark is shaving. They will emerge until the last of them comes out with the Messiah. So when you meet them, kill them. They are the worst of creation and creatures.'"],[2843,"\"Do not extol me as the Christians extolled 'Isa b. Maryam. I am only a servant, so say: 'The servant of Allah and His Messenger.'\""],[2864,"\"I saw the whiteness of the armpit of the Messenger of God ﷺ while he was prostrating.\""],[2883,"I looked into Paradise and saw that most of its people are the poor, and I looked into the Fire and saw that most of its people are women."]]);
